hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"7201","7195 - And with the same chain: from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined Zuhr and Asr, and Maghrib and Isha, in Madinah, while resident, without fear or travel; he only intended thereby ease for his ummah. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awwam except Abdillah ibn Khirash."
"7202","7196 - Muhammad ibn Mahmawayh al-Jawhari narrated to us, Mamar ibn Sahl narrated to us, Ubaydillah ibn Tamam narrated to us, from Said al-Jurayri, from Abdillah ibn Buraydah, from Aishah, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to his bed, he would say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from evil as a constant companion, and from hunger as a bedfellow. No one narrated this hadith from al-Jurayri except Ubaydillah ibn Tamam; Mamar ibn Sahl alone transmitted it, and it is not narrated from Aishah except with this chain."
"7203","7197 - Muhammad ibn Mahmawayh al-Jawhari narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Sinan al-Hanzali narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Yahya al-Darir narrated to us, Abbad ibn Rashid informed me, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Does not the one who raises his head before the imam, and lowers his head, fear that Allah will transform his head into the head of a donkey? No one narrated this hadith from Abbad ibn Rashid except al-Qasim ibn Yahya; al-Hasan ibn Sinan alone transmitted it."
"7204","7198 - Muhammad ibn Mahmawayh al-Jawhari narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Sinan al-Hanzali narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, from Sharik ibn Abdillah, from Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from his father who said: I saw Ali ibn Abi Talib displaying a sword of his in the courtyard of Kufah, saying: Who will buy this sword of mine from me? By Allah, I have cleared with it more than one distress from the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and if I had the price of a waist-wrapper, I would not sell it. No one narrated this hadith from Ali ibn al-Aqmar except Sharik, and none narrated it from Sharik except Sulayman ibn al-Hakam; al-Hasan ibn Sinan alone transmitted it."
"7205","7199 - Muhammad ibn Mahmawayh al-Jawhari narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Sinan al-Hanzali narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, Sharik ibn Abdillah al-Nakhai informed me, from Abdillah ibn Ulathah, from his father who said: I heard al-Numan ibn Bashir saying upon the pulpit in Kufah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to stand at night until his feet cracked, so it was said to him: O Messenger of Allah, has not Allah forgiven you what preceded of your sin and what followed? He said: Shall I not be a grateful servant. No one narrated this hadith from Abdillah ibn Ulathah, who is Abu Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Ulathah, except Sharik, and none from Sharik except Sulayman ibn al-Hakam; al-Hasan ibn Sinan alone transmitted it, and it is not narrated from al-Numan ibn Bashir except with this chain."
"7206","7200 - Muhammad ibn Mahmawayh al-Jawhari narrated to us, Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Adam ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, Abu Ghalib narrated to us, from Abu Umamah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says after the dawn prayer: There is no god but Allah alone, without partner; to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise; He gives life and causes death; in His Hand is good; and He is over all things Powerful, one hundred times, before he folds his legs, he will on that day be the best of the people of the earth in deed, except one who says like his saying, or adds to what he said. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ghalib except Adam ibn al-Hakam, and none narrated it from Adam except Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith."
"7207","7201 - Muhammad ibn Mahmawayh al-Jawhari narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Qasim al-Hashimi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Hani Abu Nuaym al-Nakhai narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Yasir narrated to us, from Ibrahim al-Nakhai, from Alqamah ibn Qays, from Abdillah ibn Masud, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the dawn prayer on Friday: Alif Lam Mim, the revelation, and Has there come upon man. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim except Sulayman ibn Yasir; Abu Nuaym al-Nakhai alone transmitted it."
"7208","7202 - Muhammad ibn Mahmawayh al-Jawhari narrated to us, Mamar ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abu Ali al-Hanafi narrated to us, Salm ibn Zarir narrated to us, Abu Ghalib narrated to us, from Abu Umamah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The Children of Israel split into seventy-one sects, and the Christians split into seventy-two sects, and my ummah will exceed them by one sect; all of them are in the Fire except the great multitude. No one narrated this hadith from Salm except Abu Ali al-Hanafi."
"7209","7203 - Muhammad ibn Said ibn Jaban al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mihran al-Jammal al-Razi narrated to us, Ali ibn Thabit al-Jazari narrated to us, from al-Wazi ibn Nafi, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Jabir ibn Abdillah who said: While the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying Asr in the campaign of Badr, he smiled; then when he finished the prayer, it was said to him: O Messenger of Allah, you smiled during the prayer? He said: Mikail passed by me, with dust upon his wing, so he laughed to me, and I smiled. No one narrated this hadith from Jabir except Abu Salamah, and none from Abu Salamah except al-Wazi ibn Nafi; Ali ibn Thabit alone transmitted it."
"7210","7204 - Muhammad ibn Jaban narrated to us, Zunayj Abu Ghassan al-Razi narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Bashir ibn Salman narrated to us, from Amr ibn Qays al-Mulai, from Jabalah ibn Suhaym, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever seeks Laylat al-Qadr, let him seek it in the last ten. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Qays except al-Hakam ibn Bashir."
"7211","7205 - Muhammad ibn Jaban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mihran al-Jammal narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Muslim ibn Ziyad, the freedman of Maymunah the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no man who says in the morning: O Allah, I enter the morning calling You to witness, and calling the bearers of Your Throne, Your angels, and all Your creation to witness, that You are Allah, there is no god but You, alone, without partner, and that Muhammad is Your servant and Messenger, except that Allah forgives him what sin he commits in that day of his; and if he says it in the evening, Allah forgives him what he commits in that night of his. This hadith is not narrated from Anas except with this chain; Baqiyyah alone transmitted it."
"7212","7206 - Muhammad ibn Jaban narrated to us, Zunayj Abu Ghassan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Mualla al-Razi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Zubayd narrated to us, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awsajah, from al-Bara ibn Azib who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to come to the first row from its beginning to its end, straightening the rows, the people and their shoulders, and saying: Do not differ, lest your hearts differ; Allah and His angels send blessings upon the first rows. And he used to say: Whoever grants a milch animal, or a loan of silver, or guides through a lane, it is like freeing a soul; and whoever says: There is no god but Allah alone, without partner; to Him belongs dominion, and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things Powerful, it is like freeing a soul. And he used to say: Adorn the Quran with your voices. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Rahman ibn Zubayd al-Yami except Muhammad ibn al-Mualla, and Shuja ibn al-Walid."
"7213","7207 - Muhammad ibn Jaban al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us, Zunayj narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Mualla narrated to us, Ashath narrated to us, from Ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik who said: Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) imposed upon the wealth of the Muslims, of every forty dirhams a dirham; and upon the wealth of the dhimmis, of every twenty dirhams a dirham; and upon the wealth of one who has no dhimmah, of every ten dirhams a dirham. No one ascribes this hadith except Muhammad ibn al-Mualla; Zunayj alone transmitted it. And Ayyub, Salamah ibn Alqamah, Yazid ibn Ibrahim, Jarir ibn Hazim, Habib ibn al-Shahid, al-Haytham al-Sayrafi, and a group narrated it, from Anas ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik, that Umar ibn al-Khattab imposed, and he mentioned the story."
"7214","7208 - Muhammad ibn Jaban narrated to us, Zunayj narrated to us, Hakkam ibn Salm narrated to us, from al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, she said: Ibn Masud wanted to build a house, so Quraysh said: Shall we not prevent Ibn Umm Abd from building a house among us? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If I commanded that, then I am unjust; Allah does not sanctify a nation in which the right of its weak is not taken from its strong. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, except al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah; Hakkam ibn Salm alone transmitted it. And Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr al-Mulayki narrated it, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn Abbas."
"7215","7209 - Muhammad ibn Jaban narrated to us, Zunayj Abu Ghassan narrated to us, Hakkam narrated to us, from al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while upon the pulpit, saying: When one of you goes to Friday, let him perform ghusl. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub ibn Musa except al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah; Hakkam ibn Salm alone transmitted it."
"7216","7210 - And with the same chain: from al-Muthanna, from Ata ibn Rabah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We have no evil example: the one who takes back his gift is like the one who returns to his vomit. No one narrated this hadith from Ata except al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah; Hakkam ibn Salm alone transmitted it. And the well-known is from the hadith of Ikrimah."
"7217","7211 - Muhammad ibn Jaban narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Musa al-Sinani narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Ziyad ibn Abi al-Jad, from Salamah ibn Abi Ziyad, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Abu Umamah who said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with two small boys of hers, one boy she was nursing, and she asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), but he found nothing to give her until he found three dates with one of his wives, so he gave her; so she gave this one a date and this one a date, and kept a date; then one of the two boys wept, so she split the date into two halves, and gave this one a half and this one a half. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Caring mothers, bearing mothers, nursing mothers, merciful to their children; were it not for what they do to their husbands, those of them who pray would enter Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Yazid ibn Ziyad ibn Abi al-Jad except al-Fadl ibn Musa al-Sinani."
"7218","7212 - Muhammad ibn Jaban narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us, from Talq ibn Habib, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Four things, whoever is given them has been given the good of this world and the Hereafter: a grateful heart, a remembering tongue, a body patient upon trial, and a wife who does not seek betrayal against him out of fear regarding herself nor his wealth. No one narrated this hadith from Talq ibn Habib except Humayd al-Tawil, and none narrated it from Humayd except Hammad ibn Salamah, and none narrated it from Hammad except Musa; Mahmud ibn Ghaylan alone transmitted it."
"7219","7213 - Muhammad ibn Jaban narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from Zuhayr, from Jabir, from Adi ibn Thabit, from al-Bara ibn Azib who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, forgive the Ansar, and the sons of the Ansar, and the freedmen of the Ansar. No one narrated this hadith from Jabir except Zuhayr; Yahya ibn Adam alone transmitted it."
"7220","7214 - Muhammad ibn Jaban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mihran al-Jammal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Mualla narrated to us, from al-Jarrah ibn al-Dahhak, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdillah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Part of faith is that a man loves a man whom he loves only for Allah, without any wealth he gave him; that is faith. No one raised this hadith from Abu Ishaq except al-Jarrah ibn al-Dahhak."
"7221","7215 - Muhammad ibn Jaban narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Soon the nations will call one another against my ummah as eaters call one another to tharid. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail except Abd al-Aziz, and none from Abd al-Aziz except Muammal; Mahmud alone transmitted it."
"7222","7216 - Muhammad ibn Jaban narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ata ibn Abi Maymunah narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade fasting on Friday, unless with it something else."
"7223","7217 - And with the same chain: he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perform wudu from what fire has altered. No one narrated these two hadiths from Ata ibn Abi Maymunah except his son Rawh, and none from Rawh except al-Nadr ibn Shumayl; Mahmud ibn Ghaylan alone transmitted them."
"7224","7218 - Muhammad ibn Jaban narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, Abu Amir al-Khazzaz narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, she said: I said: O Prophet of Allah, my neighbor, his house is where my house is, his door is far from my door, and another, his door is opposite my door, though his house is farther than the house of that one; with which of them shall I begin? He said: With the one whose door is opposite your door. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Amir al-Khazzaz except al-Nadr ibn Shumayl."
"7225","7219 - Muhammad ibn Jaban narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Saylahini narrated to us, and Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Abdillah ibn Rabah, from Abu Qatadah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by Abu Bakr while he was praying lowering his voice, and passed by Umar while he was praying raising his voice; then in the morning when they gathered with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said to Abu Bakr: O Abu Bakr, I passed by you while you were praying lowering your voice? He said: I have made heard the One whom I whispered to. He said: Raise your voice a little. And he said to Umar: I passed by you, O Umar, while you were praying raising your voice? He said: I feared Satan, O Messenger of Allah. So he said: Lower your voice a little. No one narrated this hadith, connected, from Hammad ibn Salamah except Yahya ibn Ishaq, and it is not narrated from Abu Qatadah except with this chain."
"7226","7220 - Muhammad ibn Jaban narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Muhammad al-Daif narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with the people during his illness while sitting, so they stood, and he gestured to them, so they sat. He said: The imam is followed; when he bows, bow, and when he prostrates, prostrate, and when he prays sitting, pray sitting. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Abd al-Wahhab."
"7227","7221 - Muhammad ibn Jaban narrated to us, Zunayj Abu Ghassan narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Amr ibn Qays, from Asim ibn Abi al-Najud, from Abu Razin, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque and saw the people few, so he said: If a man called the people to a bone and two arrowheads, meaning by mirmat a loaf, they would answer him, while they stay behind from this prayer. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I had intended to command youths to gather bundles of firewood, then burn houses over people who hear the caller and do not answer him. No one narrated this hadith from Asim, from Abu Razin, except Amr ibn Qays; al-Hakam ibn Bashir alone transmitted it. And the people narrated it from Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah. And it was narrated from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdillah."
"7228","7222 - And with the same chain: from Amr ibn Qays al-Mulai, from al-Hurr ibn al-Sayyah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Akhnas, from Said ibn Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Abu Bakr is in Paradise, and Umar is in Paradise, and Uthman is in Paradise, and Ali is in Paradise, and Talhah and al-Zubayr are in Paradise, and Sad ibn Abi Waqqas is in Paradise, and Abd al-Rahman is in Paradise; and the ninth, if I wished I would name him. They said: Who is he? He said: He is whoever he was; then when they pressed him, he said: I; and he wept. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Qays except al-Hakam ibn Bashir."
"7229","7223 - Muhammad ibn Jaban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mihran al-Jammal narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Malik al-Fazari who said: I heard an old shaykh, who was old and kunyahed Abu Muhammad, narrating from Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Recite the Quran with the melodies of the Arabs and their voices, and beware of the melodies of the two Peoples of the Book, and the people of fisq; for there will come after me a people who chant the Quran with the chanting of singing, monasticism, and wailing; it will not pass their throats; their hearts are tempted, and the hearts of those who admire their affair. This hadith is not narrated from Hudhayfah except with this chain; Baqiyyah alone transmitted it."
"7230","7224 - Muhammad ibn Jaban narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Buhlul al-Anbari narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Nafi al-Makhzumi al-Madini narrated to us, al-Mughirah ibn Ismail ibn Ayyub ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Zuhri, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a man who follows a woman unlawfully, may he marry her mother? Or follows the mother unlawfully, may he marry her daughter? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The unlawful does not forbid the lawful; only what is with a lawful marriage forbids. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Uthman; Abdillah ibn Nafi alone transmitted it."
"7231","7225 - Muhammad ibn Jaban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Mustamli narrated to us, Yaqub al-Zuhri narrated to us, Ismail ibn Dawud, the freedman of the Khuzaah, narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi al-Qasim ibn Amir ibn Numayr ibn Kharashah al-Thaqafi, from his father, from his grandfather Numayr ibn Kharashah who said: We came as a delegation to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and reached him at al-Juhfah; the people rejoiced at our arrival, so we embraced Islam. And he commanded them to come with him to Madinah; and their brothers among the people would attend upon them every evening, and upon the stranger Muslims who had come to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and he would urge their share, saying: Your brothers are your guests; every man according to what Allah has widened upon him. So a man would stand and take a man and two men; and the one who would take three was Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf. This hadith is not narrated from Numayr ibn Kharashah except with this chain; Yaqub al-Zuhri alone transmitted it."
"7232","7226 - Muhammad ibn Jaban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Mustamli narrated to us, Ashath ibn Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Artah ibn al-Mundhir mentioning, he said: I heard Hakim ibn Umayr mentioning, from al-Irbad ibn Sariyah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) camped at Khaybar, and the master of Khaybar was defiant and objectionable, so he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Muhammad, is it for you to slaughter our donkeys, eat our dates, enter our houses, and beat our women? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became angry and said: O Abd al-Rahman, mount your horse and call among the people: Paradise is lawful only for a believer, and gather for prayer. So they gathered, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, then said: Allah has not made lawful for you to enter the houses of the People of the Book except with permission, nor eating their wealth, nor beating their women, when they give you what is upon them, except what they willingly give; does a man think, satiated until full, reclining upon his couch, that Allah has forbidden nothing except what is in this Quran? Indeed, by Allah, I have forbidden, commanded, and admonished with things; they are indeed like the Quran, or more. Indeed, there is not lawful for you of beasts of prey every possessor of fangs, nor domestic donkeys. No one narrated this hadith from Artah ibn al-Mundhir except Ashath ibn Shubah."
"7233","7227 - Muhammad ibn Jaban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Mustamli narrated to us, Abu Ali Ubaydillah ibn Abd al-Majid al-Hanafi narrated to us, Zufar ibn al-Hudhayl narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Thabit ibn Ubayd, from Abu Masud al-Ansari, that a man came to the prayer, and his wife met him, so he bent over her and took hold of her, then he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, but he did not forbid him. No one narrated this hadith from Zufar except Abu Ali al-Hanafi."
"7234","7228 - Muhammad ibn Jaban, and Muhammad ibn al-Faraj al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us, they both said: Muhammad ibn Aban al-Balkhi narrated to us, Safwan ibn Isa al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Harun, from Ziyad ibn Sad, from Abu Nahik, from Ibn Abbas who said: Part of the sunnah is that when a man sits, he removes his sandals and places them beside him. No one narrated this hadith from Ziyad ibn Sad except Abdillah ibn Harun al-Zabibi; Safwan ibn Isa alone transmitted it."
"7235","7229 - Muhammad ibn Jaban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Aban al-Balkhi narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Suwayd al-Ramli narrated to us, Utbah ibn Abi Hakim narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan Talhah ibn Nafi, Abdillah ibn Abbas narrated to me, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had promised al-Abbas a number of camels, so he sent me to him; so I spent the night with him, and it was the night of Maymunah bint al-Harith. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slept a little, then I took as a pillow the pillow upon which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had rested; then he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood, performed wudu thoroughly, spilling little water, then stood and began the prayer; and I stood, performed wudu, and stood at his left, so he moved me with his hand, took my ear, and placed me at his right. And Maymunah was menstruating, so she stood, performed wudu, then sat behind him remembering Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Utbah ibn Abi Hakim except Ayyub ibn Suwayd."
"7236","7230 - Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Abdillah ibn Muslim al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us, Shabab al-Usfuri narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Khalid al-Samti narrated to us, Abu Jafar al-Khatmi narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Uqbah ibn al-Fakih ibn Sad al-Ansari, from his grandfather al-Fakih ibn Sad, who had companionship, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ghusl on Friday, on Fitr, on Sacrifice, and on Arafah. This hadith is not narrated from al-Fakih ibn Sad except from the hadith of Abu Jafar al-Khatmi, and none narrated it from Abu Jafar except Yusuf ibn Khalid, and Adi ibn al-Fadl."
"7237","7231 - Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us, Ali ibn Harb al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us, Ashath ibn Attaf narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Arzami, from Abdillah ibn Abi Mulaykah, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah who said: I saw Umar ibn al-Khattab come to the Stone, place his hands upon its two sides, then kiss what is between them, then say: By Allah, I know you are a stone, and you neither harm nor benefit; and were it not that I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kissing you, I would not kiss you. No one narrated this hadith from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah except Ibn Abi Mulaykah, and none from Ibn Abi Mulaykah except al-Arzami; Ashath ibn Attaf alone transmitted it."
"7238","7232 - Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Said ibn Mihran al-Razi narrated to us, Abu Muti al-Balkhi al-Hakam ibn Abdillah narrated to us, from Kharijah ibn Musab, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pronouncing talbiyah for both together: Labbayk with Hajj and Umrah together. No one narrated this hadith from Kharijah except Abu Muti."
"7239","7233 - Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Said ibn Mihran al-Razi narrated to us, Abu Muti al-Hakam ibn Abdillah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Qays al-Asadi narrated to us, from Awn ibn Abdillah ibn Utbah, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, from Abdillah ibn Masud who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: O Messenger of Allah, which deeds are most beloved to Allah, and nearest to Allah? He said: Prayer at its time. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Qays except Abu Muti."
"7240","7234 - Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated to us, Rawh ibn Qurrah al-Muqri narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Khirash narrated to us, from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Anas ibn Malik who said: I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until he passed away, and behind Abu Bakr and Umar until they passed away, and I did not hear any of them recite aloud: In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, in prayer; and they would begin with: Praise. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim al-Taymi except al-Awwam; Abdillah ibn Khirash alone transmitted it."
"7241","7235 - Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Salm ibn Rashid ibn al-Fakhir al-Hujaymi narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Qays ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sends one blessing upon me, Allah sends ten upon him; and whoever sends ten upon me, Allah sends a hundred upon him; and whoever sends a hundred upon me, Allah writes between his eyes freedom from hypocrisy and freedom from the Fire, and Allah will settle him on the Day of Resurrection with the martyrs. No one narrated this hadith from Humayd except Abd al-Aziz ibn Qays; Ibrahim ibn Salm alone transmitted it."
"7242","7236 - Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Umar ibn Yazid al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The days of Tashriq are days of eating and drinking. Muhammad ibn Yahya said: So I objected to Abdillah ibn Umar about this hadith, so he brought out a book to me and said: Abdillah ibn Wahb, the companion of al-Basri, narrated to me, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The days of Tashriq are days of eating and drinking. This hadith is not narrated from Qatadah except with this chain; Abdillah ibn Umar alone transmitted it."
"7243","7237 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Fatimah to Ali, he said: Give her something. He said: I have nothing. He said: And where is your Hutamiyyah armor. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Said, and none from Said except Abdillah ibn Ismail; Abu Kurayb alone transmitted it. And Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated it, from Said, from Ayyub."
"7244","7238 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Bakr ibn Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ulayy, from his father, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not tell you of the best of your workers and the worst of them? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The best of them are the best of them to you: whom you love and who love you, and you supplicate to Allah for them and they supplicate to Allah for you; and the worst of them are the worst of them to you: whom you hate and who hate you, and you supplicate to Allah against them and they supplicate to Allah against you. They said: Shall we not fight them, O Messenger of Allah? He said: No, leave them as long as they pray and fast. No one narrated this hadith from Musa ibn Ulayy except Bakr ibn Yunus; Abu Kurayb alone transmitted it, and it is not narrated from Uqbah ibn Amir except with this chain."
"7245","7239 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Dinar narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali al-Jufi narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, Ibn Judan narrated to us, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, that a man used to revile Abu Bakr before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while Abu Bakr was silent; then when the man fell silent, Abu Bakr answered with a word, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood up, and Abu Bakr followed him and said: O Messenger of Allah, he reviles me while you are sitting, then when I answered, or defended myself, or something like this, you stood? He said: An angel was answering him, saying: You lied; then when you spoke, Satan came, so I disliked sitting. Three things, O Abu Bakr, all of them true: no servant is wronged with an injustice and overlooks it seeking the Face of Allah, except that Allah strengthens his victory through it; and no servant opens a door of giving, seeking the Face of Allah, or kinship, except that Allah increases him in abundance through it; and no servant opens a door of begging, seeking increase through it, except that Allah increases him in scarcity through it. No one narrated this hadith from Ali ibn Zayd except Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, and none narrated it from Sufyan except Husayn al-Jufi; al-Qasim ibn Dinar alone transmitted it. And the people narrated it from Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, from Ibn Ajlan, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah. So if Husayn al-Jufi preserved it, it is strange from the hadith of Ali ibn Zayd, from Ibn al-Musayyib."
"7246","7240 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, Rayhan ibn Said narrated to us, Ararah ibn al-Birind narrated to us, al-Muthanna Abu Hatim narrated to us, from Ubaydillah ibn al-Ayzar, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give gifts, you will love one another; and emigrate, you will bequeath glory to your children; and overlook the slips of the noble. No one narrated this hadith from al-Qasim except Ubaydillah ibn al-Ayzar; al-Muthanna Abu Hatim alone transmitted it."
"7247","7241 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Abu Hammam al-Walid ibn Shuja narrated to us, Said ibn al-Fadl al-Qurashi narrated to us, Umar ibn Abi Salih al-Ataki narrated to us, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah created the intellect, He said to it: Come forward. So it came forward. Then He said to it: Go back. So it went back. Then He said: By My might, I have not created a creation more wondrous to Me than you; with you I take, and with you I give; with you is reward, and upon you is punishment. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Umamah except with this chain; Abu Hammam alone transmitted it."
"7248","7242 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Khallad ibn Yazid al-Jufi narrated to us, from Zuhayr, from Jabir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the group who came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were the jinn of Nasibin; they came to him while he was at Nakhlah. No one narrated this hadith from Jabir except Zuhayr; Abu Kurayb alone transmitted it, from Khallad."
"7249","7243 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Uthman ibn Said narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Man narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Uthman, from Bilal, that he said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Do not precede me with Amin. No one narrated this hadith from al-Qasim except Uthman ibn Said; Abu Kurayb alone transmitted it."
"7250","7244 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Mani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Abi Yazid al-Hamdani narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Muadh ibn Jabal who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever shames his brother for a sin will not die until he does it. This hadith is not narrated from Muadh except with this chain; Ahmad ibn Mani alone transmitted it."
"7251","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Salih ibn Qatan al-Bukhari narrated, Muhammad ibn Ammar ibn Muhammad ibn Ammar ibn Yasir narrated, my father narrated to me, from my grandfather, he said: I saw Ammar ibn Yasir pray six rak'ahs after Maghrib, so I said: O my father, what is this prayer? He said: I saw my beloved, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), pray six rak'ahs after Maghrib, and he said: Whoever prays six rak'ahs after Maghrib, his sins are forgiven even if they are like the foam of the sea. This hadith is not narrated from Ammar except with this isnad; Salih ibn Qatan was alone in transmitting it."
"7252","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Yahya ibn Habib ibn Arabi narrated, Musa ibn Atiyyah al-Bahili narrated, Fudayl ibn Marzuq narrated, from Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us one day and said: Allah has prescribed Friday upon you in this standing place of mine, in this hour of mine, on this day of mine, in this month of mine, in this year of mine until the Day of Resurrection; whoever abandons it without an excuse, with a just imam or an unjust imam, may Allah not gather his affairs for him nor bless him in his matter; indeed he has no prayer, indeed he has no Hajj, indeed he has no righteousness, indeed he has no charity. This hadith was not narrated from Atiyyah except by Fudayl ibn Marzuq, nor from Fudayl except by Musa ibn Atiyyah; Yahya ibn Habib ibn Arabi was alone in transmitting it. And Asad ibn Musa and Abdullah ibn Salih al-Ijli narrated it from Fudayl ibn Marzuq, from al-Walid ibn Bukayr, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Adawi, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7253","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yazid ibn Dhakwan al-Basri narrated, Abu Hammam al-Salt ibn Muhammad al-Kharaki narrated, from al-Mu'alla ibn Rashid, from his grandmother, from Nubayshah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) detained a person on suspicion. This hadith is not narrated from Nubayshah except with this isnad; Ahmad ibn Yazid was alone in transmitting it."
"7254","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Abu Ubaydullah, the son of Hilal al-Yayi's brother, narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Attar narrated to me, Nasih Abu al-Ala narrated, from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah, he said: My name in the pre-Islamic period was Abd Kulal, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named me Abd al-Rahman. This hadith is not narrated from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah, except with this isnad; Abu Ubaydullah ibn Hilal was alone in transmitting it."
"7255","Muhammad ibn Rashid al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Khalid al-Missisi narrated, Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Guard my honor regarding my Companions, then those who follow them, then those who follow them, then those who follow them, then lying will appear until a man testifies before he is asked to testify and swears before he is asked to swear, and offers himself for false speeches; so whoever is pleased with the midst of Paradise, let him hold to the community, for the Hand of Allah is upon the community, and Satan is with the lone one, and he is farther from two; and let no man be alone with a woman, for the third of them is Satan; and whoever is saddened by his evil deed and pleased by his good deed, he is a believer. This hadith was not narrated from Ibn Abi Najih except by Ibn Jurayj; Hajjaj ibn Muhammad was alone in transmitting it."
"7256","Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated, Ismail ibn Qays ibn Sa'd ibn Zayd ibn Thabit narrated, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek livelihood and needs early in the morning, for the early morning brings blessing and success. This hadith was not narrated from Hisham except by Ismail."
"7257","Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'id ibn al-Jawhari narrated, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated, Muhammad ibn Abdullah, the nephew of al-Zuhri, narrated, from his uncle Muhammad ibn Muslim, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Hurmuz informed me, from Abdullah ibn Buhaynah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with his Companions and said: Has any of you just now recited in the prayer? They said: Yes. He said: I say: I will not be contested over the Qur'an. And the people stopped reciting with him when he said that. This hadith was not narrated from al-Zuhri, from al-A'raj, from Ibn Buhaynah, except by the nephew of al-Zuhri; Ya'qub was alone in transmitting it. And the people narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Ibn Ukaymah, from Abu Hurayrah."
"7258","Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated, Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Ibn Abi Ablah narrated to me, from Ibn Budayl ibn Warqa, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Budayl to detain the captives and the properties at al-Ji'ranah until he would come to him, so they were detained. This hadith was not narrated from Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah except by Muhammad ibn Ishaq; Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi was alone in transmitting it."
"7259","Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated, Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Marwudhi narrated, from Sulayman ibn Qarm, from Abu al-Jahhaf, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Zamin, from Zadham, from Ali, he said: The first prayer in which we bowed was Asr, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is this? He said: By this I was commanded. This hadith was not narrated from Abu al-Jahhaf except by Sulayman ibn Qarm; Husayn ibn Muhammad was alone in transmitting it."
"7260","Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated, Shabab ibn Sawwar narrated, from Abdullah ibn al-Ala ibn Zabr, from al-Qasim and Salim and Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray voluntarily upon his mount wherever it turned with him. This hadith was not narrated from al-Qasim except by Abdullah ibn al-Ala; Shabab ibn Sawwar was alone in transmitting it."
"7261","Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated, Sa'id ibn Muhammad al-Warraq narrated, Fudayl ibn Ghazwan narrated, Abu al-Mughirah al-Dhuhli narrated, Fulfulah al-Ju'fi narrated to me, he said: I heard al-Hasan ibn Ali say: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a dream clinging to the Throne, and I saw Abu Bakr holding the waist of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I saw Umar holding the waist of Abu Bakr, and I saw Uthman holding the waist of Umar, and I saw blood pouring from the sky to the earth. Then al-Hasan narrated this hadith while some Shi'ah people were with him, so they said: And did you not see Ali? So al-Hasan said: There was no one dearer to me to see holding the waist of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than Ali, but it is a dream I saw. Then Abu Mas'ud said: You narrate from al-Hasan ibn Ali about a dream he saw, while we were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in an expedition, and hardship struck the people until I saw grief on the faces of the Muslims and joy on the faces of the hypocrites; when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw that, he said: By Allah, the sun will not set until Allah brings you provision. So Uthman knew that Allah and His Messenger would speak the truth, so Uthman bought fourteen mounts with the food upon them and sent nine of them to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw that, he said: What is this? They said: Uthman has gifted it to you. So joy was recognized on the faces of the Muslims and grief on the faces of the hypocrites, and I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raise his hands until the whiteness of his armpits was seen, supplicating for Uthman with a supplication I never heard him supplicate for anyone before him nor after him with its like: O Allah, give Uthman; O Allah, do for Uthman. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari except with this isnad; Sa'id ibn Muhammad al-Warraq was alone in transmitting it."
"7262","Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated, Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi narrated, Muhammad ibn Qays al-Asadi narrated, from Abu Awn al-Thaqafi, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The sons of so-and-so came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we submitted and did such, and we did not fight you while the Arabs fought you. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to Abu Bakr and Umar and said: Do you two say likewise? They said: No. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Their understanding is little, and Satan has spoken upon their tongues. This hadith was not narrated from Abu Awn except by Muhammad ibn Qays; Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi was alone in transmitting it."
"7263","Muhammad ibn Rashid al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated, Abu al-Jawwab narrated, from Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Abbas, from Sa'id ibn Masruq, from Mundhir al-Thawri, from Sa'd ibn Hudhayfah, from Hudhayfah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sent to the Arabian Peninsula and filled it with equity and justice, then Abu Bakr journeyed with them, and he journeyed with them a pleasant journeying, then Umar journeyed with them, and he journeyed with them a pleasant journeying. This hadith was not narrated from Sa'id ibn Masruq except by Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Abbas."
"7264","Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated, Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Marwudhi narrated, from Sulayman ibn Qarm, from Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Abbas, from Ammar al-Duhni, from Aqrab bint Af'a, from Umm Salamah, she said: Jibril, upon him be peace, used to dictate to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). This hadith was not narrated from Ammar al-Duhni except by Abd al-Jabbar, nor from Abd al-Jabbar except by Sulayman ibn Qarm; Husayn ibn Muhammad was alone in transmitting it."
"7265","Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated, Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated, Sulayman ibn Qarm narrated, from Abu al-Jahhaf, from Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Subayh, from his grandfather, from Zayd ibn Arqam, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a house in which were Fatimah and Ali and Hasan and Husayn, and said: I am at war with whoever wars against you, and at peace with whoever makes peace with you. This hadith was not narrated from Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman except by Abu al-Jahhaf, nor from Abu al-Jahhaf except by Sulayman ibn Qarm, nor from Sulayman except by Husayn ibn Muhammad; Ibrahim ibn Sa'id was alone in transmitting it."
"7266","Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated, Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yahya ibn Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, he said: Usamah ibn Zayd said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when the people crowded upon him, would go quickly, and when he found an opening he would walk briskly; when he looked at the people he said: O people, righteousness is not in rushing. He said: And Usamah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) traveled until he stopped at the mountain pass between Muzdalifah and Arafah, then he urinated, so I poured for him from the water-skin and he performed ablution, then I said: O Prophet of Allah, the prayer. He said: The prayer is ahead of you. Then the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mounted until he stopped at Muzdalifah. This hadith was not narrated from Muhammad ibn Abbad except by Ibn Ishaq, nor from Ibn Ishaq except by Yahya ibn Sa'id; and the well-known version is from the hadith of Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Usamah."
"7267","Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated, Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah narrated, from Qudamah ibn Musa, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate: O Allah, set right for me my religion which You made the protection of my affair, and set right for me my worldly life in which You placed my livelihood, and set right for me my Hereafter to which You made my return, and make life an increase for me in every good, and make death a rest for me from every evil. This hadith was not narrated from Qudamah ibn Musa except by Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah; Abu Qatan was alone in transmitting it."
"7268","Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated, al-Aswad ibn Amir, Shadhan, narrated, Ja'far al-Ahmar narrated, from Abdullah ibn Ata, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father, he said: The most beloved of women to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was Fatimah, and among men, Ali. This hadith was not narrated from Ja'far al-Ahmar except by Shadhan, and none narrated it from Abdullah ibn Ata except Ja'far al-Ahmar and Mindal ibn Ali."
"7269","Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated, Ja'far ibn Awn narrated, Abu al-Umays narrated, from Abd al-Majid ibn Suhayl, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, he said: Ibn Abbas said to me: O Ibn Utbah, do you know the last surah of the Qur'an revealed in full? I said: Yes, When the help of Allah comes. He said: You spoke the truth. This hadith was not narrated from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah except by Abd al-Majid ibn Suhayl, nor from Abd al-Majid except by Abu al-Umays; Ja'far ibn Awn was alone in transmitting it."
"7270","Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Khalid al-Missisi narrated, Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated, he said: Ibn Jurayj said: Khusayf said: I asked Sa'id ibn Jubayr about His saying: I ask you no reward for it except love for kinship. He said: Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in the midst of Quraysh, all of them related to him, so he said: Say: I ask you no reward for it except love for kinship, except that you love me due to the kinship between me and you. This hadith was not narrated from Ibn Jurayj except by Hajjaj ibn Muhammad, and none narrated it from Khusayf except Ibn Jurayj and Sharik."
"7271","Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Khalid al-Missisi narrated, Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated, from Abu Bakr al-Hudhali, from Amir al-Sha'bi, that Abu Hurayrah narrated to him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah says: O son of Adam, when you remember Me you thank Me, and when you forget Me you disbelieve in Me. This hadith was not narrated from al-Sha'bi except by Abu Bakr al-Hudhali; Hajjaj ibn Muhammad was alone in transmitting it."
"7272","And with the same isnad: Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad, from his father, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Niyar ibn Mukram, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The bid' (number) is between three and nine. This hadith was not narrated from Ibn Jurayj except by Hajjaj."
"7273","Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us, Isam ibn Rawwad ibn al-Jarrah narrated, my father narrated, Nafi' ibn Umar narrated, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, that she heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever revives dead land, it is his, and there is no right for an unjust root."
"7274","And with the same isnad: he said: Aishah narrated to me that she heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah has obligated upon the servants five prayers in every day and night. This hadith was not narrated from Nafi' ibn Umar except by Rawwad ibn al-Jarrah."
"7275","Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Khalid al-Missisi narrated, Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated, from Abu Ghassan Muhammad ibn Mutarrif, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi', from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Idris, upon him be peace, was a friend of the Angel of Death, so he asked him to show him Paradise and Hell. So he ascended with Idris and showed him Hell, and he was frightened of it and almost fainted, so the Angel of Death wrapped him with his wing. The Angel of Death said: Have you not seen it? He said: Yes, and I have never seen anything like today. Then he went with him until he showed him Paradise, and he entered it. The Angel of Death said to him: Have you not seen it? He said: Yes, by Allah, this is Paradise. The Angel of Death said to him: Then go, you have seen it. He said: To where? The Angel of Death said: To where you were. Idris said: No, by Allah, I will not leave it after having entered it. So it was said to the Angel of Death: Did you not admit him to it, and none who enters it shall leave it. This hadith is not narrated from Umm Salamah except with this isnad."
"7276","Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us, Ahmad ibn al-Walid al-Karkhi narrated, Ishaq ibn Muhammad al-Farwi narrated, Nafi' ibn Abi Nu'aym narrated, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he prayed, would spread his fingers. This hadith was not narrated from Nafi' ibn Abi Nu'aym except by Ishaq al-Farwi; Ahmad ibn al-Walid was alone in transmitting it."
"7277","Muhammad ibn Rashid al-Asbahani narrated to us, Musa ibn Amir Abu Amir narrated, Irak ibn Khalid ibn Yazid narrated, from Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from his father, from Zayd ibn Thabit, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah have mercy on whoever hears this saying of mine and memorizes it until he conveys it to others. Three things over which the heart of a Muslim man bears no malice: sincerity of deed for Allah, sincere advice to the leaders of the Muslims, and adherence to their community, for their supplication encompasses those behind them. Whoever has this world as his intention, Allah places his poverty before his eyes, and Allah scatters his property, and nothing of it comes to him except what was written for him. And whoever has the Hereafter as his intention, Allah places his richness in his heart, and suffices him his property, and the world comes to him humbled. This hadith was not narrated from Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah except by Irak ibn Khalid ibn Yazid."
"7278","Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Khalid al-Missisi narrated, Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated, Abu Ghassan Muhammad ibn Mutarrif narrated, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When the people of Paradise enter Paradise, a man will stand and say: O Lord, permit me to farm. So He will permit him, and he will sow his seed, and he will not turn until every ear grows twelve cubits long, then he will not move from his place until there are heaps of it like mountains. Then a Bedouin said: O Messenger of Allah, you will not find this man except a Qurashi or an Ansari. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed. This hadith was not narrated from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah, except by Abu Ghassan; Hajjaj ibn Muhammad was alone in transmitting it."
"7279","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Ajlan Abu Shaykh al-Asbahani al-Abhari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated, Suhayl ibn Abdullah narrated, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is not pleased with the decree of Allah and does not believe in the predestination of Allah, let him seek a god other than Allah. This hadith was not narrated from Khalid al-Hadhdha except by Suhayl ibn Abdullah; Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi was alone in transmitting it."
"7280","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan Abu Shaykh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abadah al-Wasiti narrated, Abu Sufyan al-Himyari narrated, Hushaym narrated, from Humayd, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Richness is not from abundance of goods; richness is only richness of the soul. This hadith was not narrated from Humayd except by Hushaym, nor from Hushaym except by Abu Sufyan; Muhammad ibn Abadah was alone in transmitting it."
"7281","Muhammad ibn Nusayr al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated, Mubarak ibn Fudalah narrated, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A dream is not narrated except to a scholar or a sincere adviser. This hadith was not narrated from Mubarak ibn Fudalah except by Ismail ibn Amr."
"7282","Muhammad ibn Nusayr narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud ash-Shadhakuni narrated, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated, al-Qasim ibn Ma'n informed, he said: I found in my brother's book, in his handwriting, informing that in our father's book: Zahr ibn Rabi'ah narrated to me that Abdullah ibn Mas'ud informed him that the Messenger of Allah said: Amputation is for a dinar or ten dirhams. This hadith was not narrated from al-Qasim ibn Ma'n except by Ibn Abi Za'idah."
"7283","Muhammad ibn Nusayr al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated, Muhammad ibn Marwan narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Those blessed with favors have enviers, so beware of them. This hadith was not narrated from Ibn Jurayj except by Muhammad ibn Marwan."
"7284","Muhammad ibn Nusayr al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ismail ibn Amr narrated, Isra'il and Abu Isra'il narrated, from Hakim ibn Jubayr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from Aishah, she said: I used to prepare nabidh for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a green jar. This hadith was not narrated from Sa'id ibn Jubayr except by Hakim ibn Jubayr, and none narrated it from Hakim except Isra'il and Abu Isra'il."
"7285","Muhammad ibn Nusayr narrated to us, Ismail ibn Amr narrated, Abu Maryam Abd al-Ghaffar ibn al-Qasim narrated, Simak ibn Harb narrated, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: While we were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a young man came to seek his ruling, and mentioned that he met a woman and kissed her and touched her and fondled her and desired her but could not go further. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him no ruling. When he left, he sent a man after him, called him, and recited this verse to him: And establish prayer at the two ends of the day and approaches of the night, the verse. The man said: O Messenger of Allah, is it for him alone or for people in general? He said: Rather, for people in general. This hadith was not narrated from Abu Maryam except by Ismail ibn Amr."
"7286","Muhammad ibn Nusayr narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud ash-Shadhakuni narrated, Abd al-Wahid ibn Abdullah al-Ansari narrated, Sharqi ibn al-Qutami narrated, from Amr ibn Qays, from Muhill ibn Wada'ah, from Shurayh ibn Abraha, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) utter the takbir in the days of Tashriq from the Dhuhr prayer on the Day of Sacrifice until he left Mina, uttering the takbir after every obligatory prayer. Abu Ayyub ash-Shadhakuni said: This follows the takbir of the people of Madinah. This hadith is not narrated from Shurayh ibn Abraha except with this isnad; Sharqi ibn al-Qutami was alone in transmitting it."
"7287","Muhammad ibn Nusayr narrated to us, ash-Shadhakuni informed, Abu Umayyah ibn Ya'la narrated, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire. This hadith was not narrated from Abu al-Zinad except by Abu Umayyah; ash-Shadhakuni was alone in transmitting it."
"7288","And with the same isnad: Abu Umayyah ibn Ya'la narrated, Nafi' narrated, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no draught greater with Allah than a draught of anger swallowed by a Muslim seeking the Face of Allah. This hadith was not narrated from Nafi' except by Abu Umayyah; ash-Shadhakuni was alone in transmitting it."
"7289","Muhammad ibn Nusayr narrated to us, ash-Shadhakuni narrated, Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated, Muhammad ibn Mihzam narrated, from Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Islam began strange, and it will return strange as it began, so glad tidings to the strangers. This hadith was not narrated from Muhammad ibn Mihzam except by Salm ibn Qutaybah; ash-Shadhakuni was alone in transmitting it."
"7290","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram narrated to us, Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated, my father narrated, Muhammad ibn Aban narrated, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit, and from Ibn Buraydah, from his father, they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) complained of al-udhrah (throat ailment) until it caused him headache, and it was seen upon him. Jibril came to him and said: Your Lord has sent me to you to perform ruqyah upon you. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) uncovered his head, and he said: In the name of Allah I perform ruqyah upon you, from everything that harms you, from the evil of the eye of every envier I perform ruqyah upon you. He said: He repeated it to him three times, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recovered. This hadith was not narrated from Alqamah ibn Marthad except by Muhammad ibn Aban."
"7291","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated, my father narrated, Thabit ibn Yazid Abu Zayd narrated, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I was standing serving my paternal uncles a drink of their fadikh, when a man came and said: Wine has been prohibited. They said: Pour it out. So I poured it out. I said: What was it? He said: Unripe and ripe dates. Abu Bakr said: That was their wine that day, while Anas was listening. This hadith was not narrated from Asim al-Ahwal except by Thabit Abu Zayd; Muhammad ibn al-Hasan was alone in transmitting it."
"7292","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram narrated to us, Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated, my father narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Thabit, from Anas, that a man came after the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had prayed, and stood praying alone, so he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will trade profitably with this one and pray with him?"
"7293","And with the same isnad: Hammad narrated, from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Is any of you unable to recite a third of the Qur'an every night? They said: And who can bear that? He said: He recites: Say: He is Allah, the One. These two hadiths were not narrated from Hammad ibn Salamah except by Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi."
"7294","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated, my father narrated, Utbah Abu Amr narrated, from Abu Rawq, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in the garden of a man from the Ansar, when a man came seeking to enter. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Stand, O Anas, open for him and give him glad tidings of Paradise, and inform him that he will rule my Ummah after me. So I stood and opened for him, and it was Abu Bakr. I gave him glad tidings of Paradise, so he praised Allah and entered. Then another came and knocked on the door. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Stand, O Anas, open for him and give him glad tidings of Paradise, and inform him that he will rule my Ummah after Abu Bakr. So I opened for him, and it was Umar. I gave him glad tidings, so he praised Allah and entered. Then another came and knocked on the door. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Stand, O Anas, open for him and give him glad tidings of Paradise, and inform him that he will rule my Ummah after Abu Bakr and Umar, and that he will meet harshness from the subjects until they reach his blood in that, so I command him then to restrain. So I opened for him, and it was Uthman ibn Affan. I gave him glad tidings of Paradise, so he praised Allah, then I informed him of his rule and that they would reach his blood in that, so he said: To Allah we belong and to Him we return, then he entered. This hadith was not narrated from Abu Rawq except by Utbah; Muhammad ibn al-Hasan was alone in transmitting it."
"7295","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Tusi narrated, Yunus ibn Muhammad al-Mu'addib narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Wa'lah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Any skin that is tanned has become pure. This hadith was not narrated from Hammad ibn Zayd except by Yunus ibn Muhammad al-Mu'addib; Muhammad ibn Mansur was alone in transmitting it."
"7296","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Khalid ibn Yazid al-Lu'lu'i narrated, my father narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated, from Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, from Amr ibn Dinar, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah say: We used to take provisions from the meat of the sacrificial animals in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Madinah. This hadith was not narrated from Qays except by Khalid ibn Yazid al-Lu'lu'i."
"7297","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram al-Asbahani narrated to us, Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi narrated, my father narrated, al-Ala ibn Zuhayr narrated, from Wabarah ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: We were with Abdullah ibn Umar when a man from the people of Kufah asked him: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, inform me about Uthman ibn Affan: did he witness Badr? He said: No. He said: Allah is Most Great. He said: Inform me: was Uthman among those who turned away on the day the two hosts met? He said: Yes. He said: Allah is Most Great. He said: Inform me: did Uthman witness the Pledge of Ridwan? He said: No. He said: Allah is Most Great. Then he left. I said to him, in my place: The man is from the people of Kufah, and they love Ali and hate Uthman. He said: Bring the man to me. So he was brought. He said: You asked me about Uthman, did he witness Badr? I said to you: No, and I will inform you about that: the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was ill, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Stay behind with my daughter? He said: As you like. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: It is dearer to me that you stay behind with her; and he gave him the like of the reward of whoever witnessed it and allotted him a share. Say once: Allah is Most Great. As for your saying that he was among those who turned away on the day the two hosts met, Allah has informed us that He has pardoned them. Say twice: Allah is Most Great. As for your saying that he did not witness the Pledge of Ridwan, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Uthman to the people of Makkah, and when he commanded the pledge, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, Uthman is engaged in Your need and the need of Your Messenger; this is my hand and this is the hand of Uthman; and he struck with his hand upon his other hand and pledged allegiance on his behalf. This hadith was not narrated from Wabarah except by al-Ala ibn Zuhayr; Muhammad ibn al-Hasan was alone in transmitting it."
"7298","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated, my father narrated, Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated, from his father, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Muhajirun said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): We have come to a people the like of whom we have never seen in consoling with little nor in giving generously with much; by Allah, they have sufficed us the burden and shared with us the pleasant livelihood, and we fear they will take all the reward. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No; as long as you praise them and supplicate for them. This hadith was not narrated from Sulayman al-Taymi except by his son; Muhammad ibn al-Hasan was alone in transmitting it."
"7299","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Tusi narrated, Salih ibn Ishaq al-Jihbidh narrated, Yahya ibn Ma'in pointed him out to me, Ma'ruf ibn Wasil narrated, from Ya'qub ibn Abi Nabat, from Abd al-Rahman al-Agharr, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Some people from the people of La ilaha illa Allah will enter the Fire due to their sins, then the people of al-Lat and al-Uzza will say to them: What did your saying La ilaha illa Allah avail you while you are with us in the Fire? So Allah will become angry for them and bring them out, and cast them into the River of Life, and they will recover from their burning as the moon recovers from its eclipse, and they will enter Paradise, and they will be called therein al-Jahannamiyyin. A man said: O Anas, did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? Anas said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire. Yes, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say this. This hadith was not narrated from Ma'ruf ibn Wasil except by Salih ibn Ishaq al-Jihbidh."
"7300","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated, Bakr ibn Yahya ibn Zabban narrated, Hibban ibn Ali narrated, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Dawud ibn Ali, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The child of adultery is the worst of the three, if he acts upon the deed of his parents. This hadith was not narrated from Dawud ibn Ali except by Ibn Abi Layla; Bakr ibn Yahya ibn Zabban was alone in transmitting it."
"7301","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated, Abdullah ibn Qays al-Raqashi al-Khazzaz narrated, Hassan ibn Zarbi al-Nahdi narrated, from Abu Sa'id al-Raqashi, he said: I entered upon Aishah, and she said: What is with Abu Hasan that he kills his companions, the reciters? He said: I said: O Mother of the Believers, we found among the slain Dhu al-Thudayyah. She sobbed, or breathed, then said: Concealing testimony is like bearing false witness; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The best of my Ummah will kill this faction. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Sa'id al-Raqashi except with this isnad; Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna was alone in transmitting it."
"7302","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan narrated, Ishaq ibn Idris narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam narrated, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves to bracelet his child with a bracelet of fire, let him bracelet him with a bracelet of gold; but as for silver, work with it as you wish. This hadith was not narrated from Abu Hazim except by Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd, nor from Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd except by Ishaq ibn Idris; Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan was alone in transmitting it."
"7303","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Mundhir al-Tariqi narrated, Ishaq ibn Mansur al-Saluli narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi' and Mu'awiyah ibn Ishaq narrated, from Abu Salih al-Hanafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever mutilates something and then does not repent from it, he will be mutilated on the Day of Resurrection. This hadith was not narrated from Mu'awiyah ibn Ishaq except by Qays; Ishaq ibn Mansur was alone in transmitting it."
"7304","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, Ali ibn Harb al-Mawsili narrated, Abu Sa'id al-Haytham ibn Mahfuz al-Sa'di narrated, Abu Isra'il narrated, from al-Sari ibn Ismail, from al-Sha'bi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Salman al-Farisi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to marry Arab women. This hadith was not narrated from Ibn Abi Layla except by al-Sha'bi, nor narrated it from al-Sha'bi except by al-Sari ibn Ismail, nor narrated it from al-Sari except by Abu Isra'il; al-Haytham ibn Mahfuz was alone in transmitting it."
"7305","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Ya'qub al-Rukhami narrated, Habib, the scribe of Malik, narrated, Abdullah ibn Amir al-Aslami narrated, from Amr ibn Muslim al-Junda'i, from Rifa'ah ibn Rafi', from al-Bara ibn Azib, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abu Bakr and Umar: Praise be to Allah who has supported me with you two; were it not that you two differ over me, I would not have differed from you. This hadith is not narrated from al-Bara ibn Azib except with this isnad; Habib, the scribe of Malik, was alone in transmitting it."
"7306","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Waki' ibn al-Jarrah narrated, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not shake hands with the Jews and Christians. This hadith was not narrated from Suhayl except by Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash."
"7307","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated, Safwan ibn Isa narrated, Ziyad Abu Amr narrated, from Abu al-Khalil, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the cutting of al-marajih (swings). This hadith is not narrated from Aishah except with this isnad; Safwan ibn Isa was alone in transmitting it."
"7308","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram narrated to us, Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated, Shu'bah narrated, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, I heard Abd al-Rahman al-A'raj narrating from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he opened the prayer, said: Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds, then paused briefly. This hadith was not narrated from Shu'bah except by Abu Dawud."
"7309","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated, Sa'id ibn Zakariyya al-Mada'ini narrated, from Anbasah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is part of righteousness to maintain ties with the friend of your father. This hadith is not narrated from Anas except with this isnad; and Ibn Sabit narrated no hadith from Anas other than this."
"7310","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, Nasr ibn Ali narrated, Harun ibn Muslim, the owner of henna, narrated, al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ansari narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the two rak'ahs before Fajr and the two rak'ahs after Maghrib: Say: O disbelievers, and Say: He is Allah, the One. This hadith is not narrated from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Aishah, except with this isnad; Harun ibn Muslim was alone in transmitting it."
"7311","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Yunus al-Raqqi narrated, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Aishah, she said: The owner of Alexandria, al-Muqawqis, gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a cane kohl stick holder from Sham, a mirror, and a comb. This hadith was not narrated from Ibn Jurayj except by al-Walid ibn Muslim; Abd al-Rahman ibn Yunus was alone in transmitting it."
"7312","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Nasih al-Mukharrimi narrated, Ruwaym ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated, Ismail ibn Yahya al-Taymi narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw Abu al-Darda walking in front of Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, and said: O Abu al-Darda, do you walk in front of a man after the Prophets upon whom the sun has not risen over one better than him? After that, Abu al-Darda was never seen walking except behind Abu Bakr. This hadith was not narrated from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Jabir, except by Ismail ibn Yahya; Ruwaym ibn Yazid al-Muqri was alone in transmitting it. And others narrated it from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Abu al-Darda."
"7313","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Harb al-Nasha'i narrated, Abu Sufyan al-Himyari narrated, al-Dahhak ibn Humrah narrated, from Yazid ibn Khumayr, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The days were presented to me, and Friday was presented to me among them, and it was like a beautiful mirror, and in its middle was a black spot. I said: What is this? It was said: The Hour. This hadith was not narrated from Yazid ibn Khumayr except by al-Dahhak ibn Humrah; Abu Sufyan al-Himyari was alone in transmitting it."
"7314","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Harb al-Nasha'i narrated, Ali ibn Yazid al-Akfani narrated, from Hafs al-Ghadiri, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from his father, he said: Ali ibn Abi Talib heard a noise in the mosque, reciting the Qur'an and teaching it, and said: Glad tidings to these; these were the most beloved of people to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). This hadith was not narrated from Asim ibn Kulayb except by Hafs al-Ghadiri; Ali ibn Yazid was alone in transmitting it."
"7315","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn al-Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal al-Anmati narrated, my father narrated, Yazid ibn Ibrahim al-Tustari narrated, Layth ibn Abi Sulaym narrated, from al-Nu'man ibn Salim, from al-Rubayyi' bint Mu'awwidh, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to come to us and visit us, and when prayer time came, we placed a vessel for him, estimating that he would take a mudd or a mudd and a half, and he would wash his hands three times, rinse his mouth three times, sniff water three times, wash his face three times, then wash his hands three times three times, wipe his head once, wash his ears, their outer and inner and their folds, wash his feet three times three times, and run his fingers between his toes. This hadith was not narrated from al-Nu'man ibn Salim except by Layth, nor from Layth except by Yazid, nor from Yazid except by Hajjaj; his son was alone in transmitting it."
"7316","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated, al-Minhal ibn Bahr narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Abu Sinan, from al-Mughirah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ubayd, from his father, from his grandfather, who had companionship, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Faith is three hundred and thirty-three legislations; whoever fulfills one of them enters Paradise. This hadith was not narrated from Hammad ibn Salamah except by al-Minhal ibn Bahr; Abu Hafs was alone in transmitting it."
"7317","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Hisham al-Asbahani narrated, Ibrahim ibn Hayyan ibn Hakim ibn Hanzalah ibn Suwayd ibn Alqamah ibn Sa'd ibn Mu'adh al-Ansari narrated, Sharik narrated to me, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Clean between your teeth, for it is cleanliness, and cleanliness calls to faith, and faith is with its companion in Paradise. This hadith was not narrated from Mughirah except by Sharik, nor from Sharik except by Ibrahim ibn Hayyan; al-Nadr ibn Hisham was alone in transmitting it."
"7318","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Waqid narrated, Ayyub ibn Jabir narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform Witr with: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and Say: O disbelievers, and Say: He is Allah, the One. This hadith was not narrated from Abu Ishaq, from Nafi', except by Ayyub ibn Jabir; Abd al-Rahman ibn Waqid was alone in transmitting it. And the people narrated it from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas. And Isra'il narrated it from Abu Ishaq, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas."
"7319","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, Ali ibn Salim al-Baghdadi narrated, Yahya ibn Zakariyya, meaning Ibn Abi Za'idah, narrated, from al-Ajlah, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from his father Kuhayl, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to close the door, to cover the vessel, to tie the mouth of the waterskin, and to extinguish the lamp. Kuhayl Abu Salamah narrated no hadith from Ali other than this, and none narrated it from Salamah ibn Kuhayl except al-Ajlah, nor from al-Ajlah except Yahya ibn Zakariyya."
"7320","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, Khallad ibn Aslam narrated, Muhammad ibn al-Zibriqan narrated, from Marwan ibn Salim, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the servant stands in prayer, his sins are gathered upon his head, then when he bows they scatter. This hadith was not narrated from Ubaydullah ibn Umar except by Marwan; Muhammad ibn al-Zibriqan was alone in transmitting it."
"7321","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated, Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated, Wuhayb narrated, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Utayy, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of al-uqdah have perished, by the Lord of the Ka'bah; by Allah, I do not grieve over them, but I grieve over those destroyed from the Ummah of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). This hadith was not narrated from Yunus except by Wuhayb, nor from Wuhayb except by Sahl ibn Bakkar; Ibn al-Muthanna was alone in transmitting it."
"7322","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn Fudayl al-Jazari narrated, Amr ibn Uthman narrated, Asbagh ibn Muhammad al-Raqqi narrated, from Ja'far ibn Burqan, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the signs of the Hour is that Luka' ibn Luka' prevails over the world; then the best of people that day is a believer between two noble ones. This hadith was not narrated from al-Zuhri except by Ja'far ibn Burqan, nor from Ja'far except by Asbagh ibn Muhammad; Amr ibn Uthman was alone in transmitting it."
"7323","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, Khallad ibn Aslam narrated, Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most beloved food to Allah is that over which many hands gather. This hadith was not narrated from Ibn Jurayj except by Abd al-Majid."
"7324","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram narrated to us, Abbad ibn Ya'qub al-Asadi narrated, Ali ibn Hashim ibn al-Barid narrated, Nasih narrated, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali: You are appointed as a commander and left as a successor, and you will be killed, and this will be dyed from this, his beard from his head. This hadith was not narrated from Simak ibn Harb except by Nasih, nor from Nasih except by Ali ibn Hashim; Abbad ibn Ya'qub was alone in transmitting it."
"7325","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Tusi narrated, Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Saylahini narrated, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated, from his father Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from his father Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah, from Umm Habibah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me saying: To Allah we belong and to Him we return; woe to the Arabs from an evil that has drawn near; opened of the barrier of Gog and Magog like this, and he made a circle of ninety. I said: O Messenger of Allah, will we perish while the righteous are among us? He said: Yes, when filth increases. Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf narrated no hadith from Abu Salamah other than this; Yahya ibn Ishaq was alone in transmitting it."
"7326","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Harb al-Nasha'i narrated, Ali ibn Yazid al-Akfani narrated, from Fudayl ibn Marzuq, from Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not enter the bathhouse except with a waistcloth; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not admit his wife into the bathhouse; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him hasten to Friday; and whoever dispenses with it through amusement and trade, Allah dispenses with him, and Allah is Rich, Praiseworthy. This hadith was not narrated from Fudayl ibn Marzuq except by Ali ibn Yazid; Muhammad ibn Harb was alone in transmitting it."
"7327","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Khalid ibn Yazid al-Lu'lu'i narrated, my father narrated, Sharik narrated, from Mutarrif, from Zayd al-Ammi, from Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji and Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Ibn Umar, that the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked him about the train of the garment, and he said: Make it a span. They said: A span does not cover any nakedness. He said: Make it a cubit; do not exceed that. This hadith was not narrated from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid except by Sharik, nor from Sharik except by Khalid ibn Yazid, the owner of pearls; his son was alone in transmitting it."
"7328","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mas'ud ibn al-Ajami narrated, al-Haytham ibn Jamil narrated, Mubarak ibn Fudalah narrated, from Bakr ibn Abdullah al-Muzani, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I joke, but I say only the truth. This hadith was not narrated from al-Mubarak ibn Fudalah except by al-Haytham ibn Jamil."
"7329","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abd al-Hakam al-Warraq narrated, Anas ibn Iyad narrated, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of minor sins, for minor sins are like a people who stopped in the belly of a valley, and this one came with a stick and that one came with a stick, until they gathered what they cooked their bread with; and minor sins, when their companion is taken for them, destroy him. This hadith is not narrated from Sahl ibn Sa'd except with this isnad; Abd al-Wahhab was alone in transmitting it."
"7330","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Sahl al-A'raj narrated, Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated, Isra'il narrated, from Mu'awiyah ibn Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, exalted be His mention, has permitted me to narrate about a rooster whose legs have pierced the earth, and whose neck is bent beneath the Throne, saying: Glory be to You, how great You are, our Lord. So He replies to him: He who swears by Me falsely does not know that. This hadith was not narrated from Mu'awiyah ibn Ishaq except by Isra'il; Ishaq ibn Mansur was alone in transmitting it."
"7331","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Asfati narrated, Safwan ibn Hubayrah narrated, Isa ibn al-Musayyib al-Bajali the judge narrated, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Four matters of the son of Adam have been concluded: creation, character, provision, and term. This hadith was not narrated from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman except by Isa ibn al-Musayyib; Safwan ibn Hubayrah was alone in transmitting it."
"7332","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Khalid al-Khallal narrated, al-Hasan ibn Bishr narrated, he said: I found in my father's book: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever walks to fulfill his brother's need is better for him than ten years of seclusion in worship; and whoever secludes himself for a day seeking the Face of Allah, Allah places between him and the Fire three trenches, each trench farther than what is between the two horizons. This hadith was not narrated from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad except by Bishr ibn Salm al-Bajali; his son was alone in transmitting it."
"7333","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Yunus narrated, Mansur ibn Ammar narrated, from Ibn Lahi'ah, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out having tied a knot between his shoulders, and a Bedouin said to him: What is this, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Woe to you, O Bedouin, I have only worn it to suppress pride."
"7334","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Yunus narrated, he said: I heard Mansur ibn Ammar, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not raise a man of honor in his estimation nor lower him except by piety. These two hadiths were not narrated from Urwah except by Abu al-Aswad Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, nor from Abu al-Aswad except by Ibn Lahi'ah; Mansur ibn Ammar was alone in transmitting them."
"7335","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim narrated, Ali ibn Thabit al-Dahhan narrated, al-Hakam ibn Abd al-Malik narrated, from Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Aishah, she said: A scorpion stung the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in prayer, and he said: May Allah curse the scorpion; it stings the one praying and the one not praying; kill it in the lawful land and the sanctuary. This hadith was not narrated from Qatadah except by al-Hakam ibn Abd al-Malik; Ali ibn Thabit was alone in transmitting it."
"7336","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hanan narrated, Damrah narrated, Uthman ibn Ata narrated, from his father, from Sulayman, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a land of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf in which there was crops, and said: O Abd al-Rahman, do not eat usury nor feed it, and do not sow except in a land you inherit or bequeath or are granted. This hadith was not narrated from Ata al-Khurasani except by his son Uthman. And Sulayman, from whom Ata narrated, is Sulayman ibn Yasar."
"7337","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Yunus narrated, Mutarrif ibn Mazin narrated, from Ma'mar, from Abd al-Karim, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, from al-Nazzal ibn Sabrah, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no suckling after weaning, no orphanhood after puberty, no silence a day until night, and no divorce except after marriage. Thus Mutarrif ibn Mazin narrated this hadith from Ma'mar, from Abd al-Karim, who is Ibn Abi al-Mukhariq. And Abd al-Razzaq narrated it from Ma'mar, from Juwaybir, from al-Dahhak."
"7338","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Ya'qub narrated, al-Haytham ibn Jamil narrated, Mubarak ibn Fudalah narrated, from Asim, I think from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: We were taught the istikhara as we were taught a surah of the Qur'an: when a man intends a matter, he says: O Allah, I seek good from You by Your knowledge, and I seek ability from You by Your power, and I ask You of Your vast bounty, for You are able and I am not able, and You know and I do not know, and You are the Knower of the unseen. O Allah, if this matter which I intend, and he names it, is good for me in my religion, and good for me in my worldly life, and good for me in my Hereafter, and good for me in the outcome of my affair, then make it easy for me and bless it for me; and if it is evil for me in my religion, and evil for me in my worldly life, and evil for me in the outcome of my affair, then turn it away from me, and make good easy for me, and decree it for me, then make me pleased with Your decree. This hadith was not narrated from Mubarak ibn Fudalah except by al-Haytham ibn Jamil; al-Fadl ibn Ya'qub was alone in transmitting it."
"7339","Muhammad ibn Aban al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated, Abu Awanah narrated, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Abu Bakr entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: How are you this morning, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Well and good, from a man who did not wake up fasting, nor visit a sick person, nor follow a funeral. This hadith was not narrated from Umar ibn Abi Salamah except by Abu Awanah; Abu Dawud was alone in transmitting it."
"7340","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isa al-Damaghani narrated, Salamah ibn al-Fadl narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, raising the hadith to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Among what Allah created is a rooster whose talons are upon the seventh earth, and its comb is folded beneath the Throne, its two wings having encompassed the two horizons; when the last third of the night remains, it strikes with its wings, then says: Glorify the Sovereign, the Holy; glory be to our Lord, the Sovereign, the Holy; we have no god other than Him. He said: All between the two horizons hears it except the two heavy ones. He said: They deem that roosters strike with their wings and cry only when they hear that. This hadith was not narrated from Mansur except by Muhammad ibn Ishaq, nor from Ibn Ishaq except by Salamah ibn al-Fadl; Muhammad ibn Isa was alone in transmitting it."
"7341","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isa al-Damaghani narrated, Salamah ibn al-Fadl narrated, from Mika'il, from Layth, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, from Abu Dharr, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, was Adam a prophet? He said: Yes, he was a prophet and a messenger; Allah spoke to him face to face; He said to him: O Adam, dwell, you and your wife, in Paradise. This hadith was not narrated from Ibrahim al-Taymi except by Layth, nor from Layth except by Mika'il, a Kufan shaykh, nor from Mika'il except by Salamah ibn al-Fadl."
"7342","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Haddadi narrated, Humayd ibn Mihran narrated, from Abu al-Zibriqan al-Hilali, from Burayd ibn Abi Maryam, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever recites: Say: He is Allah, the One, it is as if he recited a third of the Qur'an. This hadith is not narrated from Burayd ibn Abi Maryam except with this isnad; Zayd ibn Akhzam was alone in transmitting it."
"7343","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated, Bishr ibn Umar al-Zahrani narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from al-Nu'man ibn Murrah, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Ansar are my trust and my charge; so accept from their doers of good and overlook their doers of evil. This hadith was not narrated from Yahya ibn Sa'id except by Hammad ibn Salamah, nor from Hammad except by Bishr ibn Umar; Zayd ibn Akhzam was alone in transmitting it."
"7344","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Marwazi narrated, Yahya ibn Nasr ibn Hajib narrated, from Warqa, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I see that your dreams have coincided upon the last ten nights, so seek it in the last ten. This hadith was not narrated from Ayyub ibn Musa except by Warqa, nor from Warqa except by Yahya ibn Nasr; Ahmad ibn Mansur was alone in transmitting it."
"7345","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Abu Mahdhurah Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah narrated, al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan al-Ashqar narrated, Hushaym narrated, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was distributing the spoils of Hunayn while Jibril was beside him, when an angel came and said: Your Lord commands you with such and such. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) feared he might be a devil, so he said to Jibril: Do you know him? He said: He is an angel, and I do not know all the angels of your Lord. This hadith was not narrated from Dawud except by Hushaym; Husayn al-Ashqar was alone in transmitting it."
"7346","And with the same isnad: Husayn al-Ashqar narrated, Sharik narrated, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of the lofty degrees, those below them see them as you see the brilliant star on the horizon of the sky; and Abu Bakr and Umar are among them, and how excellent. This hadith was not narrated from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir except by Sharik; Husayn al-Ashqar was alone in transmitting it."
"7347","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Marwazi narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Qays al-Dabbi narrated, Hilal ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: One who remembers Allah in Ramadan is forgiven, and one who asks Allah in it is not disappointed. This hadith was not narrated from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib except by Ali ibn Zayd, nor from Ali except by Hilal ibn Abd al-Rahman; Abd al-Rahman ibn Qays was alone in transmitting it."
"7348","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ishaq al-Jawhari narrated, Khalid ibn Yazid al-Umari narrated, Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Abi Habibah narrated, from Muslim ibn Abi Maryam, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, upon the pulpit with the people around him: O people, be shy of Allah with true shyness. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, we are indeed shy of Allah. He said: Whoever among you is shy, let him not spend a night except with his term before his eyes, and let him guard the belly and what it contains, and the head and what it holds, and let him remember the graves and decay, and let him abandon the adornment of worldly life. This hadith was not narrated from Urwah except by Muslim ibn Abi Maryam, nor from Muslim except by Ibn Abi Habibah; Khalid ibn Yazid was alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Aishah except with this isnad."
"7349","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Waddah al-Hashimi narrated, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated, Abu Amir al-Khazzaz narrated, from Humayd ibn Hilal, Nasr ibn Asim narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Qurt, he said: I passed through Kufah and entered the mosque, and there were a people sitting as if their heads had been cut off. I sat at the nearest of the people and said to a man: O servant of Allah, who is this man? He said: As if you are a stranger. I said: Yes. He said: Had you been from its people you would have known him; this is Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman. He began narrating to the people and said: People used to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about good, and I would ask him about evil, so that I may avoid it, and I know that good will not escape me. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, is there after this good which comes, any evil? He said: O Hudhayfah, learn the Book of Allah and act upon what is in it. Then he said: Yes, tribulation and discord. I said: Will there be after that any good? He said: Yes, a community upon filth, and a truce upon smoke. I said: O Messenger of Allah, is there after that good any evil? He said: O Hudhayfah, learn the Book of Allah and act upon what is in it, until I asked him likewise three times, he saying the like of that. Then he said: Yes, there will be a tribulation, at whose doors are callers to the Fire; that you die when you die while biting upon a root is better than following any of them. This hadith was not narrated from Abu Amir al-Khazzaz except by Rawh ibn Ubadah."
"7350","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Aqil al-Muqri narrated, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated, al-Hasan ibn Abi Ja'far narrated, from Ash'ath ibn Jabir al-Huddani, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever repents before the sun rises from its west, Allah turns to him in forgiveness. This hadith was not narrated from Ash'ath except by al-Hasan ibn Abi Ja'far, nor from al-Hasan except by Muslim ibn Ibrahim; Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Aqil was alone in transmitting it."
"7351","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Rawh ibn Hatim Abu Ghassan al-Judhu'i narrated, Amr ibn Asim al-Kilabi narrated, Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated, from al-Walid ibn Marwan, from Ghaylan ibn Jarir, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey; some of us fasting and some of us breaking fast, and the fasting did not fault the one breaking fast, nor the one breaking fast the fasting. This hadith was not narrated from Ghaylan ibn Jarir except by al-Walid ibn Marwan, nor from al-Walid except by Mu'tamir; Amr ibn Asim was alone in transmitting it."
"7352","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Layth Abu al-Sabbah al-Haddadi narrated, Bakr ibn Yahya ibn Zabban narrated, Mindal ibn Ali narrated, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution once once, then stand and pray. This hadith was not narrated from Ibn Abi Najih except by Mindal; Bakr ibn Yahya was alone in transmitting it."
"7353","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Sawwar ibn Sahl Abu Sahl al-Makhzumi narrated, Sa'id ibn Amir al-Duba'i narrated, from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you place your dead in the graves, say: In the name of Allah and upon the religion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). This hadith was not narrated from Ayyub except by Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, nor from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah except by Sa'id ibn Amir, nor from Sa'id except by Sawwar ibn Sahl."
"7354","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Sumay' Abu Hammam narrated, Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Majid narrated, Imran Abu al-Awwam narrated, from Umar ibn Muhammad, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded a caller, who called out on a rainy night: Pray in your dwellings. This hadith was not narrated from Imran except by Abu Ali al-Hanafi, Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Majid; Abd al-Salam was alone in transmitting it."
"7355","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Sumay' narrated, Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Majid narrated, Abdullah ibn Umar narrated, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged by an oath with a single witness. This hadith was not narrated from Ubaydullah ibn Umar except by Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Majid; Abd al-Salam was alone in transmitting it."
"7356","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Muhallabi narrated, Abu Asim narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Remorse is repentance. This hadith was not narrated from Ibn Jurayj except by Abu Asim; al-Qasim ibn Muhammad ibn Abbad was alone in transmitting it."
"7357","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Salamah ibn Shabib narrated, Abdullah ibn Ibrahim al-Ghifari narrated, Hurr ibn Abdullah al-Hadhdha narrated, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most beloved religion to Allah is the easy monotheism. This hadith was not narrated from Safwan ibn Sulaym except by Hurr ibn Abdullah; Abdullah ibn Ibrahim was alone in transmitting it."
"7358","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Muhallabi narrated, Abu Asim narrated, Mansur ibn Dinar narrated, Ata informed me, Jabir ibn Abdullah informed me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade dates and unripe dates, and raisins and dates, to be steeped together."
"7359","And with the same isnad: Mansur ibn Dinar narrated, Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad informed me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered and circumambulated the House upon his mount, touching the corner with his staff. Then he said: O Abbas, is there any drink? He said: Yes. He said: From what the pilgrims have stirred with their hands, or from what is in the house? He said: From what the pilgrims have stirred with their hands. So a large cup was brought, and he raised it to his face and disliked it, then turned away. Then he said: The raisins of Ta'if have a strong foam. Then he said: Call for a skin of water for me. A skin of water was brought, and he poured it over it, then drank and gave his Companions to drink."
"7360","And with the same isnad: Mansur ibn Dinar narrated, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, he said: I said to Jabir ibn Abdullah: Did you call anyone of the people of the qiblah a disbeliever? He said: No. I said: Did you call them a polytheist? He said: Allah forbid. This hadith was not narrated from Mansur ibn Dinar except by Abu Asim."
"7361","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ammar ibn Khalid al-Wasiti narrated, Ali ibn Ghurab narrated, from Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is a day of festival which Allah has made for the Muslims; whoever comes to Friday, let him bathe, and if he has perfume let him touch of it, and upon you is the toothstick. This hadith was not narrated from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq, except by Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar, nor from Salih except by Ali ibn Ghurab; Ammar ibn Khalid was alone in transmitting it. And Mu'awiyah ibn Yahya narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Ayyub; and Ibn Lahi'ah narrated it from Uqayl, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik."
"7362","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ammar ibn Khalid narrated, Abu Sayfi narrated, he said: I heard Mujahid Abu al-Hajjaj narrating from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man was admitted to Paradise and saw his servant above his rank, and said: O Lord, this is my servant above my rank in Paradise? He said to him: Yes, I rewarded him for his deed and rewarded you for your deed."
"7363","And with the same isnad: I heard Mujahid Abu al-Hajjaj narrating from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first to be driven to Paradise is a slave who obeyed Allah and obeyed his masters, or his master."
"7364","And with the same isnad: I heard Mujahid narrating from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no charity better than a charity given to a slave under an evil master. These hadiths were not narrated from Mujahid except by Abu Sayfi."
"7365","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti narrated, Muhammad ibn Hammad al-Wasiti narrated, Umar Abu Hafs narrated, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Buraydah, from his father, he said: A small spear used to be planted for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would pray toward it; I think he said: while the riders would pass in front of him."
"7366","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Sinan narrated, Muhammad ibn Hammad narrated, Umar Abu Hafs narrated, from Alqamah, from Sulayman ibn Buraydah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say in his supplication: O Allah, guide me among those You guided, and grant me health among those You granted health, and befriend me among those You befriended, and bless for me what You gave, and protect me from the evil of what You decreed; for You decree and none decrees upon You, and he whom You befriend is never humiliated; blessed are You, our Lord, and exalted. These two hadiths were not narrated from Alqamah except by Umar Abu Hafs."
"7367","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Sinan narrated, Ya'qub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri narrated, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated, from Abd al-A'la ibn Umayyah ibn Wahb, from his father, from Aban ibn Uthman, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One in ihram shall not marry, nor propose, nor be proposed to. None narrated it from Abd al-A'la except Abd al-Aziz; Ya'qub was alone in transmitting it."
"7368","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Sinan narrated, Ali ibn Asim narrated, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abidah al-Salmani, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, he said: The Confederates distracted us on the day of the Trench from the Asr prayer, so he said: What is with them? May Allah fill their graves and houses with fire; they distracted us from the middle prayer until the sun set. This hadith was not narrated from Khalid al-Hadhdha except by Ali ibn Asim."
"7369","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Sinan narrated, Yazid ibn Harun narrated, Sulaym ibn Hayyan narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, Jabir ibn Abdullah narrated, that Mu'adh ibn Jabal used to pray with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then come to his people and pray with them. He prayed with them a prayer and recited al-Baqarah with them, so a man shortened and prayed a light prayer. That reached Mu'adh, and he said: He is a hypocrite. That reached the man, so he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are a people who work with our hands and draw water with our camels; Mu'adh prayed with us last night and recited al-Baqarah, so I shortened; he claimed I am a hypocrite. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Mu'adh, are you a causer of trial? Three times. O Mu'adh, recite: By the sun and its brightness, and: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and the like of them. This hadith was not narrated from Sulaym ibn Hayyan except by Yazid ibn Harun."
"7370","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Nasr ibn Ali narrated, my father narrated, al-Qasim ibn Ma'n narrated, Talhah ibn Yahya narrated, from Aishah bint Talhah and Mujahid, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to her and said: Do you have any food? I said: No. He said: I am fasting. He said: Then another day came, and Aishah said: O Messenger of Allah, hays has been gifted to us. He called for it and said: I had indeed woken up fasting today. This hadith was not narrated from al-Qasim ibn Ma'n except by Ali ibn Nasr; Nasr ibn Ali was alone in transmitting it."
"7371","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abadah al-Wasiti narrated, Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Saylahini narrated, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Hudhayfah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Do not drink in vessels of gold and silver, nor eat in them. This hadith was not narrated from Ibn Abi Najih except by Jarir ibn Hazim; Yahya ibn Ishaq was alone in transmitting it."
"7372","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Thabit al-Jahdari narrated, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated, from Umar ibn Sa'id, from Abu Zur'ah ibn Amr ibn Jarir, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked al-shikal in horses. This hadith was not narrated from Umar ibn Sa'id except by Sufyan ibn Uyaynah."
"7373","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Hafs ibn Amr al-Rabbali narrated, Umar ibn Habib the judge narrated, Salamah ibn Alqamah narrated, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever frees a portion of a slave while having wealth, all of him is freed; otherwise, what is freed of him is freed. This hadith was not narrated from Salamah ibn Alqamah except by Umar ibn Habib."
"7374","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Khidash narrated, Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Salamah, from Umm Salamah, she said: Evil omens were mentioned before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they said: In the house, the woman, and the mount. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If there is anything of it, it is in good omen. This hadith was not narrated from Abu Ishaq except by Yunus, nor from Yunus except by Abu Qutaybah; Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Khidash was alone in transmitting it."
"7375","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Thabit al-Jahdari narrated, Musa ibn Mas'ud narrated, Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated, from Ibrahim ibn Maysarah, he said: I heard Mujahid say: I heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Which tree among trees is like the Muslim man among people? Ibn Umar said: Nothing prevented me from asking him except that I was the youngest of the people. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is the date-palm. This hadith was not narrated from Ibrahim ibn Maysarah except by Muhammad ibn Muslim, nor from Muhammad ibn Muslim except by Abu Hudhayfah Musa ibn Mas'ud; Ahmad ibn Thabit was alone in transmitting it."
"7376","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Thabit narrated, Abu Hudhayfah Musa ibn Mas'ud narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Hanzalah, from Tawus, from Ibn Umar, I do not know it except from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Circumambulation is prayer, so speak little in it. This hadith was not narrated from Sufyan except by Abu Hudhayfah; Ahmad ibn Thabit was alone in transmitting it."
"7377","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abbad ibn Adam narrated, my father narrated, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Qatadah and Ayyub and Abdullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that Ka'b ibn Malik asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a slave-girl of his who slaughtered a sharitah (a sheep), and he said: Eat it. This hadith was not narrated from Qatadah except by Hammad ibn Salamah."
"7378","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Taymi the judge narrated, Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani narrated, Ubaydullah ibn Abi Ziyad narrated, Salim ibn Abdullah narrated, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever acquires a dog, a qirat decreases from his deed every day. This hadith was not narrated from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Ziyad except by Muhammad ibn Bakr."
"7379","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Mu'awiyah al-Hadhdha al-Wasiti narrated, my father narrated, Dawud ibn al-Zibriqan narrated, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the earnings of the cupper."
"7380","And with the same isnad: From the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): An angel calls out: O Allah, hasten for a spender a replacement, and for a withholder destruction. These two hadiths were not narrated from Muhammad ibn Juhadah except by Dawud ibn al-Zibriqan; Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Mu'awiyah, from his father, was alone in transmitting them."
"7381","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Makhlad al-Wasiti narrated, my father narrated, Sallam Abu al-Mundhir narrated, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from al-Ma'rur ibn Suwayd, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, he said: I heard the truthful and believed one (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrating from his Lord, blessed and exalted, he said: A good deed is ten or more, and an evil deed is one or I forgive it; and whoever meets Me, not associating anything with Me, with sins filling the earth, I grant him like it in forgiveness. None among those who narrated this hadith from Asim included between al-Ma'rur and Abu Dharr Abdullah ibn al-Samit except Sallam Abu al-Mundhir; Muhammad ibn Uthman, from his father, was alone in transmitting it."
"7382","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Makhlad narrated, he said: I found in my father's book, in his handwriting: Sallam Abu al-Mundhir narrated, from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came until, when at al-Ji'ranah, the people gathered upon him and his cloak caught on a tree. He said: Return my cloak to me; do you fear that I will not distribute among you? If I had livestock like the trees of Tihamah, I would distribute it among you, then you would not find me cowardly, nor miserly, nor lying. Then he said: Return the needle and thread, for misappropriation is shame and fire and disgrace upon its people on the Day of Resurrection. And he said: I have of this booty nothing like this hair, and he took it from the hump of the camel, except the fifth, and the fifth is returned to you. This hadith was not narrated from Sallam Abu al-Mundhir except by Uthman ibn Makhlad; his son was alone in transmitting it."
"7383","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Makhlad al-Wasiti narrated, he said: I found in my father's book, in his handwriting: Sallam narrated, from Asim ibn Bahdalah and Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, that the killer of al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam came seeking permission to enter upon Ali, and he said: Permit him and give him glad tidings of the Fire; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Every prophet has a disciple, and my disciple is al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam. This hadith was not narrated from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib and Asim, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, except by Sallam; Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Makhlad, from his father, was alone in transmitting it. And the people narrated it from Asim, from Zirr, from Ali."
"7384","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Shawdhab al-Wasiti narrated, Abu al-Musayyib Salm ibn Sallam narrated, Layth ibn Sa'd narrated, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Usamah ibn al-Had, from Ya'qub ibn Khalid, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The excess of the pleasure of the woman over the pleasure of the man is like the trace of a needle in clay, except that Allah covers them with modesty. This hadith was not narrated from Layth ibn Sa'd except by Abu al-Musayyib."
"7385","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Shawdhab narrated, Ya'qub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam narrated, from his father, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that your people are recent in disbelief, I would demolish the Ka'bah, then rebuild it upon the foundation of Ibrahim, and include in the House cubits of al-Hijr, and make for it two doors, leveling them with the ground. This hadith was not narrated from Zayd ibn Aslam except by his son; Ya'qub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri was alone in transmitting it."
"7386","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Shawdhab narrated, Abu al-Musayyib Sallam ibn Muslim narrated, Layth ibn Sa'd narrated, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, I think raised, he said: He is not of us who imitates others than us; do not imitate the Jews nor the Christians, for the greeting of the Jews is pointing with fingers, and the greeting of the Christians is with palms; and do not cut the forelocks, and trim the mustaches, and leave the beards; and do not walk in the mosques and markets while wearing shirts except with lower garments beneath them. This hadith was not narrated from Layth ibn Sa'd except by Abu al-Musayyib."
"7387","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Wahb al-Allaf narrated, Ya'qub ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami narrated, Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Ta'ifi narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ma'n ibn Muhammad al-Ghifari, from Hanzalah ibn Ali al-Aslami, from Abu Hurayrah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The grateful eater is like the patient fasting one. This hadith was not narrated from Ibn Jurayj except by Muhammad ibn Muslim, nor from Muhammad except by Ya'qub al-Hadrami; Ishaq ibn Wahb was alone in transmitting it."
"7388","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Wahb al-Allaf narrated, Muhammad ibn al-Qasim al-Asadi narrated, Mis'ar and Sufyan and Fitr and Khattab ibn Kaysan narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Juhayfah, he said: Ali stood upon the pulpit of Kufah and said: Shall I not inform you of the best of this Ummah after its Prophet? Indeed the best of this Ummah after its Prophet is Abu Bakr, then Umar; and had I wished to inform you of the third, I would have informed you. This hadith was not narrated from Mis'ar and Khattab ibn Kaysan except by Muhammad ibn al-Qasim; Ishaq ibn Wahb was alone in transmitting it."
"7389","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Wahb al-Allaf narrated, Umar ibn Yunus narrated, from Sulayman ibn Abi Sulayman, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in the Farewell Pilgrimage: Were it not that I had driven the sacrificial animal, I would have exited ihram; and he had entered ihram for Umrah and Hajj. They deem that the sacrificial animal prevented him from exiting his Umrah before his Hajj, while those of his Companions who had not driven a sacrificial animal had exited ihram."
"7390","And with the same isnad: From Urwah, from Aishah, that she informed him that she entered ihram in the Farewell Pilgrimage for Umrah before Hajj, and that she menstruated and was not purified to circumambulate the House until the day of Arafah; she mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Undo your head, then comb, then enter ihram for Hajj and leave the Umrah. So I did until I completed my Hajj. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent with me Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, and commanded me to perform Umrah from al-Tan'im in place of my Umrah which Hajj overtook and from which I had not exited ihram."
"7391","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Wahb al-Allaf narrated, Umar ibn Yunus narrated, from Sulayman ibn Abi Sulayman, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Nafi', from Nubayh ibn Wahb, from Aban ibn Uthman, he said: I heard Uthman say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One in ihram shall not marry, nor give in marriage, nor propose. These hadiths were not narrated from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir except by Sulayman ibn Abi Sulayman; Umar ibn Yunus was alone in transmitting them."
"7392","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Wahb al-Allaf narrated, Yazid ibn Harun narrated, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mujabbir narrated, Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Salih al-Samman, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and supplicated with a supplication the like of which people had not heard, and sought refuge with a seeking the like of which people had not heard. Some people said to him: How can we supplicate with the like of what you supplicated, and seek refuge as you sought refuge? He said: Say: O Allah, we ask You of what Muhammad, Your servant and Messenger, asked You, and we seek refuge of what Muhammad, Your servant and Messenger, sought refuge from. This hadith was not narrated from Ata ibn Yasar except by Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, nor from Ibn al-Munkadir except by Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mujabbir; Yazid ibn Harun was alone in transmitting it."
"7393","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Wahb al-Allaf narrated, Hafs ibn Umar al-Imam narrated, Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far narrated, from his father, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I missed dinner one night with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and missed that any of our brothers invite me. I prayed Isha, then wanted to sleep but could not, and wanted to pray but could not. There was a man at the chamber of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I went to him, and it was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying. He prayed, then leaned against the pillar toward which he had prayed, and said: Who is this? Abu Hirr? I said: Yes. He said: Did you miss dinner with us tonight? I said: Yes. He said: Go to the house and say: Bring the food you have. They gave me a tray with porridge of dates. I brought it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and placed it before him. He said to me: Call for me the people of the mosque. I said to myself: Woe to me, from what I see of the scarcity of food, and woe to me from disobedience; I go to a man sleeping and wake him, saying: Respond; and go to a man praying, saying: Respond; until they gathered before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He placed his fingers in it and pressed its sides, and said: Eat, in the name of Allah. They ate until full, and I ate until full. He said: Take it, O Abu Hirr, and return it to the family of Muhammad, for there is in the family of Muhammad no food eaten by a living creature other than it; an Ansari man gifted it to us. I took the tray and lifted it, and it was as it was when I placed it, except that in it were traces of the lines of the fingers of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). This hadith was not narrated from Amir ibn Sa'd except by Ja'far ibn Abdullah ibn al-Hakam, nor from Ja'far except by his son Abd al-Hamid, nor from Abd al-Hamid except by Hafs ibn Umar al-Imam; Ishaq ibn Wahb was alone in transmitting it."
"7394","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Wahb narrated, Hafs ibn Umar al-Imam narrated, Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated, from Abbad ibn Abi Ali, from Shaybah ibn al-Musawir, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prohibited six: wine, gambling, stringed instruments, flutes, the tambourine, and the kuba (drum). This hadith was not narrated from Shaybah ibn al-Musawir except by Abbad ibn Abi Ali, nor from Abbad except by Hisham; Hafs ibn Umar was alone in transmitting it."
"7395","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Wahb narrated, Ismail ibn Aban narrated, Amr ibn Thabit narrated, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that al-Harith ibn Hisham came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) once on the day of the Farewell Pilgrimage and said: O Messenger of Allah, you urge maintaining kinship, kindness to the neighbor, sheltering the orphan, feeding the guest, and feeding the poor; and all this Hisham ibn al-Mughirah used to do; what do you think of him, O Messenger of Allah? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every grave buried whose occupant does not testify that there is no god but Allah is a brand of Fire; and I found my uncle Abu Talib in a shallow pool of Fire, so Allah removed him due to his place with me and his kindness to me, and placed him in a shallow part of the Fire. This hadith was not narrated from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman except by Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, nor from Ibn Aqil except by Amr ibn Thabit; Ismail ibn Aban was alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Umm Salamah except with this isnad."
"7396","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ammar ibn Khalid al-Wasiti narrated to us, Abd al-Hakim ibn Mansur told us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Thabit al-Bunani who said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla narrating from Suhayb who said: We prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one of the two evening prayers, and when he finished he turned to us with his face smiling and said: Will you not ask me why I laughed? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: I marvel at Allah's decree for the Muslim servant; everything Allah decrees for him is good, and no decree of Allah is good except for the Muslim servant. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus ibn Ubayd except Abd al-Hakim ibn Mansur; Ammar ibn Khalid alone transmitted it."
"7397","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ammar ibn Khalid told us, Ali ibn Ghurab told us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not let the desert people dominate you over the name of your prayer; Allah named it al-Isha while they call it al-Atamah?"
"7398","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abbadah al-Wasiti told us, Yaqub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri told us, Hisham ibn Abd Allah ibn Ikrimah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah who said: In the morning I and Hafsah were both fasting, then a gift was given to us and we ate from it, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came in to us and we informed him of that, so he said: Make up a day in its place. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Hisham ibn Ikrimah; Yaqub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri alone transmitted it."
"7399","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Shuayb ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Wasiti told us, Yazid ibn Harun told us, Abd al-Malik ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The wedding feast on the first day is a duty, on the second day it is a kindness, and on the third day it is showing off and seeking repute. No one narrated this hadith from Mansur except Abd al-Malik ibn al-Husayn."
"7400","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abbadah al-Wasiti told us, Kathir ibn Hisham told us, Kulthum ibn Jawshan al-Qushayri narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The truthful trustworthy merchant will be with the martyrs on the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Kulthum ibn Jawshan; Kathir ibn Hisham alone transmitted it."
"7401","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Shuayb ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Wasiti told us, Musa ibn Ismail al-Jabbuli told us, Hashim ibn Subayh told us, Abu Anas al-Makki told us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No boy is born in a household except that honor comes among them which they did not have. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Abu Anas al-Makki - and his name is Imran ibn Anas - and no one narrated it from Abu Anas except Hashim ibn Subayh al-Wasiti; Musa ibn Ismail al-Jabbuli alone transmitted it."
"7402","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Abd Allah al-Kufi told us, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl told us, Hammad ibn Salamah told us, from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Numan ibn Bashir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The parable of a man and death is like that of a man who has three friends. One said: O Allah, this is my wealth, so take from it what You will, give what You will, and leave what You will. The other said: I am with you, I serve you, but when you die I will leave you. And the other said: I am with you, I enter with you and go out with you, whether you die or live. As for the one who said: This is my wealth, take from it what You will and leave what You will - that is his wealth. The other is his clan, and the other is his deed which enters with him and goes out with him wherever he is. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad ibn Salamah except al-Nadr ibn Shumayl."
"7403","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Wahb al-Allaf told us, Muhammad ibn al-Qasim al-Asadi told us, Zuhayr ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If people knew what I know about being alone, no rider would ever travel alone at night, and no man would sleep alone at night. No one narrated this hadith from Zuhayr ibn Muawiyah except Muhammad ibn al-Qasim."
"7404","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Wahb al-Allaf told us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Harun al-Ghassani told us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a servant tells a lie, the angel moves away from him the distance of a mile because of the stench of what he has brought. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi except Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad; Abd al-Rahim ibn Harun alone transmitted it."
"7405","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Harun Abu Alqamah al-Farwi told us, Yahya ibn Muhammad al-Jari told us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Raddad told us, from Abd Allah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs ghusl on Friday, then touches the best of his perfume, wears the best of his clothes, then goes out, does not separate between two people until he rises from his place, then listens attentively until the imam finishes his sermon, he is forgiven what is between the two Fridays plus three extra days."
"7406","And with the same chain: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Travel, you will be healthy and safe. Neither of these two hadiths was narrated from Abd Allah ibn Dinar except by Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Raddad."
"7407","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Harun al-Farwi told us, Yahya ibn Muhammad al-Jari told us, from Muhammad ibn Sadaqah al-Fadaki, from Abu Damrah, from his father, from his grandfather, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The shroud comes from the whole of the wealth. This hadith is not narrated from Ali except with this chain; Yahya al-Jari alone transmitted it."
"7408","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Rawh ibn Hatim Abu Ghassan al-Judhui told us, Amr ibn Sufyan al-Qutai narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Abi Jafar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best charity is that which is given out of sufficiency. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Juhadah except al-Hasan ibn Abi Jafar."
"7409","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Abd al-Quddus ibn Muhammad al-Habhabi narrated to us, Salih ibn Abd al-Kabir narrated to us, my uncle Abd al-Salam ibn Shuayb al-Habhabi told me, from his father, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Azd are the Azd of Allah on earth; people want to bring them down while Allah refuses except to raise them, and there will come upon people a time when a man will say: Would that my father were Azdi, would that my mother were Azdiyyah."
"7410","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Abd al-Quddus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, my father Muhammad ibn Abd al-Kabir ibn Shuayb told me, my uncle Abd al-Salam ibn Shuayb told me, from his father, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a cup - or a bowl - containing milk and honey, and he said: Two condiments in one vessel? I will not eat it, but I do not forbid it. Neither of these two hadiths was narrated from Shuayb ibn al-Habhab except by his son Abd al-Salam; Abd al-Quddus alone transmitted them, from his father."
"7411","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Abd al-Quddus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, my mother Habibah bint Mansur told me, Umm Sulaymah bint Shuayb ibn al-Habhab told me, from her father, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a woman perfumes herself for other than her husband, it is only fire in disgrace. This hadith is not narrated from Shuayb ibn al-Habhab except with this chain; Abd al-Quddus alone transmitted it."
"7412","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Abd al-Quddus ibn Muhammad told us, Said ibn Suwayd al-Mawali told us, Khalid ibn Ziyad - the dealer in sabiri cloth - told us, from Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji, from Abu Said al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of your dates is al-Barni; it removes illness and there is no illness in it. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Said except with this chain; Abd al-Quddus alone transmitted it."
"7413","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Abd al-Quddus ibn Muhammad told us, Amr ibn Asim al-Kilabi told us, Imran al-Qattan told us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Abd Allah ibn Abd Allah, the judge of al-Rayy, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Usayd ibn Hudayr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perform wudu from camel meat, do not pray in their resting places, do not perform wudu from sheep meat, and pray in their resting places. No one narrated this hadith from Imran except Amr ibn Asim."
"7414","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali told us, Musa ibn Mutayr told us, from Abu Ishaq who said: Al-Bara ibn Azib said to me: Shall I not teach you a supplication which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me? He said: When you see people competing over gold and silver, supplicate with these supplications: O Allah, I ask You for steadfastness in the matter, I ask You for resolve upon guidance, I ask You for gratitude for Your blessing, patience upon Your trial, I ask You for excellence in worshipping You, contentment with Your decree, I ask You for a sound heart and a truthful tongue, I ask You from the good of what You know, I seek refuge in You from the evil of what You know, and I seek Your forgiveness for what You know. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Musa ibn Mutayr; Ismail ibn Amr alone transmitted it."
"7415","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Abd al-Quddus ibn Muhammad told us, Nail ibn Najih told us, Ismail ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade wearing weapons in the lands of Islam on the two Eids, unless in the presence of his enemy. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Ismail ibn Ziyad, and none from Ismail except Nail; Abd al-Quddus alone transmitted it."
"7416","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Rawh ibn Hatim Abu Ghassan al-Judhui narrated to us, al-Minhal ibn Bahr told us, Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr told us, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two binding decrees are: whoever dies not associating anything with Allah enters Paradise, and whoever dies associating with Him enters the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Rabi except al-Minhal ibn Bahr."
"7417","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Rawh ibn Hatim Abu Ghassan told us, Musa ibn Masud Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A town-dweller must not sell for a desert-dweller, and whoever buys a musarrah animal has the choice of the two options: if he wishes he may return it along with a sa of dates. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Abi Najih except Muhammad ibn Muslim, and none from Muhammad ibn Muslim except Abu Hudhayfah; Rawh ibn Hatim alone transmitted it."
"7418","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bistam al-Zafarani narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Abu Amir al-Khazzaz narrated to us, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When one of you cleans himself with stones, let him use an odd number, for Allah is Odd and loves the odd. Do you not see the heavens are seven, and the days, and the earths are seven, and the tawaf, and the jamarat. And he mentioned other things. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Amir al-Khazzaz except Rawh; Ibrahim ibn Bistam alone transmitted it."
"7419","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Layth Abu al-Sabbah al-Haddadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Umar al-Rumi narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Said Abu Muslim, the guide of al-Amash, told us, from al-Amash, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abd Allah, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The Fire has been kindled and Paradise has been brought near, O people of the chambers; if you knew what I know you would laugh little and weep much. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Abu Muslim; Ibn al-Rumi alone transmitted it."
"7420","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Layth Abu al-Sabbah al-Haddadi told us, Abu Hammam al-Dallal told us, Dawud ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Attar narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No charity is better than the remembrance of Allah."
"7421","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali told us, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, al-Harish ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Khaythamah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Recite the Quran in a month. I said: I have strength. He said: Then recite it in three. No one narrated this hadith from Talhah ibn Musarrif except al-Harish ibn Sulaym, and none from al-Harish except Abu Dawud; Abu Hafs alone transmitted it."
"7422","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Umar ibn Abi Khalifah narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Mikhraq told me, from Abd Allah ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Muadh ibn Jabal and Abu Musa to Yemen and said: Support one another, obey one another, make things easy and do not drive people away. Then Muadh addressed the people, urging them to Islam and commanding them to understanding and the Quran, and said: Shall I inform you of the people of Paradise and the people of the Fire? When a man is mentioned with good, he is among the people of Paradise, and when he is mentioned with evil, he is among the people of the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from Ziyad ibn Mikhraq except Umar ibn Abi Khalifah."
"7423","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali told us, Kamil Abu al-Ala told us, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Zadham, from al-Bara ibn Azib who said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a funeral, and we reached the grave before it was dug as a lahd; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat and we sat around him - then he mentioned the hadith of the punishment of the grave."
"7424","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Wahb al-Allaf told us, Umar ibn Yunus al-Yamami narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abi Sulayman narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Qazah ibn Yahya, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a woman to travel with other than a mahram relative for more than three days. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir except Sulayman; Umar ibn Yunus alone transmitted it."
"7425","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Rawh ibn Hatim Abu Ghassan narrated to us, al-Minhal ibn Bahr narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr told us, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Deeds are presented on Monday and Thursday; whoever seeks forgiveness is forgiven, whoever repents is accepted, and the people of grudges are turned back for their grudges until they repent. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Rabi except al-Minhal ibn Bahr."
"7426","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abbad ibn Adam narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from his father who said: I heard Jubayr ibn Mutim saying: On the day of Hunayn we saw something black descending between the heaven and the earth; it fell to the earth and spread like ants, and it routed the polytheists."
"7427","And with the same chain: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Sirin, from Ibn Umar who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) beside the chamber of Aishah supplicating: O Allah, bless for us our mudd, bless for us our sa, bless for us our Sham and our Yemen. Then he faced the east and said: From here emerges the horn of Satan, earthquakes and tribulations, and from here are the loud-voiced harsh ones. Neither of these two hadiths was narrated from Hammad ibn Salamah except by Abbad ibn Adam; his son alone transmitted them."
"7428","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khalaf ibn Salih al-Basri told us, Muhriz ibn Bashshar told us, Salih al-Murri told me, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Forty traits by which Allah admits to Paradise; the highest of them in trait is the gift of a goat's milk. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Hassan except Salih al-Murri."
"7429","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Harb ibn Sinan ibn Jabalah al-Basri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar - Ghundar - told us, Said ibn Abi Arubah told us, from Abu Mashar, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to send the sacrificial animals, twisting their garlands, then he would not refrain from anything that the muhrim refrains from. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Mashar except Said ibn Abi Arubah."
"7430","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali told us, Israil narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that I would impose hardship upon my ummah, I would have commanded them to use the siwak at every prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Israil except Ismail ibn Amr."
"7431","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali told us, Abd al-Ghaffar ibn al-Qasim Abu Maryam told us, from Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani, from Hani ibn Hani and Hubayrah ibn Yarim, from Ali ibn Abi Talib who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wake his family in the last ten nights of Ramadan, and every young and old who could bear prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq, from Hani, except Abu Maryam; Ismail ibn Amr alone transmitted it. And the hadith of Hubayrah is with al-Thawri, Shubah and others."
"7432","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah told us, from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every prayer in which the Fatihat al-Kitab is not recited is deficient; it is deficient, it is deficient. No one narrated this hadith from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah except Ibn Lahiah; Ibn al-Muqri alone transmitted it, from his father."
"7433","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Muawiyah al-Hadhdha narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Tammar narrated to us, Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad narrated to us, from Dithar al-Qattan, from Abu Abd al-Rahim al-Kindi, from Zadham who said: I heard Ali saying: I prayed before the people. No one narrated this hadith from Dithar al-Qattan except Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad; Hafs ibn Umar al-Tammar alone transmitted it."
"7434","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Sulayman al-Shadhakuni narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Sulayman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from Imran ibn Kathir, from Abu Zurah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sufficient for you among the women of the worlds are four: Fatimah bint Muhammad, Khadijah bint Khuwaylid, Maryam bint Imran, and Asiyah bint Muzahim. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Juhadah except Dawud ibn Abi Sulayman; al-Shadhakuni alone transmitted it."
"7435","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Shadhakuni narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Sulayman narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not listen to anything as He listens to one chanting the Quran. No one narrated this hadith from Ali ibn Zayd except Dawud ibn Abi Sulayman; al-Shadhakuni alone transmitted it."
"7436","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Sulayman al-Shadhakuni told us, Hammad ibn Zayd told us, Ayyub told us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abd Allah ibn Masud who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears a binding oath deliberately in order to cut off thereby the wealth of a Muslim without right, he will meet Allah while He is angry with him. No one raised this hadith from Hammad ibn Zayd except al-Shadhakuni."
"7437","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, al-Shadhakuni narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah al-Harrani told us, Abu Abd al-Rahim Khalid ibn Yazid told us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Kab ibn Ujrah who said: A blind man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I hear the call to prayer, but perhaps I cannot find a guide and it is hard upon me; may I take a mosque in my house? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Does the call reach you? He said: Yes. He said: Then when you hear the call, respond. No one narrated this hadith from Adi ibn Thabit except Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah."
"7438","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Humayd ibn Masadah told us, Yunus ibn Arqam told us, al-Hasan ibn Salih told us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from Hakim ibn Jubayr, from Ibrahim al-Nakhai, from al-Aswad, from Aishah who said: We used to make nabidh for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a green jar. No one placed Ibrahim ibn Muhajir between al-Hasan ibn Salih and Hakim ibn Jubayr among those who narrated this hadith from al-Hasan ibn Salih except Yunus ibn Arqam; Humayd ibn Masadah alone transmitted it."
"7439","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Asfati narrated to us, Abu Yazid al-Kufi Bishr ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sawa told us, from Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from al-Qasim ibn Awf al-Shaybani, from Zayd ibn Arqam who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman must not withhold herself from her husband, even if she is upon a saddle. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Said ibn Abi Arubah, and none from Said except Muhammad ibn Sawa; al-Asfati alone transmitted it, from Bishr ibn Abd al-Malik."
"7440","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Fadl al-Khuraqi narrated to us, Abu Amir al-Aqadi told us, Abd Allah ibn Budayl ibn Warqa told us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was never given a choice between two matters except that he chose the easier of them, so long as it did not involve disobedience; and when it was disobedience he was the furthest of people from it."
"7441","And with the same chain: From Aishah, that she said: O Messenger of Allah, Aflah sought permission to enter upon me, yet only the wife of his brother nursed me? He said: Give him permission, for he is your uncle. Neither of these two hadiths from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah was narrated except by Abd Allah ibn Budayl; Abu Amir al-Aqadi alone transmitted them. And the companions of al-Zuhri narrated them from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr."
"7442","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Fadl al-Khuraqi narrated to us, Abu Amir al-Aqadi narrated to us, Adi ibn al-Fadl informed me, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the ghouls appear to you, call out the adhan, for when Satan hears the call he turns back with a farting sound. No one narrated this hadith from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih except Adi ibn al-Fadl; Abu Amir alone transmitted it."
"7443","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Mumin al-Wasiti told us, Attab ibn Harb told us, from Salih ibn Rustum Abu Amir al-Khazzaz, from al-Hasan, from Maqil ibn Yasar who said: I was holding a branch of a tree above the head of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was taking the pledge from the people, and he did not take their pledge unto death; he took their pledge that they would not flee. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Amir al-Khazzaz except Attab."
"7444","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali told us, Fudayl ibn Marzuq told us, from Atiyyah, from Abu Said who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dead person knows who washes him, who shrouds him, and who lowers him into his pit. No one narrated this hadith from Fudayl ibn Marzuq except Ismail ibn Amr."
"7445","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Suwayd al-Judhuyi told us, Amir ibn Mudrik told us, Fudayl ibn Marzuq told us, from Atiyyah, from Abu Said who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been given five things no prophet before me was given: I was sent to the red and the black, while a prophet was only sent to his people; I was aided with terror over a month's journey; the spoils of war were made lawful food for me though none before me was fed them; the earth was made for me a mosque and a purification; and there is no prophet except that he was given a supplication which he hastened, while I delayed my supplication as intercession for my ummah, and it will reach - if Allah wills - whoever dies not associating anything with Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Fudayl except Amir ibn Mudrik."
"7446","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abbadah al-Wasiti told us, Yaqub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri told us, Ishaq ibn Jafar ibn Muhammad told us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Aziz told us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham and Said ibn al-Musayyib and Abd Allah ibn Wahb ibn Zamah - some adding over others - from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the Muslims in Makkah when their kinsfolk had turned harsh against them: Disperse in the land. So they dispersed to the land of Abyssinia, and Quraysh sent Abd Allah ibn Abi Rabiah and Amr ibn al-As. Among what Amr and Abd Allah said to the Negus was: They do not greet you with the greeting that those of us who enter upon you greet you with. So he said to Jafar and his companions: Why do you not greet me as your companions greet me? They said: We greet you with the greeting of our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): peace; our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed us that it is the greeting of the people of Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib and Abd Allah ibn Wahb ibn Zamah, except Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Umami - from the descendants of Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf al-Ansari - and none narrated it from him except Ishaq ibn Jafar ibn Muhammad; Yaqub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri alone transmitted it. And Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman alone."
"7447","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Hassan al-Wasiti told us, Musa ibn Ismail al-Jabbuli told us, Jarir ibn Hazim told us, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to deliver the sermon leaning against a piece of wood, and when the minbar was made he went to ascend it, and the wood moaned; so he came down and touched it, and it became still. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan except Jarir ibn Hazim, and none from Jarir except Musa ibn Ismail."
"7448","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali told us, al-Hasan ibn Salih told us, from Musa ibn Abi Aishah, from Sulayman ibn Surad who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Use the siwak, clean yourselves, and make it odd, for Allah is Odd and loves the odd. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan ibn Salih except Ismail ibn Amr, and it is not narrated from Sulayman ibn Surad except with this chain."
"7449","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Khallad al-Wasiti told us, Yazid ibn Harun told us, Abu al-Miqdam Hisham ibn Ziyad narrated to us, saying: I heard Musa ibn Anas narrating from Anas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever has love for his brother in his soul, let him inform him of that. No one narrated this hadith from Musa ibn Anas except Hisham ibn Ziyad."
"7450","And with the same chain: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Bahr al-Saqqa told us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Salim, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Eat together and do not separate, for the food of one suffices two, and the food of two suffices four. O Allah, bless the people of Madinah in their sa and bless them in their mudd. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Dinar except Bahr al-Saqqa; Yazid ibn Harun alone transmitted it."
"7451","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Sad told us, Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Muslim ibn Khalid al-Zanji told us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fixed al-Aqiq as the miqat for the people of the east. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Muslim; Musa ibn Dawud alone transmitted it."
"7452","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ali ibn Hassan al-Attar told us, Yahya ibn Said al-Qattan told us, Qurrah ibn Khalid told us, from Ismail ibn Kathir, from Asim ibn Laqit ibn Sabirah, from his father - the delegate of Banu al-Muntafiq - that he came to Aishah, he and a companion of his, seeking the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) but did not find him, so Aishah fed us lunch of dates and asidah. It was not long before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, walking briskly and swaying. He said: Have you two eaten? We said: Yes. I said: O Messenger of Allah, about prayer? He said: Perform wudu thoroughly, run water between the fingers, and exaggerate in sniffing water into the nose unless you are fasting. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a wife - and he mentioned her foul tongue - he said: Divorce her. I said: She has companionship and children? He said: Then admonish her; if there is good in her she will respond, and do not beat your traveling wife as you beat your slave girl. While we were thus, the shepherd raised upon his hands in the pen a young goat. He said: Has it given birth? He said: Yes. He said: What? He said: A lamb. He said: Slaughter a sheep in its place. Then he turned to me and said: Do not think - and he did not say: do not deem - that we slaughtered it only for your sake; we have one hundred sheep and we do not like them to increase beyond that; when the shepherd delivers a lamb we command him to slaughter a sheep in its place. No one narrated this hadith from Qurrah ibn Khalid except Yahya ibn Said; Ali ibn Hassan alone transmitted it. If Ali ibn Hassan preserved it, it is strange from the hadith of Qurrah ibn Khalid, for others than Ali ibn Hassan narrated it from Yahya ibn Said, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ismail ibn Kathir."
"7453","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali told us, Israil told us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abd Allah who said: We used to eat with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and we would hear the tasbih of the food. No one narrated this hadith from Mansur except Israil; Ismail ibn Amr alone transmitted it."
"7454","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated to us, Abu Shihab narrated to us, from Habib ibn al-Shahid, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father, from Muadh ibn Jabal: he brought the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a riding animal for him to ride, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man has most right to the front of his animal. He said: O Messenger of Allah, it is yours. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rode and seated Muadh behind him. No one narrated this hadith from Habib ibn al-Shahid except Abu Shihab; Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali alone transmitted it."
"7455","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ismail ibn Amr narrated to us, Jarir told us, from Mughirah, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from Abu Masud al-Ansari who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: From what people have learned of prophethood: if you do not feel shame, do whatever you wish. No one narrated this hadith from Mughirah except Jarir; Ismail ibn Amr alone transmitted it."
"7456","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ismail ibn Amr narrated to us, Hushaym told us, from Zakariyya ibn Abi Maryam who said: I heard Abu Umamah al-Bahili saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah has made the fast of Ramadan obligatory upon you, and has not made its standing in prayer obligatory upon you; its standing is only something you innovated, so persist in it, for some people among the Children of Israel innovated an innovation and Allah blamed them for abandoning it, and He said: And monasticism they innovated; We did not prescribe it for them except seeking the pleasure of Allah, but they did not observe it with its due observance - to the end of the verse. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Umamah except with this chain; Ismail ibn Amr alone transmitted it."
"7457","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ismail ibn Amr narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When food is served and prayer is established, begin with the food. No one narrated this hadith from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih except Zuhayr; Ismail ibn Amr alone transmitted it."
"7458","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ismail ibn Amr narrated to us, Mindal narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sneezed he would cover his face and lower his voice. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Mindal; Ismail ibn Amr alone transmitted it."
"7459","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ismail ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Husayn ibn Qabisah, from Ali who said: I was a man who emitted much madhy, so I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: When you see madhy, wash your private part and perform wudu, and when you see gushing water, perform ghusl. No one narrated this hadith from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman except Zaidah; Ismail ibn Amr alone transmitted it. And others than Ismail narrated it from Zaidah, from Abu Hasin, from Husayn ibn Qabisah."
"7460","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ismail told us, Abu Bakr al-Nahshali narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Ibn Masud, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led the people in five rakahs. They said: O Messenger of Allah, has something been added to the prayer? He said: Why is that? They said: You prayed five. So he prostrated two prostrations. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad except Abu Bakr al-Nahshali; Ismail ibn Amr alone transmitted it. And Abu Nuaym and others narrated it from Abu Bakr al-Nahshali, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father. And Abu Attab al-Dallal and Abu Ghassan narrated it from Abu Bakr al-Nahshali, from al-Haytham, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abd Allah."
"7461","Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Ismail ibn Amr told us, Ismail ibn Ayyash told us, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Muadh ibn Jabal who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Adam descended to the earth he wept over Paradise for a hundred autumns, then he looked at the vastness of the earth and said: My Lord, does Your earth have no inhabitant dwelling in it besides me? So Allah revealed to him: Yes indeed, houses will be raised in which My name is mentioned, and I shall settle you in a house thereof which I single out with My honor, I imbue it with My greatness, and I name it My House, I make it speak with My greatness, yet I do not dwell in it, nor is it fitting for Me to dwell in houses nor can they contain Me; rather I am upon My Throne and the Kursi of My greatness, and nothing I created can escape My grasp nor My power. And you, Adam, shall maintain it as long as you live, then generations after you shall maintain it, nation after nation, generation after generation, until it reaches a son among your sons called Ibrahim; I shall make him among its maintainers and dwellers. This hadith was not narrated from Muadh ibn Jabal except with this chain; Ismail ibn Amr alone transmitted it."
"7462","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Washsha al-Asbahani narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Harish told us, Abd Allah ibn Raja told us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The imam is appointed only to be followed, so when he says takbir, say takbir, when he bows, bow, when he says: Allah hears whoever praises Him, say: O Allah, our Lord, to You belongs praise, when he prostrates, prostrate, and when he prays sitting, pray sitting. No one narrated this hadith from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar except Abd Allah ibn Raja al-Makki; Zayd ibn al-Harish alone transmitted it."
"7463","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Washsha narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Harish narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Zibriqan told us, from Hudbah ibn al-Minhal, from Qabus ibn Abi Zibyan, from his father, that he sent to Aishah asking her about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: He used to pray and leave off, but I never saw him leave the two rakahs before the dawn prayer, neither in travel nor residence, neither in health nor sickness. No one narrated this hadith from Hudbah ibn al-Minhal except Abu Hammam."
"7464","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Washsha narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Harish narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Fudayl told us, from Rishdin ibn Kurayb, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Ibn Abbas, two rakahs before the morning prayer: at the retreat of the stars, and two rakahs after Maghrib: after the prostrations. No one narrated this hadith from Rishdin ibn Kurayb except Muhammad ibn Fudayl."
"7465","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Washsha narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bazi told us, Fudayl ibn Sulayman told us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar narrated to us, saying: I heard Ayyub ibn Jarir ibn Abd Allah al-Bajali narrating from his father Jarir who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about wiping over the khuffs? He said: Three days for the traveler, and a day and night for the resident. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub ibn Jarir except Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar."
"7466","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Washsha narrated to us, Talut ibn Abbad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Warrad, the freedman of al-Mughirah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shubah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of gossip and hearsay, withholding and demanding, disobedience to mothers, burying daughters alive, and wasting wealth. No one narrated this hadith from Ata ibn al-Saib except Hammad ibn Salamah."
"7467","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Washsha narrated to us, Abu al-Ashath Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam told us, Asram ibn Hawshab narrated to us, Qurrah ibn Khalid narrated to us, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, from Tawus who said: I heard Abu al-Darda saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah has imposed obligations, so do not neglect them; He has set limits, so do not transgress them; He has remained silent about many things, not out of forgetfulness, so do not burden yourselves with them, as a mercy from Allah - so accept it. No one narrated this hadith from Qurrah ibn Khalid except Asram ibn Hawshab; Abu al-Ashath alone transmitted it."
"7468","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Washsha narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar - Ghundar - narrated to us, Shubah told us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My father is a very old man; if I carry him he cannot hold on? He said: Perform Hajj on behalf of your father."
"7469","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Washsha narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Abi Hafsah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, the like of it. No one narrated this hadith from Shubah, from Umarah, except Abu Asim; Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri alone transmitted it."
"7470","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Malik al-Dabbi al-Asbahani narrated to us, Zunayj Abu Ghassan told us, al-Hakam ibn Bashir ibn Salman narrated to us, Amr ibn Qays narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Abi Fakhitah, from his father who said: Ali took my hand and entered upon al-Hasan ibn Ali while he was ill, and Abu Musa was with him. He said: Visiting or returning? He said: Rather visiting. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No Muslim visits a Muslim except that Allah appoints for him seventy thousand angels praying for him, if in the evening until morning, and if in the morning until evening, and He makes for him chambers in Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Qays except al-Hakam ibn Bashir."
"7471","Muhammad ibn Shuayb al-Asbahani narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Mihraqani narrated to us, Hammad ibn Qirat told us, from Abu Jafar, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, when is the Hour? He said: What have you prepared for it? He said: By Allah, I have not prepared much deed for it, except that I love Allah and His Messenger. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A person is with whom he loves. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus ibn Ubayd except Abu Umarah and Abu Jafar - and he is Jasr ibn Farqad; Abd al-Hamid ibn Bayan alone transmitted it from Abu Umarah, and Hammad ibn Qirat alone transmitted it from Jasr."
"7472","Muhammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Mihraqani told us, al-Najm ibn Bashir told us, from Ismail ibn Sulayman - the brother of Ishaq ibn Sulayman - from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, from Ata, from Anas ibn Malik who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a garden, and a bird was brought, and he said: O Allah, bring me the most beloved of Your creation to You to eat with me from this bird. Then Ali came and knocked on the door. I said: Who is this? He said: I am Ali. I said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is attending to a need. He went away, then came and knocked on the door. I said: Who is it? He said: I am Ali. I said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is attending to a need. Then he came and knocked on the door, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go and open. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What kept you, may Allah have mercy on you? He said: This is the third time coming; each time Anas tells me: you are attending to a need. He said: O Anas, what carried you to do that? I said: I heard your supplication, so I wanted it to be a man from my people. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, from Ata, from Anas, except Ismail ibn Sulayman, and none narrated it from Ismail except al-Najm ibn Bashir; Hafs ibn Umar al-Mihraqani alone transmitted it."
"7473","Muhammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Mihraqani told us, al-Qasim ibn al-Hakam al-Urani narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn Murrah al-Jamali narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Suqah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir told us, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he went out one night having delayed the Isha prayer until a while or an hour had passed, while the people were waiting for him in the mosque. He said: What are you waiting for? They said: We are waiting for the prayer. He said: You will remain in prayer as long as you wait for it. Then he said: It is a prayer which none among the nations before you has prayed. Then he raised his head to the sky and said: The stars are the security of the sky; when the stars are effaced, there comes to the sky what it is promised. I am the security of my companions; when I am taken, there comes to my companions what they are promised. My companions are the security of my ummah; when my companions are taken, there comes to my ummah what they are promised. None narrated it from Muhammad ibn Suqah except Abd Allah ibn Amr; al-Qasim alone transmitted it."
"7474","Muhammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Salamah al-Razi told us, Salamah ibn al-Fadl told us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from al-Agharr - the Agharr of Muzaynah - who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had ordered for me a portion of dates held by a man of the Ansar, but he delayed me in it, so I spoke to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about him. He said: Go with him, O Abu Bakr, and take his dates for him. He said: Abu Bakr promised me at the mosque when we prayed Fajr; I found him where he had promised me, and we set out. Whenever a man saw Abu Bakr from afar he greeted him, so Abu Bakr said: Do you not see the bounty the people gain over you: no one precedes you in greeting. He said: So whenever a man appeared, we hastened to greet him before he greeted us. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi except Muhammad ibn Ishaq; Salamah ibn al-Fadl alone transmitted it."
"7475","Muhammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Salamah narrated to us, Salamah ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah who said: There was a woman of Banu Qurayzah called Tamimah - under Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Zubayr - and he divorced her, then Rifah - a man of Banu Qurayzah - married her, then separated from her, and she wanted to return to Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Zubayr. She said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, that from him is only like the fringe of my garment. He said: By Allah, O Tamimah, you shall not return to Abd al-Rahman until another man tastes your little honey. She said: O Messenger of Allah, he had already come to me once. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Ishaq except Salamah ibn al-Fadl."
"7476","Muhammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Salamah told us, Abu Zuhayr Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra told us, from Umar ibn Abd Allah ibn Yala ibn Murrah, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three things Allah loves: hastening the iftar, delaying the suhur, and striking one hand upon the other in prayer. This hadith is not narrated from Yala ibn Murrah except with this chain; Abu Zuhayr alone transmitted it."
"7477","Muhammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Salamah told us, Hammad ibn Qirat told us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: I have been given five which no prophet before me was given: spoils were made lawful for me though not lawful for any prophet before me; the earth was made for me a mosque and a purification, while those before us prayed in sanctuaries; I was sent to every black and red, while a man was sent only to his people; I was aided with terror over a month's journey ahead of me - a people a month's journey between me and them hear of me and are struck with fear of me - and terror was made victory for me; and it was said to me: Ask and you shall be given, so I made it intercession for my ummah, and it will reach whoever testifies that there is no god but Allah, not associating anything with Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Hassan except Hammad ibn Qirat."
"7478","Muhammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Umayr told us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sufficient for a man as faith is to say: I am pleased with Allah as Lord, with Muhammad as Messenger, and with Islam as religion. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Muhammad ibn Umayr al-Razi."
"7479","Muhammad narrated to us, Ahmad told us, Abd Allah ibn Abi Jafar al-Razi narrated to us, from his father, from al-Rabi ibn Anas, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Hudhayfah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not care about the affair of the Muslims is not of them, and whoever does not wake and sleep as a sincere adviser to Allah, His Messenger, His Book, his imam and the generality of Muslims is not of them. This hadith is not narrated from Hudhayfah except with this chain; Abd Allah ibn Abi Jafar al-Razi alone transmitted it."
"7480","And with the same chain: Abd Allah ibn Abi Jafar narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Ali ibn Abi Talib who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is grieved by his evil deed is a believer. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah except Muhammad ibn Kab, and none from Muhammad ibn Kab except Musa ibn Ubaydah; Abd Allah ibn Abi Jafar alone transmitted it."
"7481","Muhammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Dashtaki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Ali ibn Abi Ali al-Lahabi, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When Ibrahim was taken up, he saw a man committing adultery with a woman and supplicated against him, so he perished; then he saw a servant in disobedience and supplicated against him, so Allah revealed to him: O Ibrahim, whoever worships Me has from Me three traits: either he repents and I accept from him, or he seeks My forgiveness and I forgive him, or there emerges from his loins one who worships Me. O Ibrahim, do you not know that among My names is that I am al-Sabur. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir except Ali ibn Abi Ali; Ibn Abi Fudayk alone transmitted it."
"7482","Muhammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muqatil al-Razi narrated to us, Hakkam ibn Salm told us, from Abu Jafar al-Razi, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Aliyah who said: Abu Musa al-Ashari led us in the fear prayer at Isfahan though there was no great fear, to show us the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He stood and said takbir, and a group of the people said takbir with him, while a group faced the enemy with their weapons. He prayed with them one rakah, then they left and went to the station of their brothers, then the other group came and he prayed with them another rakah, then he gave salam, and each of them prayed the second rakah alone. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Abu Musa, except Abu Jafar al-Razi, and none from Abu Jafar except Hakkam; Muhammad ibn Muqatil alone transmitted it."
"7483","Muhammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us, Said ibn Anbasah al-Qattan narrated to us, Abu Ubaydah al-Haddad told us, Abu Hilal narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Buraydah, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The master of condiments in this world and the Hereafter is meat, the master of drinks in this world and the Hereafter is water, and the master of fragrant plants in this world and the Hereafter is al-faghiyah."
"7484","And with the same chain, Abu Ubaydah al-Haddad narrated to us, Wasil ibn Yazid ibn Wasil told us, my father and my uncles told me, from Malik ibn Umayr who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a poet; what do you think of poetry? He said: That what is between your collarbone and your pubic area be filled with pus and festering fluid is better than that it be filled with poetry. This hadith is not narrated from Malik ibn Umayr except with this chain; Said ibn Anbasah alone transmitted it."
"7485","Muhammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abi Surayj al-Razi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn al-Jahm told us, Amr ibn Abi Qays told us, from Umar ibn Qays al-Masir, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Umm Salamah who said: Quraysh were concerned about the affair of the Makhzumi woman who stole. They said: Who will speak to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about her? They said: Who dares upon him except Usamah ibn Zayd, the beloved of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? So they spoke to him about that, and he came to him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Those before you perished only because when the noble stole they left him, and when the weak stole they established the hadd upon him. By Allah, if it were Fatimah bint Muhammad, I would cut off her hand. So he cut off her hand. No one narrated this hadith from Umar ibn Qays al-Masir except Amr ibn Abi Qays. And Umar ibn Qays differed with the companions of al-Zuhri in the chain of this hadith, saying: from Urwah, from Umm Salamah. And the companions of al-Zuhri narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah."
"7486","Muhammad narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abi Surayj told us, Shuayb ibn Harb told us, Kamil Abu al-Ala narrated to us, Abu Salih told us, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman entered the Fire because of a cat of hers; she had tied it, neither feeding it nor letting it eat from the vermin of the earth. No one narrated this hadith from Kamil Abu al-Ala except Shuayb ibn Harb; Ahmad ibn Abi Surayj alone transmitted it."
"7487","Muhammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Salamah al-Razi told us, Abu Zuhayr Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra told us, Muhammad ibn Kurayb told us, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by two men tied together performing Hajj as a vow, and said: Remove your bonds. They said: O Messenger of Allah, it is a vow. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Remove your bonds, then perform Hajj. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Kurayb except Abu Zuhayr."
"7488","Muhammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Salamah told us, Abu Zuhayr told us, from Muhammad ibn Kurayb, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The adulterer does not commit adultery while he is a believer when he commits it, nor does the thief steal while he is a believer when he steals, nor does one plunder a plunder while the believers raise their heads toward him while he is a believer. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Kurayb except Abu Zuhayr."
"7489","Muhammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us, Yaqub al-Dashtaki told us, Hisham ibn Ubayd Allah al-Sinni told us, Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah and al-Aswad who said: Abd Allah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never performed qunut in any of the prayers except in al-Witr, but when he fought he would perform qunut in all the prayers, supplicating against the polytheists. And Abu Bakr, Umar and Uthman never performed qunut until they died. And Ali did not perform qunut until he fought the people of Sham; he would perform qunut in all the prayers, and Muawiyah would also supplicate against him - each of them supplicating against the other. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah and al-Aswad, from Abd Allah, except Muhammad ibn Jabir. And al-Hasan ibn al-Hurr narrated it from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Umar."
"7490","Muhammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Isa ibn Maysarah al-Razi narrated to us, al-Furat ibn Khalid narrated to us, Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us, saying: I heard Abu Awn Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah al-Thaqafi narrating from Warrad, the freedman of al-Mughirah ibn Shubah, that Muawiyah wrote to him - meaning al-Mughirah - asking him about what he heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he wrote to him, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah dislikes for you three things: disobedience to mothers, burying daughters alive, and withholding and demanding, gossip and hearsay, excessive questioning, and wasting wealth."
"7491","Muhammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Isa narrated to us, al-Furat ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Malik ibn Mighwal who said: I heard Ata ibn al-Saib mentioning from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Two traits are easy, yet few act upon them; none persists upon them except that he enters Paradise: after every prayer ten takbirs, ten tasbihs and ten tahmids - these are one hundred fifty on the tongue and one thousand five hundred on the scale - and when he retires to his bed he glorifies Allah thirty-three times, praises Him thirty-three times and magnifies Him thirty-four times - that is one hundred on the tongue and one thousand on the scale. So which of you commits two thousand five hundred sins in a day and night? Some said: This is a matter whose deed is easy. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Satan comes to one of you when he finishes his prayer and says: Remember the need of such and such and the need of such and such. Neither of these two hadiths from Malik ibn Mighwal was narrated except by al-Furat ibn Khalid and Muhammad ibn Sabiq."
"7492","Muhammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Isa told us, al-Furat ibn Khalid told us, from al-Dahhak ibn Uthman, from Yahya ibn Said, from al-Araj, from Ibn Buhaynah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood in the two rakahs of Zuhr, so the people clapped and glorified Allah to alert him, until he knew he had forgotten; he continued until his prayer was complete, then prostrated two prostrations while sitting before giving salam. No one narrated this hadith from al-Dahhak ibn Uthman except al-Furat ibn Khalid."
"7493","Muhammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Salamah al-Razi narrated to us, Abu Zuhayr Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra narrated to us, from al-Ajlah, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from his father, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wearing poor clothes and in bad appearance, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Do you have wealth? He said: Yes, of all kinds of wealth. He said: Then let what Allah has provided you be seen upon you. No one narrated this hadith from al-Ajlah except Abu Zuhayr."
"7494","Muhammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abi Surayj al-Razi told us, Amr ibn Mujammi told us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us not to stone the jamrah until the sun rises. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail except Amr ibn Mujammi; Ahmad ibn Abi Surayj alone transmitted it."
"7495","Muhammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Salamah told us, Abu Zuhayr told us, Wiqa ibn Iyas al-Walibi narrated to us, saying: I heard Suhayl ibn Dhakwan Abu Salih mentioning from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to the door of a man of the Ansar and greeted, while the Ansari was with his wife; he returned the greeting while upon her. Then he greeted a second time, and he returned the greeting but did not get up. Then he turned away when he did not permit him. The other got up before finishing and went out after the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking him. Abu Hurayrah said: So we came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was standing, and we gathered to him, and the man bathed in a river beside his house; he came having bathed. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He has bathed though ghusl was not obligatory upon him. Then the man came apologizing to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him of his affair. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You bathed though ghusl was not obligatory upon you. No one narrated this hadith from Wiqa except Abu Zuhayr; Abd al-Rahman ibn Salamah alone transmitted it."
"7496","Muhammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Salamah told us, Abu Zuhayr told us, Muhammad ibn Kurayb told us, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, from Sad ibn Ubadah who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My mother died without bequest and without charity; will it be accepted if I give charity on her behalf? He said: Yes. He said: Will it benefit her? He said: Yes, even with a burnt goat's trotter. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Kurayb except Abu Zuhayr."
"7497","And with the same chain: From Muhammad ibn Kurayb, from his father who said: I witnessed al-Ahnaf ibn Qays narrating from his uncle - and his uncle is Jariyah ibn Qudamah - that he said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me a saying by which Allah benefits me, and make it brief so that I may grasp it. He said: Do not become angry. Then he repeated, and he said: Do not become angry. No one narrated this hadith from Kurayb except his son Muhammad; Abu Zuhayr alone transmitted it. And the well-known version is from the hadith of Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Jariyah ibn Qudamah."
"7498","Muhammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Asim al-Razi narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father told me, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Hittan ibn Abd Allah al-Raqashi, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was given al-kafit. It was said to al-Hasan: What is al-kafit? He said: Intercourse. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, except Hisham, and none from Hisham except his son; Abd al-Salam ibn Asim alone transmitted it."
"7499","Muhammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Salamah told us, Abu Zuhayr told us, al-Hasan ibn Salim ibn Abi al-Jad told us, saying: I heard Nuaym ibn Abi Hind, Ribi ibn Hirash narrated to us, Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman told me, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I have been given verses from a house of treasure beneath the Throne, which no prophet before me was given, nor shall anyone after me be given them; the earth was made for me a mosque and a purification; our rows were made like the rows of the angels; and I was aided with terror over a month's journey. Then he recited the verses from the end of al-Baqarah: To Allah belongs what is in the heavens and what is on earth, until he sealed the surah. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan ibn Salim ibn Abi al-Jad except Abu Zuhayr."
"7500","Muhammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Dimashqi told us, al-Harith ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Bahr al-Saqqa, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, that a man of Thaqif - called Ghaylan ibn Salamah - embraced Islam while having ten wives, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to choose four of them and leave six."
"7501","And with the same chain: From al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah who said: We fasted the day of Ashura before Allah made the fast of Ramadan obligatory; when Allah made the fast of Ramadan obligatory, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever of you wishes, let him fast it, and whoever wishes, let him leave it. And it was a day on which the Kabah was covered."
"7502","And with the same chain: From Bahr al-Saqqa, from Juwaybir, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The siwak is a purification for the mouth, pleasing to the Lord, and a clarity for the sight. None of these hadiths from Bahr al-Saqqa was narrated except by al-Harith ibn Muslim."
"7503","Muhammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Asim al-Razi told us, al-Sabbah ibn Muharib told us, Dawud al-Awdi narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If bad omen is in anything, it is in the house, the woman and the horse. No one narrated this hadith from Dawud al-Awdi except al-Sabbah ibn Muharib."
"7504","Muhammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Salamah al-Razi narrated to us, Abu Zuhayr said: al-Mufaddal ibn Fudalah said: We were discussing righteousness with Abu Harb ibn Abi al-Aswad al-Dili, and Abu Harb said: We were discussing righteousness with Imran ibn Husayn, and he said: We were discussing righteousness with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he began narrating to us. He said: Among the nations before you there was a devout man, a man of a hermitage, called Jurayj. He had a wife - or a mother - who would come to him and call him, and he would look down upon her and speak to her. One day she came to him while he was in his prayer turned to it, and she called him - and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) imitated her, placing his hand upon his forehead - she kept calling him, raising her head to him, placing her hand upon her forehead: O Jurayj, O Jurayj, three times, each time thrice; each time Jurayj would say: My Lord, my mother or my prayer? So she became angry and said: O Allah, let Jurayj not die until he looks upon the faces of prostitutes. He said: And the daughter of the village chief attained maturity, became pregnant and gave birth to a boy. They said to her: Who did this to you? Who is your companion? She said: He is the man of the hermitage, Jurayj. Jurayj did not realize until he heard axes at the base of his hermitage. He kept asking them: Woe to you, what is wrong with you? But they did not answer him. When he saw that, he took a rope and let himself down. They began pulling his nose, beating him and saying: A show-off deceiving people with your deed. He said: Woe to you, what is wrong with you?! They said: The daughter of the village chief, the king's daughter whom you impregnated? He said: What did she do? They said: She gave birth to a boy. He said: Is the boy alive? They said: Yes. He said: Then turn away from me. So he turned aside, prayed two rakahs, then walked to a tree, took a branch from it, then came to the boy while he was in his cradle, struck him with that branch and said: O insolent one, who is your father? He said: My father is so-and-so the shepherd. They said: If you wish we shall build your hermitage for you of gold, and if you wish of silver. He said: Restore it as it was. Abu Harb claimed that none spoke in the cradle except three: Isa son of Maryam, the witness of Yusuf, and the companion of Jurayj. No one narrated this hadith from Mufaddal ibn Fudalah - and he is the brother of al-Mubarak - except Abu Zuhayr, and it is not narrated from Imran ibn Husayn except with this chain."
"7505","And with the same chain: al-Mufaddal ibn Fudalah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik who said: On the day of Uhud the people of Madinah scattered in flight; they said: Muhammad has been killed, until wailing increased in the quarters of Madinah. A woman of the Ansar went out girded, and she was met with her son, her father, her husband and her brother - I do not know with which of them she was met first - and when she passed by the last of them she said: Who is this? They said: Your father, your brother, your husband, your son. She would say: What happened to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? They would say: Ahead of you. Until she was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); she seized the edge of his garment, then said: May my father and mother be ransom for you, O Messenger of Allah; I do not care, since you are safe, who perishes. No one narrated this hadith from Thabit except al-Mufaddal ibn Fudalah; Abu Zuhayr alone transmitted it."
"7506","Muhammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Salamah narrated to us, Abu Zuhayr Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra narrated to us, from al-Mufaddal ibn Fudalah, from Bakr ibn Abd Allah al-Muzani, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the bygone nations there was a man called Muwarriq, and he was devout. While he was standing in his prayer he thought of women, desired them, and became aroused until he broke his prayer. He became angry, took his bow, cut its string, tied it to his testicles, fastened it to his heels, then stretched his legs and tore them out. Then he took his two worn garments and his sandals until he came to a land with neither human nor beast, made a trellis, then stood praying. Each morning the earth would split open for him and there would emerge something with a vessel of food in it, and he would eat until full; then it would enter and emerge with a vessel of drink, and he would drink until quenched; then it would enter and the earth would close. In the evening the like of that would happen. He said: And some people passed near him; two men of the company came to him under the night and asked him about their destination, and he pointed to them with his hand: This is your destination, and: This is your destination where you intend. They walked a short distance; one of them said: What keeps this man here, a land with neither human nor beast? If we returned to him to learn his affair. So they returned and said to him: O servant of Allah, what keeps you in this place, in a land with neither human nor beast? He said: Go about your business and leave me. They refused and insisted upon him. He said: I shall inform you on condition that whoever of you conceals it for me, Allah honors him in this world and the Hereafter, and whoever of you discloses it about me, Allah humiliates him in this world and the Hereafter. They said: Yes. So they alighted; in the morning the thing emerged from the earth with the like of what used to emerge of food and twice as much with it, and they ate until full; then it entered and emerged to them with drink in a vessel like what used to emerge every day and twice as much with it, and they drank until quenched; then it entered and the earth closed. One of them looked at his companion and said: Why should we hasten! This is food and drink, and we know our path from the land; stay until evening. They stayed, and in the evening there emerged to them of food and drink the like of what emerged at the start of the day. One of them said to his companion: Stay with us until morning. They stayed; in the morning the like of that emerged to them. Then they rode off. One of them stayed at the king's door until he became among his intimates and evening companions, while the other turned to his trade and work. That king would not let anyone among his kingdom in his time tell a known lie except that he crucified him. One night while they were in evening company narrating to him of the wonders they had seen, that man began speaking. He said: I shall narrate to you, O king, a hadith the like of whose wonder you never heard. He narrated the story of that man whose affair he had seen. The king said: I never heard a greater lie than this; by Allah, you shall bring me proof for what you said or I shall crucify you. He said: My proof is so-and-so. He said: Agreed; bring him to me. When he came, the king said to him: This one says you two passed by a man, then such and such happened of his affair? The man said: O king, do you not know this is a lie, and this is what cannot be? Had I narrated this to you, would it be right upon you to crucify me for it? He said: You have spoken truth and done right. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So he admitted the man who had concealed it for him into his intimates and evening company, and ordered the other to be crucified. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for the one of them who concealed it for him, Allah has honored him in this world and the Hereafter; as for the one who disclosed it about him, Allah has humiliated him in this world and will humiliate him in the Hereafter. Then Bakr ibn Abd Allah looked at Thumamah ibn Abd Allah ibn Anas and said: O Abu al-Muthanna, did you hear your grandfather narrating this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes."
"7507","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Rustah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Imran al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi told us, Hisham ibn Ziyad told me, from his brother al-Walid ibn Ziyad, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Part of a man's righteousness to his father after his death is preserving the family of his father's loved ones after him. No one narrated this hadith from al-Walid ibn Ziyad except his brother; Abu Dawud alone transmitted it."
"7508","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Rustah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Sayrafi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Yusuf al-Azraq told us, from Abu Janab al-Kalbi, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awsajah, from al-Bara ibn Azib who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts a day without breaking it, ten good deeds are written for him. No one narrated this hadith from Talhah ibn Musarrif except Abu Janab, and none from Abu Janab except Ishaq al-Azraq; Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Wahhab alone transmitted it."
"7509","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Rustah narrated to us, Amr ibn Malik al-Rasibi told us, Fudayl ibn Sulayman told us, Yazid ibn Said ibn Abi al-Yasar narrated to us, my father told me, from his father who said: Muadh said: O Messenger of Allah, command me a deed that admits me to Paradise. He said: Believe in Allah, speak good and it will be written for you, and do not speak evil lest it be written against you. He said: Are we taken to account for what we speak? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And does anything throw people upon their nostrils into the Fire except the harvests of their tongues? This hadith is not narrated from Abu al-Yasar ibn Amr except with this chain; Amr ibn Malik alone transmitted it."
"7510","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Rustah narrated to us, Amr ibn Malik al-Rasibi told us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Masmul told us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Sabrah told us, al-Qasim ibn Abi Ashmat informed me, my father told me, from my grandfather Hisl - one of Banu Amir ibn Luayy - who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed during his Hajj - while we were with him - by a man who had finished his Hajj, and said to him: Is your Hajj accepted and sound for you? He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Begin deeds anew. This hadith is not narrated from Hisl except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Masmul alone transmitted it."
"7511","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Rustah narrated to us, Said ibn Abi al-Rabi al-Samman told us, Ziyad ibn Maymun told us, Hisham ibn Hassan told me, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is invited to a wedding feast and does not respond has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham except Ziyad ibn Maymun; Said ibn Abi al-Rabi alone transmitted it."
"7512","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Rustah narrated to us, Huraym ibn Abd al-Ala told us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman told us, saying: I heard my father narrating from Qatadah, from Abu al-Hajjaj, from Abu Musa al-Ashari who said: A man came once and sought permission, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Permit him and give him glad tidings of Paradise; and it was Abu Bakr. Then another man came, and he said: Permit him and give him glad tidings of Paradise; and it was Umar. Then another came and sought permission, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Permit him and give him glad tidings of Paradise despite a trial - or as he said. Uthman said: I ask Allah for patience. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah, from Abu al-Hajjaj, except Sulayman al-Taymi. And Mamar narrated it from Qatadah, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi."
"7513","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Rustah narrated to us, Said ibn Abi al-Rabi al-Samman told us, Said ibn Salamah ibn Abi al-Husam told us, Sharik ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Namir told us, from Anas ibn Malik, that water was scarce in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); in summer the people would pray Zuhr then go out to seek coolness. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr, then went out and they went out with him to the courtyard of the mosque; he stayed until when it was time for the call he sent me to the house of Umm Salamah to bring him wudu water. I entered and brought him a cup containing two-thirds or half of it; he performed wudu, and when he finished his wudu there remained in the cup some leftover of his wudu. He raised his head and saw the people standing, and said: Who are these? Anas said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, they find no water for wudu. He said: Call them. I did so, and the people came; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) put his hand into the cup in the leftover that remained of his wudu. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, none of them remained except that he performed wudu from what was in the palm of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a leftover remained in the cup; I returned with it to the house. No one narrated this hadith from Sharik ibn Abi Namir except Said ibn Salamah."
"7514","And with the same chain: Said ibn Salamah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Khusayfah told us, from Ibn Salamah ibn al-Akwa, from Salamah who said: I used to travel with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I never saw him pray after Asr nor after Fajr at all. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Salamah except Yazid ibn Khusayfah; Said ibn Salamah alone transmitted it."
"7515","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Rustah narrated to us, Said ibn Abi al-Rabi al-Samman told us, Muhammad ibn Dinar told us, Khalid ibn Dhakwan told us, Bushayr ibn Kab narrated to us, from Abu Dharr, that he was asked: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shake hands? He said: Never did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) meet me and I greeted him except that he shook my hand, except one time and it was the best of them: I entered upon him while he was ill, bent over him, and he embraced me. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Dharr except with this chain; Said ibn Abi al-Rabi alone transmitted it."
"7516","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Rustah narrated to us, Said ibn Abi al-Rabi told us, Muhammad ibn Dinar told us, Sad ibn Aws told us, Sayyar ibn Mikhraq narrated to us, saying: I asked Ibn Umar about the fasting of the traveler? He said: The Messenger of Allah set out when fourteen nights of Ramadan had passed; he made his camel kneel, placed one of his legs in the stirrup and the other on the ground, then called for milk from its milk and drank. No one narrated this hadith from Sayyar ibn Mikhraq except Sad ibn Aws, and none from Sad except Muhammad ibn Dinar; Said ibn Abi al-Rabi alone transmitted it."
"7517","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Rustah narrated to us, Said ibn Abi al-Rabi told us, Said ibn Salamah ibn Abi al-Husam told us, Yazid ibn Khusayfah told me, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Ibn Umar, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever withdraws his hand from the congregation comes on the Day of Resurrection with no proof for him, and whoever dies in other than obedience dies a death of ignorance. No one narrated this hadith from Yazid ibn al-Asamm except Yazid ibn Khusayfah, and none from Yazid except Said ibn Salamah; Said ibn Abi al-Rabi alone transmitted it."
"7518","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Rustah narrated to us, Sulayman al-Shadhakuni told us, Abu Umayyah ibn Yala told us, Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir told us, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade three riding upon one animal. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir except Abu Umayyah ibn Yala; al-Shadhakuni alone transmitted it."
"7519","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Rustah narrated to us, al-Shadhakuni told us, al-Nadr ibn Ismail al-Bajali told us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Dawud, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Spittle in the mosque is a sin, and its expiation is burying it. No one narrated this hadith from Dawud ibn Ali except Ibn Abi Layla, and none from Ibn Abi Layla except al-Nadr ibn Ismail; al-Shadhakuni alone transmitted it."
"7520","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Rustah narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh told us, Isa ibn Maymun told us, from Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi, from Ibn Abbas - and from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Umar - who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out with his head bandaged, ascended the steps of the minbar and said: What are these books which I hear you write? A book alongside the Book of Allah? It is near that Allah becomes angry for His Book and it is taken away by night, leaving not a letter of it in a paper nor in a heart except taken away. One who attended the gathering said: Then how, O Messenger of Allah, with the believing men and believing women? He said: Whoever Allah intends good for, He keeps in his heart: there is no god but Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Aslam except Isa ibn Maymun; Shayban alone transmitted it."
"7521","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Rustah narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Shadhakuni told us, Abd Allah ibn Idris told us, from his father, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a horse called al-Murtajiz. No one narrated this hadith from Adi except Idris, and none from Idris except his son; al-Shadhakuni alone transmitted it."
"7522","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Rustah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr al-Uruqi told us, Yaqub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri told us, Ishaq ibn Jafar told me, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Kinani told me, from Amir ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from Abu Lubabah ibn Abd al-Mundhir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he intended to enter a town, would not enter it until he said: O Allah, Lord of the seven heavens and what they shade, Lord of the seven earths and what they bear, Lord of the winds and what they scatter, Lord of the devils and what they mislead; I ask You its good and the good of what is in it, and I seek refuge in You from its evil and the evil of what is in it. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Lubabah except with this chain; Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr al-Uruqi alone transmitted it."
"7523","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Rustah narrated to us, Abu Kamil al-Jahdari told us, Abu Awanah told us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Fatimah bint al-Mundhir, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Nothing of breastfeeding prohibits except what opens the intestines and becomes in the body like food. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Abu Awanah; Abu Kamil alone transmitted it."
"7524","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Rustah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Salm ibn Rashid told us, Umar ibn Habib al-Qadi told us, Hisham ibn Urwah told us, from his father, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has two daughters, two sisters, two paternal aunts or two maternal aunts and maintains them, the eight gates of Paradise are opened for him: O servants of Allah, aid him; O servants of Allah, give him; O servants of Allah, lend him."
"7525","And with the same chain: From Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever brings joy to a Muslim household, Allah is not pleased with a reward for him less than Paradise. Neither of these two hadiths from Hisham ibn Urwah was narrated except by Umar ibn Habib; Ibrahim ibn Salm alone transmitted them."
"7526","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Rustah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Salm told us, Hashim ibn Musa al-Khassaf told us, Sulayman ibn Ali ibn Abd Allah ibn Abbas told us, my father told me, from my grandfather who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever spends the evening weary from the work of his hands spends the evening forgiven. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain; Ibrahim ibn Salm alone transmitted it."
"7527","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Rustah narrated to us, Zunayj Abu Ghassan told us, Ishaq ibn Sulayman told us, from al-Mughirah ibn Muslim, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to prostrate upon seven bones. No one narrated this hadith from al-Mughirah ibn Muslim except Ishaq ibn Sulayman."
"7528","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Rustah narrated to us, Zunayj told us, Ishaq told us, from Ibrahim ibn Yazid, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: We would eat and drink and give the charity of al-Fitr, then go out to the prayer place. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Dinar except Ibrahim ibn Yazid; Ishaq ibn Sulayman alone transmitted it."
"7529","Muhammad narrated to us, Zunayj told us, Ishaq told us, from al-Mughirah ibn Ziyad, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: On Friday the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would stand upon the minbar twice and sit twice: when he came out he sat, when the muadhdhin called he stood and delivered the sermon, then sat and rested, then stood and delivered the sermon. No one narrated this hadith from al-Mughirah ibn Ziyad except Ishaq ibn Sulayman."
"7530","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Rustah narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Imran told us, Abd Allah ibn Nafi told us, Mamar ibn Abd al-Rahman told me, from Ibn Qusayyt, from Abu Hurayrah who said: Bilal came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to announce the Fajr prayer to him, and he said: Command Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. He returned to him and saw heaviness in him, so he said: Command Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. He went and called the adhan, adding to his adhan: Prayer is better than sleep. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What is this you added to your adhan? He said: I saw heaviness in you and wanted you to become active. He said: Go and add it to your adhan, and command Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Qusayyt except Mamar, and none from Mamar except Abd Allah ibn Nafi."
"7531","Muhammad ibn Rashid ibn Yazid al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Shubah told us, from al-Amash, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited this verse: Fear Allah as He should be feared, and do not die except as Muslims. Then he said: If a drop of Zaqqum were to drip into the seas of the world, it would spoil the livelihoods of the people of the world; so how about one whose food it is? No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Shubah."
"7532","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Shabib al-Assal al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali told us, Abu Maryam Abd al-Ghaffar ibn al-Qasim told us, Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad told us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla who said: Ammar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: The rebellious party will kill you. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla except Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad; Abu Maryam alone transmitted it."
"7533","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Shabib told us, Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated to us, Zaidah told us, from Mansur, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: A she-camel struck and killed a muhrim man, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wash him with water and lote, shroud him in his two garments, do not apply hanut to him, do not cover his face, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection saying labbayk. No one narrated this hadith from Mansur except Zaidah; Ismail ibn Amr alone transmitted it."
"7534","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Assal narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Shami told us, al-Walid ibn Muslim told us, al-Awzai told us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No disciplinary beating above ten lashes. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awzai except al-Walid; Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Shami alone transmitted it."
"7535","And with the same chain: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no servant upon whom Allah bestows a blessing and completes it for him, then makes some of people's needs depend upon him, yet he grows weary of it, except that he exposes that blessing to removal. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except al-Walid and Muhammad ibn Marwan al-Suddi; Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Shami alone transmitted it from al-Walid."
"7536","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Assal narrated to us, Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali told us, Abu al-Ahwas told us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It suffices one of you to place his hand upon his thigh and greet his brother to his right: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, and to his left the like of that. No one narrated this hadith from Simak except Abu al-Ahwas; Ismail ibn Amr alone transmitted it."
"7537","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Assal narrated to us, Ismail ibn Amr told us, Muhammad ibn Marwan told us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Everything has an adornment, and the adornment of the Quran is a beautiful voice. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Muhammad ibn Marwan."
"7538","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim told us, Ismail told us, Abu al-Ahwas told us, from Layth, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever conceals knowledge he has, Allah will bridle him on the Day of Resurrection with a bridle of fire. No one narrated this hadith from Layth except Abu al-Ahwas; Ismail ibn Amr alone transmitted it."
"7539","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim told us, Ismail told us, Abu Maryam told us, Iyas ibn Salamah ibn al-Akwa told me, from Muslim ibn Jarhad who said: Ibn Umar fell ill, and a man said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, the deserts have grown green; if you bought goats and went out to the countryside you would recover. He said: None of us was permitted open country life except Aslam. None narrated from Muslim ibn Jarhad a hadith from Ibn Umar other than this, and none narrated it from Muslim except Iyas ibn Salamah; Abu Maryam alone transmitted it."
"7540","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim told us, Ismail told us, Hammad ibn Shuayb told us, from Mansur and al-Amash, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If one of you, when he comes to his wife, says: O Allah, keep us away from Satan and keep Satan away from what You provide us, and a child is decreed between them, Satan never harms him. None among those who narrated it from al-Amash raised it except Hammad ibn Shuayb."
"7541","Muhammad narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Muslim ibn Subayh, from Masruq, from Aishah, who said: Sheep were gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from al-A'mash from Abu al-Duha except Sharik. And people narrate it from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah."
"7542","Muhammad narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Hani, from Majid al-Hanafi, from Ibn Mas'ud, who said: We asked our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about walking with the funeral bier, and he said: Walking with it is less than trotting; if it is good, he is hastened to it, and if it is evil, then away with the companions of the Fire. And the funeral bier is to be followed and does not follow. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Hani except Sharik; Ismail ibn Amr was alone in transmitting it. And the well-known version is from the hadith of Yahya ibn al-Harith al-Taymi al-Jabir - also called al-Mujabbir, who used to set bones - and in this hadith he said: from Majid, though it is really Abu Majid."
"7543","Muhammad narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Umayr ibn Abdillah, from Salit ibn Abdillah, from Dhuhayl ibn Awf, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we came upon camels with tied-up udders sheltering by the trees, with no herdsman with them. Some of us said: If only we got up and milked them; others said: How can we milk them while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is among us and we have not sought his permission? Some of us said: He has kept silent, and his silence is permission. So we got up to them, but he called us back and said: What would you think if people came to you while you were asleep and took what was in your provision bags - would that harm you? They said: Yes. He said: Then what is in the udders of these camels is like what is in your provision bags. We said: O Messenger of Allah, what is lawful for a man from his brother's property when he is in need of it? He said: He may eat but not carry away, and he may drink but not carry away. No one narrated this hadith from Umayr ibn Abdillah except Qays ibn al-Rabi'."
"7544","Muhammad narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever begs from people in order to increase his wealth, it is only a coal from Hell; so whoever wishes, let him take much, and whoever wishes, let him take little. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Husayn except Qays."
"7545","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Habib ibn Hassan, from Urwah, from Aishah, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, he would follow every prescribed prayer with two rak'ahs, except the dawn prayer, for he would place them before it. No one narrated this hadith from Habib ibn Hassan except Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman."
"7546","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Assal narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Shadhakuni narrated to us, Ubays ibn Maymun narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to me, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fever is the believer's share of the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Ubays ibn Maymun; al-Shadhakuni was alone in transmitting it."
"7547","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Khalid ibn Nafi' al-Ash'ari narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Burdah narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Musa, that Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan said to him: Did you not know that when two disputants brought their dispute to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and they set an appointment, then one of them came and the other did not come, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would judge for the one who came against the one who did not come? So Abu Musa said: That was only about a riding animal, a sheep, and a camel; but what we are engaged in is the affair of the people. No one narrated this hadith from Sa'id ibn Abi Burdah except Khalid ibn Nafi'."
"7548","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, al-Shadhakuni narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Masmul al-Makhzumi narrated to us, who said: I heard al-Qasim ibn Mukhawwal al-Bahzi saying: I heard my father saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spent the evening narrating to us, and he said: A time will come upon people when the best wealth of people will be sheep between trees, eating from the trees and coming to the waters; their owners will eat from their milk yield, drink from their milk, and wear from their hair - or he said: from their wool - while tribulations sink down among the germs of the Arabs; they will be put to trial, by Allah, they will be put to trial, by Allah, they will be put to trial, by Allah - the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying it three times. This hadith is not narrated from Mukhawwal al-Bahzi except with this chain; al-Shadhakuni was alone in transmitting it."
"7549","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, al-Shadhakuni narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Bab ibn Umayr, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the prayer of fear with one of the two groups one rak'ah, then the other group came forward and he prayed with them one rak'ah, then he prostrated two prostrations. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awza'i except Isa ibn Yunus; al-Shadhakuni was alone in transmitting it."
"7550","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, al-Shadhakuni narrated to us, Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Abdillah al-Hadadi narrated to us - and he was trustworthy - from Abu al-Ala, who heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The best of the believers is a man who is easy in selling, easy in buying, easy in settling debts, and easy in seeking repayment. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Ala - he is Yazid ibn Abdillah ibn al-Shikhkhir - except Abdillah ibn Abdillah al-Hadadi; al-Shadhakuni was alone in transmitting it."
"7551","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Assal narrated to us, Sulayman al-Shadhakuni narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ata ibn Abi Maymunah narrated to us, Husayn ibn Imran narrated to us, from Jabir al-Ju'fi, from al-Sha'bi, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever washes a dead person and fulfills the trust in it - meaning that he does not disclose anything he saw during his washing - he will be free of his sins as on the day his mother gave birth to him. He said: And the one most entitled to wash him should wash him; otherwise, one whom you know to possess a share of piety and trustworthiness. No one narrated this hadith from al-Sha'bi except Jabir, and none narrated it from Jabir except Husayn ibn Imran and Sallam ibn Abi Muti', and none narrated it from Husayn ibn Imran except Rawh ibn Ata; al-Shadhakuni was alone in transmitting it."
"7552","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from his mother, from Aishah, who said: We used to prepare nabidh for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a waterskin with its mouth tied at the top and with a spout; we would prepare it in the morning and he would drink it in the evening, and we would prepare it in the evening and he would drink it in the morning. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus ibn Ubayd except Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi."
"7553","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, al-Shadhakuni narrated to us, Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Layth, from Makhul, from Anbasah ibn Abi Sufyan, from Umm Habibah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever prays four rak'ahs before Zuhr, Allah will forbid him to the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from Layth except Hassan ibn Ibrahim."
"7554","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Assal narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Thawban, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among my ummah there are those who, if one of you came to him and asked him for a dinar, he would not give it to him; if he asked him for a dirham, he would not give it to him; if he asked him for a fils, he would not give it to him; yet if he asked Allah for Paradise, He would give it to him - a man in two worn garments, paid no heed to; if he swore by Allah, Allah would fulfill his oath."
"7555","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated to us, Dawud ibn al-Zibriqan narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) broke his fast, he would say: In the name of Allah; O Allah, for You I fasted, and upon Your provision I broke my fast. No one narrated this hadith from Shu'bah except Dawud ibn al-Zibriqan; Ismail ibn Amr was alone in transmitting it."
"7556","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Nasr ibn Shabib al-Asbahani narrated to us, Makhlad ibn al-Hasan ibn Abi Zumayl narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Abu Ishaq al-Sabi'i, from Jarir ibn Abdillah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Fasting three days of every month is fasting the whole year: the white days - the thirteenth, fourteenth, and fifteenth. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah."
"7557","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Nasr ibn Shabib narrated to us, Makhlad ibn Abi Zumayl narrated to us, Abu al-Malih al-Hasan ibn Amr al-Raqqi narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Yazid, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, who said: Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I intend to command my young men to gather bundles of firewood, then go to people who pray in their houses though they have no ailment, and burn them upon them. No one narrated this hadith from Yazid ibn Yazid except Abu al-Malih al-Raqqi."
"7558","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Nasr ibn Shabib al-Asbahani narrated to us, Harun ibn Abdillah al-Hammal narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sa'd narrated to us, Ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn al-Fadl, from Anas ibn Malik, that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey and the sun declined before he set out, he would pray Zuhr and Asr together; but if he set out before the sun declined, he would combine them at the beginning of the time of Asr; and he would do the same with Maghrib and Isha. No one narrated this hadith from Abdillah ibn al-Fadl except Ibn Ajlan, and none from Ibn Ajlan except Muhammad ibn Sa'd; Ya'qub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri was alone in transmitting it."
"7559","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Shabib al-Muqri al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Qarm narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdillah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three days. No one narrated this hadith from al-A'mash except Sulayman ibn Qarm, and none from Sulayman except Husayn ibn Muhammad; Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari was alone in transmitting it."
"7560","Muhammad ibn Asim al-Asbahani narrated to us, Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn A'yan narrated to us, Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Abu Murawih, from Hamzah ibn Amr al-Aslami, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, I have strength to fast while traveling - is there any sin upon me? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is a concession from Allah; whoever takes it, it is good, and whoever wishes to fast, there is no sin upon him. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Aswad except Amr ibn al-Harith; Musa ibn A'yan was alone in transmitting it."
"7561","Muhammad ibn Asim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman - Luwayn - narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Balisi narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A mudd suffices for ablution, and a sa' for bathing. No one narrated this hadith from Khusayf except Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Rahman; Luwayn was alone in transmitting it."
"7562","Muhammad ibn Asim narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Malik narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi al-Hawajib narrated to us, Idris ibn Yazid al-Awdi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and I were under one blanket while I was menstruating. No one narrated this hadith from Idris al-Awdi except Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi al-Hawajib."
"7563","Muhammad ibn Asim narrated to us, Hammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Anbasah al-Warraq narrated to us, Habban ibn Hilal narrated to us, Mujja'ah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abdillah ibn Mughaffal, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man should not comb his hair except every few days, four or five days apart. No one narrated this hadith from Mujja'ah except Habban ibn Hilal."
"7564","Muhammad ibn Asim narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Shabib al-Madani narrated to us, Abu Jabir Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever among you prays after Friday, let him pray four rak'ahs. No one narrated this hadith from Shu'bah except Abu Jabir; Abdillah ibn Shabib was alone in transmitting it."
"7565","Muhammad ibn Asim narrated to us, Ali ibn Harb al-Mawsili narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Amir al-Duba'i narrated to us, from Abu Amir al-Khazzaz Salih ibn Rustum, who said: Abu Qilabah said, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A time will come upon people when they will boast of the multitude of mosques, but they will maintain them only a little. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Amir al-Khazzaz except Sa'id ibn Amir."
"7566","Muhammad ibn Asim narrated to us, Ali ibn Harb al-Mawsili narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Yahya al-Madani narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the mosque waiting for the prayer, when a man stood up and said: I have committed a sin. He turned away from him. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished the prayer, the man stood up and repeated his words. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Did you not pray this prayer with us and perform ablution well for it? He said: Yes. He said: Then it is an expiation for your sin. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Isra'il, and none from Isra'il except Abd al-Rahman ibn Yahya al-Madani; Ali ibn Harb was alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Ali except with this chain."
"7567","Muhammad ibn Asim narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Shabib al-Madani narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abdillah al-Ja'fari narrated to us, Hatim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Ka'b ibn Malik, from his father, who said: A slave girl of mine was pasturing my sheep when a wolf ate a sheep, so I struck the slave girl's face, then I regretted it. I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, if I knew she was a believer I would free her. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who am I? She said: The Messenger of Allah. He said: Then who is Allah? She said: The One in the heaven. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Free her, for she is a believer. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Ajlan except Hatim, and none from Hatim except Dawud al-Ja'fari, and it is not narrated from Ka'b ibn Malik except with this chain."
"7568","Muhammad ibn Asim narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Ju'fi narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdillah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Overlook the slips of people of standing. No one narrated this hadith from Asim except Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash; Abdillah ibn Yazid ibn Muhammad was alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Ibn Mas'ud except with this chain."
"7569","Muhammad ibn Asim narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Shabib narrated to us, Umar ibn Sahl al-Mazini narrated to us, Umar ibn Suhban narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hadrad al-Aslami, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after I had married, and he said: How much did you give as dowry, O Abu Hadrad? I said: Five uqiyyahs. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: If you were scooping from Bathan, you would not have given more. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Aslam except Umar ibn Suhban; Umar ibn Sahl was alone in transmitting it. And the well-known version is from the hadith of Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Abu Hadrad."
"7570","Muhammad ibn Asim narrated to us, Ali ibn Harb narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Kathir narrated to us, my grandfather Yahya ibn Kathir ibn Yahya narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Najdah al-Himsi, from al-Awza'i, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from his father Salih ibn al-Mutawakkil, who said: I heard Mazin ibn al-Ghadubah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hold fast to truthfulness, for it guides to Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awza'i except Abd al-Rahman ibn Najdah; Ali ibn Harb was alone in transmitting it."
"7571","Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Abdi al-Asbahani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, al-Husayn ibn Hafs narrated to us, Ikrimah ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conquered Khaybar and gave it to its Jewish owners for half, and when the fruit ripened he sent Abdillah ibn Rawahah to them, who said: Take from me sixty wasqs of dates, and for us is what is on the tops of the palms. They said: Then you wrong us. He said: Then give me sixty wasqs, and for you is what is on the tops of the palms. They said: By this the heavens and earth stand, and by this you are helped. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Ikrimah; al-Husayn ibn Hafs was alone in transmitting it."
"7572","Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abdillah narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Hatim ibn Ubaydillah al-Namari narrated to us, Sallam Abu al-Mundhir narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to his officials concerning the sunnah of charity: For forty sheep one sheep up to one hundred and twenty; if one more is added, then two sheep up to two hundred; if one more is added, then three sheep up to three hundred; and when sheep become many, then for every hundred sheep one sheep. And he wrote concerning the charity of cattle: For every thirty cattle a jadha'ah, and for forty cattle a musinnah. And he wrote concerning the charity of camels: For five camels one sheep, for ten two sheep, for fifteen three, for twenty four, for twenty-five a she-camel in her second year up to thirty-five; if one more is added, then a she-camel in her third year up to forty-five; if one more is added, then a hiqqah that can be mounted by the stallion up to sixty; if one more is added, then a jadha'ah up to seventy-five; if one more is added, then two young she-camels up to ninety; if one more is added, then two hiqqahs up to one hundred and twenty; and if camels become many, then for every fifty a hiqqah, and for every forty a young she-camel. No one narrated this hadith from Dawud ibn Abi Hind except Sallam Abu al-Mundhir; Hatim ibn Ubaydillah was alone in transmitting it."
"7573","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Amir al-Asbahani narrated to us, my father Ibrahim ibn Amir narrated to us, from my grandfather Amir ibn Ibrahim, who said: I heard Nahshal ibn Sa'id al-Tirmidhi narrating, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, from al-Harith al-A'war, from Ali, who said: I regretted not having asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to make al-Hasan and al-Husayn muezzins."
"7574","And he said: I heard Nahshal narrating from al-Dahhak, from al-Harith, from Ali, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no prayer for one who has no tashahhud. These two hadiths are not narrated from al-Dahhak, from al-Harith, from Ali, except with this chain; Amir ibn Ibrahim was alone in transmitting them."
"7575","And with the same chain, he said: I heard Nahshal ibn Sa'id narrating, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, from al-A'mash, from Badham, from Qanbar, from Ali, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Indeed Paradise has longed for four of my companions, and my Lord commanded me to love them. Then Suhayb the Roman, Bilal ibn Rabah, Talhah, al-Zubayr, Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, and Ammar ibn Yasir stepped forward, and they said: O Messenger of Allah, who are these four that we may love them? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Ammar, Allah has made you know the hypocrites; as for these four, one of them is Ali ibn Abi Talib, the second is al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad al-Kindi, the third is Salman al-Farisi, and the fourth is Abu Dharr al-Ghifari. No one narrated this hadith from al-A'mash except al-Dahhak, and it is not narrated from Qanbar except with this chain; Amir ibn Ibrahim was alone in transmitting it."
"7576","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Amir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from my grandfather, from Nahshal, from al-Dahhak, from Sufyan, from Badham, from Qanbar, from Ali, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: No hypocrite memorizes Surah Hud, Bara'ah, Ya-Sin, al-Dukhan, and Amma Yatasa'alun. This hadith is not narrated from Qanbar, from Ali, except with this chain; Amir ibn Ibrahim was alone in transmitting it. And the Sufyan from whom al-Dahhak narrated is Sufyan ibn al-Layl, from whom al-Sha'bi narrated."
"7577","And with the same chain, from al-Dahhak, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdillah ibn Mas'ud, who said: The supplication of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after the tashahhud in the obligatory prayer was: O Allah, we ask You for all good, its near and its distant, what we know of it and what we do not know; and we seek refuge in You from all evil, its near and its distant, what we know of it and what we do not know. O Allah, we ask You for what Your righteous servants asked You, and we seek refuge in You from what Your righteous servants sought refuge from. Our Lord, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter and shield us from the punishment of the Fire. Our Lord, we have believed, so forgive us our sins, expiate our evil deeds, and take us in death with the righteous. Our Lord, give us what You promised us through Your messengers and do not disgrace us on the Day of Resurrection; indeed You do not break the promise. And he would greet to his right and to his left."
"7578","And with the same chain, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdillah ibn Mas'ud, who said: The supplication of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the two Eids was: O Allah, we ask You for a God-fearing life, a sound death, and a return that is neither disgracing nor exposing. O Allah, do not destroy us suddenly, nor take us by surprise, nor make us hasten away from a right or a bequest. O Allah, we ask You for chastity and sufficiency, piety and guidance, and a good end in the Hereafter and this world; and we seek refuge in You from doubt and dissension, showing off and seeking repute in Your religion. O Turner of hearts, do not turn our hearts away after You guided us, and grant us mercy from Yourself; indeed You are the Bestower."
"7579","And with the same chain, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdillah ibn Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever forgets wiping the head and remembers while praying, and finds wetness in his beard, let him take from it and wipe his head with it, for that suffices him; but if he finds no wetness, let him repeat the ablution and the prayer."
"7580","And with the same chain, from Abdillah ibn Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Recite the Quran with correct grammar, for whoever recites the Quran with correct grammar, for every letter there are ten good deeds, expiation of ten evil deeds, and raising by ten degrees."
"7581","And with the same chain, from Abdillah ibn Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People are two men: a scholar and a learner; both are equal in reward, and there is no good in the rest of the people between them."
"7582","And with the same chain, from Abdillah ibn Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, the two feet of a servant will not move on the Day of Resurrection until he is asked about four: about his life in what he spent it, his body in what he wore it out, his wealth in what he earned it and where he placed it and where he spent it. No one narrated these hadiths from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdillah, except Nahshal ibn Sa'id; Amir ibn Ibrahim was alone in transmitting them."
"7583","And with the same chain, from al-Dahhak, from Masruq, from Aishah, who said: When the last ten nights began, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would tighten his waist-wrapper and avoid women. No one narrated this hadith from al-Dahhak, from Masruq, except Nahshal; Amir ibn Ibrahim was alone in transmitting it."
"7584","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Amir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from my grandfather, Abu Ghalib al-Nadr ibn Abdillah al-Azdi narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Ghazwan narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was pressed by travel, he would combine the two prayers, Maghrib and Isha. No one narrated this hadith from Fudayl ibn Ghazwan except al-Nadr ibn Abdillah; Amir ibn Ibrahim was alone in transmitting it."
"7585","And with the same chain, from al-Nadr ibn Abdillah, al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from Abu Harun al-Abdi, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has an imam, the recitation of the imam is recitation for him. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan ibn Salih, from Abu Harun, except al-Nadr ibn Abdillah; Amir ibn Ibrahim was alone in transmitting it."
"7586","And with the same chain, from al-Nadr ibn Abdillah al-Azdi, from Shayban, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: Two men sneezed before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he said Tashmit to one of them but not to the other. He said: O Messenger of Allah, you said Tashmit to so-and-so but did not say it to me? He said: He praised Allah, but you did not praise Him. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir except Shayban, and none from Shayban except al-Nadr ibn Abdillah; Amir ibn Ibrahim was alone in transmitting it."
"7587","And with the same chain, from al-Nadr, from Bashir Abu Ismail, Mujahid narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Amr, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog. No one narrated this hadith from Bashir except al-Nadr; Amir ibn Ibrahim was alone in transmitting it."
"7588","And with the same chain, from al-Nadr, from al-Hasan ibn Salih, from Ash'ath, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The blood-money of a covenanted non-Muslim is half the blood-money of a Muslim. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi' except Ash'ath, and none from Ash'ath except al-Hasan ibn Salih, and none from al-Hasan except al-Nadr ibn Abdillah; Amir ibn Ibrahim was alone in transmitting it."
"7589","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Amir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from my grandfather, Amr ibn Salih al-Thaqafi narrated to us, Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, who said: Bilal came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to announce the dawn prayer and found him asleep, so he said: Prayer is better than sleep, and it was established in the dawn call. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar, and none from Salih except Amr ibn Salih; Amir ibn Ibrahim was alone in transmitting it."
"7590","And with the same chain, Amr ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Mubarak ibn Fadalalah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was shrouded in three white Sahuli garments of cotton. No one narrated this hadith from Mubarak except Amr ibn Salih; Amir ibn Ibrahim was alone in transmitting it."
"7591","And with the same chain, from Amr ibn Salih, Abu Hamzah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among those before you there was a man who bought wine, mixed it and added some water to it, then went with it, sold it, and took dinars, which he put in a bag. He boarded a ship on the sea, taking a monkey with him. When they were at sea, the monkey took the bag, climbed up until it sat on the top of the mast, then opened the bag and began throwing one dinar into the sea and one dinar into the ship, until it finished what was in the bag - the monkey doing that because the man had cheated. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Hamzah except Amr ibn Salih; Amir ibn Ibrahim was alone in transmitting it."
"7592","And with the same chain, from Amr ibn Salih, from Ash'ath, from Ibn Sirin, from Amr ibn Wahb, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey and performed ablution while al-Mughirah poured water over him; then we reached the people while Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf was leading them, so we prayed what we caught and made up what we missed. Al-Mughirah said: I went to inform him, but he said: Leave him. No one narrated this hadith from Ash'ath except Amr; Amir ibn Ibrahim was alone in transmitting it."
"7593","And with the same chain, from Amr ibn Salih, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from Bakr ibn Abdillah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stopped at a place, he would not depart until he prayed Zuhr, and he would pray when the sun declined. No one narrated this hadith from Bakr ibn Abdillah except Ismail ibn Muslim, and none from Ismail except Amr ibn Salih; Amir ibn Ibrahim was alone in transmitting it."
"7594","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Amir narrated to us, my uncle Muhammad ibn Amir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ziyad Abu Hamzah narrated to us, from Hamzah al-Zayyat, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, who said: The firmly established prostrations are four: Alif Lam Mim, the Revelation, the prostration, Ha Mim, the prostration, the Star, and Read in the name of your Lord."
"7595","And with the same chain, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would be intimate with his wives and then not touch water; if in the morning he wished to repeat, he repeated, and if he did not wish, he bathed."
"7596","And with the same chain, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Wahb, who said: Abdillah ibn Mas'ud said: People will remain holding fast as long as knowledge comes to them from the companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and from their elders; but when it comes to them from the young, then they perish."
"7597","And with the same chain, from Hamzah al-Zayyat, from al-A'mash, from Khaythamah, from Adi ibn Hatim, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Each of you will speak to his Lord with no interpreter between him and Him; he will look to his right and see what he sent forth, and to his left and see what he sent forth, and in front of him there will be the Fire; so fear the Fire even with half a date. No one narrated these hadiths from Hamzah al-Zayyat except Ziyad Abu Hamzah; Amir ibn Ibrahim was alone in transmitting them."
"7598","Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Ahmad ibn Usayd al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abdillah al-Abdi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Aban narrated to us, Abu Maryam Abd al-Ghaffar ibn al-Qasim al-Ansari narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubshi ibn Junadah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali: You are to me as Harun was to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Abu Maryam; Ismail ibn Aban was alone in transmitting it."
"7599","Muhammad ibn Ismail narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abdillah narrated to us, Hatim ibn Ubaydillah al-Namari narrated to us, from Isa ibn Maymun, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forgot before completion, so he prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness before greeting, and he said: Whoever forgets before completion prostrates the two prostrations of forgetfulness before greeting, and if he forgets after completion he prostrates the two prostrations of forgetfulness after greeting. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah with this wording except Isa ibn Maymun; Hatim was alone in transmitting it."
"7600","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Walid al-Asbahani narrated to us, Sa'd ibn Abdillah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated to us, Qudamah ibn Muhammad al-Ashja'i narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Shaybah al-Ta'ifi, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no one of my ummah who is put in charge of any affair of the people and does not guard them as he guards himself and his family, except that he will not smell the fragrance of Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Ismail ibn Shaybah; Qudamah ibn Muhammad was alone in transmitting it."
"7601","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Shayban al-Ramli narrated to us, Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, from Talhah ibn Amr, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A sin that is forgiven, a sin that is not forgiven, and a sin that is requited. As for the sin that is not forgiven, it is associating partners with Allah. As for the sin that is forgiven, it is your deed between you and your Lord. And as for the one for which you are requited, it is your wronging your brother. No one narrated this hadith from Ata except Talhah ibn Amr."
"7602","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Amr al-Sakuni narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Mahfuz ibn Miswar, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadar, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever hears a hadith from me and denies it has denied three: Allah, His Messenger, and the one who narrated it. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadar except Mahfuz ibn Miswar; Baqiyyah was alone in transmitting it."
"7603","Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Umarah al-Asbahani narrated to me, al-Abbas ibn Muhammad ibn Hatim narrated to us, Shabbabah ibn Sawwar narrated to us, al-Mughirah ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Walid ibn Muslim, from Jundub, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When one of you seeks permission three times and is not granted it, let him return. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus except al-Mughirah ibn Muslim; Shabbabah was alone in transmitting it."
"7604","Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Umarah narrated to me, al-Abbas ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yazid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Kamil Abu al-Ala narrated to us, from Talhah ibn Yahya, from Aishah bint Talhah, from Aishah, who said: I would sometimes scrape semen from the garment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Aishah bint Talhah except Talhah ibn Yahya, and none narrated it from Talhah except Kamil, and none from Kamil except Khalid ibn Yazid; al-Abbas ibn Muhammad was alone in transmitting it."
"7605","And with the same chain, Kamil narrated to us, from Abu Yahya, from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the slave girl commits adultery, then commits adultery, then commits adultery, sell her even for a rope. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Yahya al-Qattat except Kamil, and none narrated it from Kamil except Khalid ibn Yazid; al-Abbas was alone in transmitting it."
"7606","And with the same chain, from Mujahid, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) missed two rak'ahs before Asr; when he finished he prayed them, then he never prayed them again. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Yahya al-Qattat except Kamil, and none from Kamil except Khalid ibn Yazid; al-Abbas was alone in transmitting it."
"7607","Muhammad ibn Hamzah narrated to me, al-Abbas ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Bukayr the nephew of Juwayriyah narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Sulayman al-Duba'i narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that he used to order the killing of all snakes, until Abu Lubabah ibn Abd al-Mundhir informed him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade killing the snakes that live in houses. And he narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to touch the Black Stone when a scorpion stung him, and he said: What is with you, may Allah curse you? If you were to spare anyone you would have spared the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Hisham except Ja'far, and none from Ja'far except Bukayr; al-Abbas was alone in transmitting it, and the end of the hadith is not narrated from Abu Lubabah except with this chain."
"7608","Muhammad ibn Harmalah al-Qalzumi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ya'qub al-Dari narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Hashim ibn Salih al-Makhzumi narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Qays narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted the pilgrim in ihram to kill five kinds of animals: the crow, the kite, the vicious dog, the scorpion, and the mouse."
"7609","And with the same chain, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not sell fruits until their soundness appears; he forbade both the seller and the buyer."
"7610","And with the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two parties to a sale have the choice, each of them, as long as they have not parted and were together, or one of them gives the other the choice; if one of them gives the other the choice and they conclude the sale on that basis, the sale becomes binding."
"7611","And with the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The poor will enter Paradise five hundred years before the rich. No one narrated these hadiths from Ya'qub ibn Qays except Sa'id ibn Hashim; Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Dari - of the descendants of Tamim al-Dari - was alone in transmitting them."
"7612","Muhammad ibn Abi Harmalah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ismail ibn Abd al-A'la al-Ayli narrated to us, Amr ibn Hashim al-Bayruti narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abdillah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not accept the prayer of a woman until she covers her adornment, nor of a slave girl who has reached menstruation until she wears a head-cover. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awza'i except Amr ibn Hashim; Ishaq ibn Ismail was alone in transmitting it."
"7613","Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Shadhan narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Sa'd ibn al-Salt narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Amr al-Fuqaymi narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Khusayfah, from Thawban, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts six days after the breaking of the fast consecutively, it is as if he fasted the year. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan ibn Amr except Sa'd ibn al-Salt; Shadhan was alone in transmitting it. And he said: from Yazid, from Thawban, though it is really Yazid - meaning Ibn Khusayfah - from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban."
"7614","Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Sa'd ibn al-Salt narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that she heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever owes a debt and intends to repay it, Allah's help will be with him, and Allah will provide him sustenance. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Sa'd ibn al-Salt, and none narrated it from Sa'd except Shadhan."
"7615","Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Sa'd ibn al-Salt narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from his grandfather Ali ibn Husayn, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wear a red cloak on the day of Eid. No one narrated this hadith from Ja'far ibn Muhammad except Sa'd ibn al-Salt; Shadhan was alone in transmitting it."
"7616","And with the same chain, Sa'd ibn al-Salt narrated to us, from Mubarak ibn Fadalalah, from Ali ibn Zayd ibn Jud'an, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, who said: In the year he performed Hajj, Uthman ibn Affan was brought a broth with some of this partridge on it, caught by people in a state of non-ihram. Some of the people said: Ali dislikes this. So he sent for Ali and called him; he had been fixing a water-trough of his, so he shook off his hands and came. Uthman said to him: You keep differing on something; they claim you say this is not proper. Ali became angry and said: Is it for this that you say to me that I differ? I ask by Allah whoever heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying in the year of Hajj, when he was brought the leg of a wild donkey, and he said: Feed it to the people in non-ihram, for we are in ihram? Several men stood up and testified for him. Then he said: I ask by Allah whoever heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying in the year of Hajj, when he was brought ostrich eggs: Feed them to the people in non-ihram, for we are in ihram? Several men stood up and testified for him. Then they dispersed from that bowl. Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib said: It is as if I am looking at the leg of that partridge standing, with no one eating it. No one narrated this hadith from Mubarak ibn Fadalalah except Sa'd ibn al-Salt; Shadhan was alone in transmitting it."
"7617","Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us, Abbad ibn Rashid narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Deeds are presented to Allah on the Day of Resurrection. Prayer will come and say: O Lord, I am prayer. Allah will say: You are upon good. Charity will come and say: O Lord, I am charity. He will say: You are upon good. Fasting will come and say: O Lord, I am fasting. He will say: You are upon good. Until Islam comes and says: O Lord, You are Peace and I am Islam. Allah will say: You are upon good; by you I take today and by you I give. Then Allah says: Indeed the religion with Allah is Islam, and whoever seeks a religion other than Islam, it will never be accepted from him, and he will be among the losers in the Hereafter."
"7618","And with the same chain, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The first thing the servant will be asked about on the Day of Resurrection is his prayer. He will say: Look at the prayer of My servant; if he completed it, it will be said: O Lord, he completed it; and if he fell short, it will be said: O Lord, he fell short. Then Allah will say: Look whether My servant has voluntary prayers. It will be said: Yes, many. He will say: Then complete for My servant from his voluntary deeds. Then the rest of the deeds will be taken in like measure. No one narrated these two hadiths from Abbad ibn Rashid except Hajjaj ibn Nusayr."
"7619","Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Sa'd ibn al-Salt narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Alqamah al-Laythi, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not face the qiblah nor turn your backs to it to urinate or defecate; rather face east or west. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Amr except Sa'd ibn al-Salt; Shadhan was alone in transmitting it."
"7620","Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Kirmani ibn Amr narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Zarbi al-Khuza'i narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sirin narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, from Umm Salamah, who said: Fatimah came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a pot of hers in which she had made porridge for him; she carried it on a tray and placed it before him. He said to her: Where are your cousin and your two sons? She said: In the house. He said: Go and call them. So she went to Ali and said: Answer the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), you and your two sons. Umm Salamah said: So Ali came walking, holding al-Hasan and al-Husayn by the hand, with Fatimah walking with them. When he saw them approaching, he stretched his hand to a cloak that was on the bed, spread it, seated them on it, took the four ends of the cloak in his left hand and gathered it over their heads, raised his right hand to his Lord and said: O Allah, these are my household, so remove impurity from them and purify them thoroughly - three times. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Hurayrah except Muhammad ibn Sirin, and none from Ibn Sirin except Sa'id ibn Zarbi; al-Kirmani ibn Amr was alone in transmitting it."
"7621","Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Sa'd ibn al-Salt narrated to us, Mis'ar ibn Kidam narrated to us, from al-Abbas ibn Dharih, from Ziyad ibn Abdillah al-Bajali, Ammar ibn Yasir narrated to us, that they asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Did you ever approach anything unlawful with women in the pre-Islamic period? He said: No; I had two appointments: one of them my eyes overcame me and kept me from, and the other the evening company of the people kept me from. No one narrated this hadith from Mis'ar except Sa'd ibn al-Salt; Shadhan was alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Ammar except with this chain."
"7622","And with the same chain, Sa'd ibn al-Salt narrated to us, Abu al-Jahm Harun ibn al-Jahm al-Qurashi narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Muharib ibn Dithar, who said: I heard Ibn Umar narrating from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Birds strike the ground with their beaks and shake their tails from the terror of the Day of Resurrection, yet the false witness will not finish speaking, nor will his feet settle on the ground, before he is cast into the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr except Abu al-Jahm, and none from Abu al-Jahm except Sa'd ibn al-Salt; Shadhan was alone in transmitting it."
"7623","Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Budayl ibn Maysarah al-Uqayli narrated to us, from his father, from Abu al-Jawza, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to open the prayer with the takbir and the recitation with Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds. When he bowed he would neither lower his head nor raise it, but between that. He would say the greetings in every two rak'ahs, and he would end the prayer with the greeting of peace. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Rahman ibn Budayl except Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi."
"7624","Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us, Abu Amir al-Khazzaz narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadar, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, who said: A man sought permission to enter upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: What an evil brother of the tribe. When he entered, he turned to him with his face and spoke with him. When he left, I said: O Messenger of Allah, you said: What an evil brother of the tribe, yet when he entered you turned to him with your face and spoke with him? He said: Among the worst of people are those feared for their evil. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Amir al-Khazzaz except Hajjaj ibn Nusayr; Shadhan was alone in transmitting it."
"7625","Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim Shadhan narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Mujashi' ibn Amr narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Uqayl ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The people suffered drought in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Muslims came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, rain has failed, trees have withered, livestock have perished, and people are in hardship; ask your Lord for rain for us. He said: When such-and-such a day comes, go out, taking your charities with you. When that day came, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the people went out, he walking and they walking, with tranquility and dignity upon them, until they reached the prayer ground. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went forward and prayed two rak'ahs with them, reciting aloud in them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the two Eids and the rain prayer in the first rak'ah the Opening of the Book and Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and in the second rak'ah the Opening of the Book and Has there reached you the story of the Overwhelming. When he finished his prayer, he faced the people, turned his cloak inside out, then knelt on his knees, raised his hands, uttered a takbir before seeking rain, then said: O Allah, give us rain and aid us. O Allah, give us a rain that brings aid, spacious, spring-like, plentiful, copious, enveloping, drenching, wholesome, agreeable, fertile, pasture-producing, heavy, comprehensive, pouring, covering, lasting, abundant, beneficial and not harmful, soon and not delayed. O Allah, with it give life to the lands, aid the servants, and make it provision for those present among us and the desert-dwellers. O Allah, send down upon our land its adornment, and send down in our land its settlement. O Allah, send down upon us pure water from the sky, revive with it a dead land, and give drink to the cattle and many people whom You created for us. He said: They had not moved before pieces of cloud advanced and joined together, then it rained upon them for seven days and nights without ceasing over Medina. The Muslims came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, the land is flooded, houses have collapsed, and roads are cut off; supplicate Allah for us to turn it away from us. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed while on the pulpit until his molars appeared, in amazement at the quick boredom of the children of Adam, then said: O Allah, around us and not upon us. O Allah, on the tops of hills, where trees grow, the bottoms of valleys, and the backs of highlands. He said: So it broke away from Medina, remaining like a shield, raining on its pastures while not a drop fell in it. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Uqayl, and none from Uqayl except Ibn Lahi'ah, and none from Ibn Lahi'ah except Mujashi' ibn Amr; Shadhan was alone in transmitting it."
"7626","Muhammad ibn al-Marzuban al-Adami al-Shirazi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Ash'ath, from al-Hasan, from Iyad ibn Himar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We do not accept the froth of the polytheists - meaning their gifts. No one narrated this hadith from Ash'ath ibn Sawwar except Hafs; Sahl ibn Uthman was alone in transmitting it."
"7627","Muhammad ibn al-Marzuban al-Adami al-Shirazi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, from Abu Ayyub, from Asim ibn Abi al-Najud, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abdillah ibn Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me while I was among sheep belonging to Uqbah; he wiped my head and said: May Allah have mercy on you; you are a taught young boy. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Abi Ayyub except Ibn Abi Za'idah; Sahl ibn Uthman was alone in transmitting it."
"7628","Muhammad ibn al-Marzuban narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, al-Muharibi narrated to us, from Layth, from Jabir, from Mundhir, from Muhammad ibn Ali, who said: I asked my father privately, saying: O father, who is the best of this ummah after its Prophet? He said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Quhafah. I said: Then who? He said: Then Umar ibn al-Khattab. No one narrated this hadith from Jabir except Layth, and none from Layth except al-Muharibi; Sahl ibn Uthman was alone in transmitting it."
"7629","Muhammad ibn al-Marzuban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Hakim al-Razi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ubaydillah al-Sunni narrated to us, Abu Mu'adh Khalid al-Balkhi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The woman with prolonged bleeding bathes once, then performs ablution - meaning for every prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Ajlan except Abu Mu'adh al-Balkhi; Hisham al-Sinni was alone in transmitting it."
"7630","Muhammad ibn al-Marzuban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Hakim al-Razi narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Imam narrated to us, from Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar, from al-Zuhri, from Nabhan, the freedman of Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to touch her intimately while she was menstruating, with a waist-wrapper over her reaching to the knees. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar; Hafs ibn Umar al-Imam was alone in transmitting it."
"7631","Muhammad ibn al-Marzuban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Hakim al-Razi narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Muslim narrated to us, Bahr al-Saqqa narrated to us, al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Urwah, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to lie with me while I was menstruating, and we would bathe together from one vessel."
"7632","And with the same chain, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdillah ibn Utbah, from Umm al-Darda, from Ka'b ibn Asim, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting while traveling is not part of righteousness. No one narrated these two hadiths from Bahr al-Saqqa except al-Harith ibn Muslim."
"7633","Muhammad ibn al-Marzuban al-Adami narrated to us, Nuh ibn Anas al-Muqri al-Razi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Fadl ibn Isa al-Raqashi, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: This Ramadan has come; in it the gates of Paradise are opened, the gates of Hell are closed, and the devils are chained. Far removed is one who reaches Ramadan and is not forgiven; if he is not forgiven in it, then when? No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Ishaq except Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra."
"7634","Muhammad ibn al-Marzuban al-Adami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Narmaqi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Abd Rabbihi al-Sindi narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn al-Ala ibn Shaybah, from Ibn Awn, from Uqbah ibn Abd al-Ghafir, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: Coitus interruptus was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: It does not matter if you do not do it, for it is only the decree. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Awn except Abdillah ibn al-Ala; Sahl ibn Abd Rabbihi al-Sindi was alone in transmitting it."
"7635","Muhammad ibn al-Marzuban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muqatil al-Razi narrated to us, Isa ibn Ibrahim al-Qurashi narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Abdillah ibn Sa'd al-Ayli, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Aishah, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) oiled his beard, he would begin with his tuft below the lower lip. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except al-Hakam ibn Abdillah; Isa ibn Ibrahim was alone in transmitting it."
"7636","Muhammad ibn al-Marzuban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muqatil al-Razi narrated to us, al-Furat ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Malik ibn Mighwal, from Abu Dawud, who said: Al-Bara ibn Azib met me, took my hand, shook hands with me, and laughed in my face. Then he said: Do you know why I took your hand? I said: No, except that I thought you did it only for good. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met me and did that to me, then said: Do you know why I did that to you? I said: No. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When two Muslims meet, shake hands, and each of them laughs in his companion's face, doing that only for Allah, they do not part until they are forgiven. No one narrated this hadith from Malik ibn Mighwal except al-Furat ibn Khalid."
"7637","Muhammad ibn al-Marzuban narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Narmaqi narrated to us, Salm ibn Salim narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Abu Umamah al-Bahili, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There has been no polytheism since Adam descended from heaven to earth except that its beginning was denial of destiny; no nation associated partners except through denial of destiny. You will be tested with it, O ummah; when you meet them, you be the questioners, and do not let them into the religion lest they cast doubts upon you."
"7638","And with the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah created creation, decreed the decree, took the covenant of the prophets while His Throne was upon the water. He took the people of faith in His right hand and the people of wretchedness in His left hand - and both Hands of the Merciful are right. He said: O people of the right side. They said: At Your service, blessed. He said: Am I not your Lord? They said: Yes. Then He mixed them together, and one of them said: Our Lord, why did You mix us together? He said: And they have other deeds besides that which they will do; lest you say on the Day of Resurrection: We were unaware of this, or you say: Our fathers associated partners before, and we were offspring after them. So Allah created creation, decreed the decree, took the covenant of the prophets while His Throne was upon the water; the people of Paradise are its people, and the people of Hell are its people. A man among the people said: Then what is the point of deeds, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Each people works for what they were created for: the people of Paradise by the deeds of the people of Paradise, and the people of Hell by the deeds of the people of Hell. Umar ibn al-Khattab said: O Messenger of Allah, are these deeds of ours something we innovate or something already finished? He said: Something already finished. He said: Then now we strive in worship. No one narrated these two hadiths from Sulayman al-Taymi except Abd al-Rahman - I think he is Ibn Umar al-Makki; Salm ibn Salim was alone in transmitting them."
"7639","Muhammad ibn al-Marzuban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muqatil al-Razi narrated to us, Hakkam ibn Salm narrated to us, from Tu'mah ibn Amr, from Aban, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: Nabhan apostatized three times, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, give me power over Nabhan with a black rope around his neck. I turned and there was Nabhan, seized, with a black rope placed around his neck. They brought him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the sword in his right hand and the rope in his left to kill him, when a man of the Ansar said: O Messenger of Allah, if only you moved away. He said: So he handed the sword to a man and said: Go and strike his neck. He said: He went with him, then Nabhan laughed and said: Would they kill a man who testifies that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah? So he let him go. No one narrated this hadith from Tu'mah ibn Amr al-Ja'fari except Hakkam."
"7640","Muhammad ibn al-Marzuban al-Adami narrated to us, Sahl ibn Zanjalah narrated to us, Ma'n ibn Isa al-Qazzaz narrated to us, from Malik ibn Anas, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray at night two rak'ahs, then two rak'ahs, then two rak'ahs, then two rak'ahs, then three. No one narrated this hadith from Malik except Ma'n ibn Isa."
"7641","Muhammad ibn al-Marzuban al-Adami narrated to us, Hamzah ibn Farrukh al-Razi narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Abd al-Rahman Abu Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Abu Kiran al-Hasan ibn Uqbah al-Muradi narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Safwan ibn Assal al-Muradi, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted wiping over the leather socks for three days and nights for the traveler, and for the resident one day and night. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Murrah except Abu Kiran; Abu Yahya al-Himmani was alone in transmitting it."
"7642","Muhammad ibn al-Marzuban narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Jabalah al-Shirazi narrated to us, Sa'd ibn al-Salt narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Wabarah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Musli, from Kharashah ibn al-Hurr, who said: I saw Umar ibn al-Khattab striking the palms of men during the fast of Rajab until they put them into food, saying: What is Rajab? Rajab was only a month that the people of ignorance used to venerate; when Islam came, it was abandoned."
"7643","Muhammad ibn al-Marzuban al-Adami narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Jabalah narrated to us, Sa'd ibn al-Salt narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Shimr ibn Atiyyah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Umm al-Darda, who said: Salman al-Farisi came to me greeting me, wearing a Qatwani cloak wrapped around him. I laid a cushion for him, but he refused it, folded a cloak, and sat on it. He said: Sufficient for you is what has reached you of the dwelling. Then he praised Allah for a while, uttered takbir, invoked blessings on the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then said: Where is your companion? - meaning Abu al-Darda. I said: He is in the mosque. He went to him, then both came together; Abu al-Darda had bought meat for a dirham and was carrying it hanging in his hand. He said: O Umm al-Darda, bake and cook. So we did. Then we brought the food to Salman. Abu al-Darda said: Eat with Umm al-Darda, for I am fasting. Salman said: I will not eat until you eat. So Abu al-Darda broke his fast and ate with him. When the hour came in which Abu al-Darda would stand, he went to stand but Salman seated him. Abu al-Darda said: Do you forbid me from worshipping my Lord? Salman said: Your eyes have a right over you, and your family has a share over you. He held him back until near dawn, when they stood, prayed some rak'ahs, performed witr, then went out to the dawn prayer. They mentioned their affair to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: What is with Salman, may his mother lose him? He has been filled with knowledge. No one narrated these two hadiths from al-A'mash except Sa'd ibn al-Salt; al-Hasan ibn Jabalah was alone in transmitting them."
"7644","Muhammad ibn Sa'dan al-Atayidi al-Shirazi narrated to us, Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated to me, Sa'id ibn Amir narrated to us, from Ash'ath, from Awf, from Yazid al-Farisi, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I said to Uthman: O Commander of the Faithful, what made you place Bara'ah among the Mi'in and al-Anfal among the Mathani, joining them together and placing them among the seven long ones, without writing between them: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Merciful? Uthman said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would receive surahs of varying lengths among what was revealed to him. When a verse was revealed to him, he would say to one of those who wrote: Put this verse in such-and-such a surah. Al-Anfal was among the first revealed in Medina, while Bara'ah was the last of the Quran. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died without clarifying it to us, and I saw that its story resembled its story, so I joined them together and did not write between them: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Merciful. No one narrated this hadith from al-Ash'ath, from Awf, except Sa'id ibn Amir; Zayd ibn Akhzam was alone in transmitting it."
"7645","Muhammad ibn Sa'dan narrated to us, Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated to us, Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Hanzalah ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Mujahid, from Abdillah ibn Ukbarah, who said: Picking the teeth is sunnah. This hadith is not narrated from Abdillah ibn Ukbarah except with this chain; Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri was alone in transmitting it."
"7646","Muhammad ibn Sa'dan narrated to us, Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated to us, Safwan ibn Isa narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Hind, from his father, from Abdillah ibn Abi Qatadah, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, who said: We entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on Friday with food before him. He said: Come near and eat. We said: We are fasting. He said: Did you fast yesterday? We said: No. He said: Do you intend to fast tomorrow? We said: No. He said: Then eat, for Friday is not to be fasted alone; it is taken as a festival. No one narrated this hadith from Abdillah ibn Abi Qatadah except Sa'id ibn Abi Hind, and none from Sa'id except his son Abdillah; Safwan ibn Isa was alone in transmitting it."
"7647","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Istakhri narrated to us, Bishr ibn Ali al-Kirmani narrated to us, Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Aban ibn Taghlib, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, who said: Witr is not obligatory, but it is a sunnah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) established."
"7648","And with the same chain, from Aban ibn Taghlib, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Abdillah ibn Ukaym, who said: The letter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached us while we were in the land of Juhaynah: Do not benefit from carrion by skin or sinew."
"7649","And with the same chain, Aban ibn Taghlib narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Razin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the strap of one of your sandals breaks, let him not walk in one sandal."
"7650","And with the same chain, from al-A'mash, from Abu Razin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The purification of the vessel of one of you, when a dog licks in it, is to wash it seven times. No one narrated these hadiths from Aban ibn Taghlib except Hassan ibn Ibrahim."
"7651","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Istakhri narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abbad al-Kirmani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Abu Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us, from al-Rabi' ibn Anas, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out and saw in the mosque a man who did not complete his bowing or prostration, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prayer of a man who does not complete bowing and prostration is not accepted. No one narrated this hadith from al-Rabi' ibn Anas except Abu Ja'far al-Razi, and none from Abu Ja'far except Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr."
"7652","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Istakhri narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Abbas al-Istakhri narrated to us, Ismah ibn al-Mutawakkil al-Istakhri narrated to us, Zafir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Bakr ibn Khunays, from Dirar ibn Amr, from Abu Rafi', from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When the warrior in the path of Allah goes out, his sins are made a bridge at the door of his house; when he leaves them behind, he leaves all his sins behind, with not even the weight of a gnat's wing remaining upon him. Allah guarantees him four things: to care for him in the family and wealth he leaves behind, that by whatever death he dies He will admit him to Paradise, that if He returns him He returns him safe with whatever booty or reward he gained, and that no sun sets except that it sets with his sins."
"7653","Muhammad ibn Musa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sahl ibn Makhlad al-Istakhri narrated to us, Ismah ibn al-Mutawakkil narrated to us, Zafir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Isra'il ibn Yunus, from Jabir, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever marries has completed half of faith, so let him fear Allah in the remaining half."
"7654","And with the same chain, Zafir narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that a man went out and ordered his wife not to leave her house. Her father was in the lower part of the house while she was in the upper part. Her father fell ill, so she sent to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him. He said: Obey your husband. Then her father died, so she sent to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Obey your husband. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to her: Allah has forgiven her father because of her obedience to her husband."
"7655","And with the same chain, Zafir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abu Raja, from Suhayl - meaning Ibn Abi Hazm - from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The family of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) have entered the morning as nine households, among whom there is not a sa' of food."
"7656","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Istakhri narrated to us, Ismail ibn Yahya al-Istakhri narrated to us, Ismah ibn al-Mutawakkil narrated to us, Zafir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Muslim, from Ibrahim ibn Maysarah, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather - I know it only as raised - who said: The soundness of the beginning of this ummah is through asceticism and certainty, and its ruin is through miserliness and hope. No one narrated these hadiths from Zafir ibn Sulayman except Ismah ibn al-Mutawakkil."
"7657","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Istakhri narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Abbas al-Istakhri narrated to us, Ismah ibn al-Mutawakkil narrated to us, Zafir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Dawud al-Ta'i, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never struck a woman, nor a servant of his, nor struck anything with his hand except to strive in the path of Allah. He was never wronged in anything and took revenge from its doer, except that the sanctities of Allah were violated, then he took revenge for Allah. He was never given a choice between two matters except that he chose the easier of them, so long as it was not a sin; if it was a sin, he was the farthest of people from it. No one narrated this hadith from Dawud al-Ta'i except Zafir ibn Sulayman; Ismah ibn al-Mutawakkil was alone in transmitting it."
"7658","And with the same chain, Ismah ibn al-Mutawakkil narrated to us, Abu Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Injury by a beast is without liability, the well is without liability, the mine is without liability, and in buried treasure is the fifth. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ja'far al-Razi except Ismah ibn al-Mutawakkil."
"7659","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Istakhri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sahl ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Ismah ibn al-Mutawakkil narrated to us, Adi ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wake in the morning in a state of major impurity from intercourse, not a wet dream, and then fast. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah ibn Umar except Adi ibn al-Fadl; Ismah ibn al-Mutawakkil was alone in transmitting it."
"7660","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Istakhri narrated to us, Ismail ibn Yahya al-Istakhri narrated to us, Ismah ibn al-Mutawakkil narrated to us, Sawwar ibn Mus'ab al-Darir al-Kufi narrated to us, from Asim ibn Abi al-Najud, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Safwan ibn Assal al-Muradi, who said: We used to travel with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we would not remove our leather socks when we had put them on in a state of ablution for three days, except from major impurity - but not from stool, urine, or sleep. No one narrated this hadith from Sawwar ibn Mus'ab except Ismah ibn al-Mutawakkil."
"7661","Muhammad ibn Musa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sahl narrated to us, Ismah ibn al-Mutawakkil narrated to us, Abu Yusuf the judge narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Ali, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, were it not that I would burden the believers, I would never stay behind any expedition in the path of Allah; but I do not find mounts to carry them on, nor do they find means to follow me, nor would they like to stay behind me."
"7662","And with the same chain, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: I wish I could fight in the path of Allah until I am killed, then be brought to life, then be killed, then be brought to life, then be killed, then be brought to life, then be killed. No one narrated these two hadiths from Abdillah ibn Ali - he is Abu Ayyub al-Ifriqi - except Abu Yusuf the judge."
"7663","Muhammad ibn Musa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sahl narrated to us, Ismah ibn al-Mutawakkil narrated to us, Abd al-A'la ibn Abi al-Musawir narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the evening, he would say: We have entered the evening and the dominion belongs to Allah, the One, the Irresistible. Praise be to Allah who took away the day and brought the night, while we are in well-being from Him. O Allah, this is a new creation of Yours that has come; whatever evil I did in it, overlook it, and whatever good I did in it, accept it and multiply it many times over. O Allah, You know all my needs and You have power over all their fulfillment. O Allah, fulfill tonight every need of mine, do not increase me in my worldly life, and do not decrease me in my Hereafter. And when morning came he would say the like of that. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Abd al-A'la ibn Abi al-Musawir; Ismah ibn al-Mutawakkil was alone in transmitting it."
"7664","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Istakhri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sahl narrated to us, Ismah ibn al-Mutawakkil narrated to us, Mubarak ibn Fadalalah narrated to us, from Abu Harun, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Avoid this evil-smelling tree; whoever eats it, let him not come near our mosque. No one narrated this hadith from Mubarak ibn Fadalalah except Ismah ibn al-Mutawakkil."
"7665","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Istakhri narrated to us, Ismail ibn Yahya al-Istakhri narrated to us, al-Kirmani ibn Amr narrated to us, Mubarak ibn Fadalalah narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, Abu Nadrah narrated to me, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Two great factions will fight, their claim being one; while they are so, a renegade group will break away from them, and the faction closer to the truth will kill them."
"7666","Muhammad ibn Musa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sahl narrated to us, Ismah ibn al-Mutawakkil narrated to us, Mubarak ibn Fadalalah narrated to us, from Abu Ghalib, who said: I was in Syria where Abu Umamah Sudayy ibn Ajlan, the companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), was, and he was a friend of mine. Heads from the heads of the Haruriyyah were brought and cast at the steps. Abu Umamah came, entered the mosque, prayed two rak'ahs, then turned toward the heads. I said: I will follow him to hear what he says. I followed him until he stood over them and wept. Then he said: Glory be to Allah, what does Iblis do with this ummah? Then he said: Dogs of the Fire, dogs of the Fire, dogs of the Fire. Then he said: The worst slain killed under the shade of the sky, and the best slain are those they killed. Then he recited this verse: On the day when faces turn white and faces turn black; as for those whose faces turn black: Did you disbelieve after your faith? Then he turned to me and saw me - Abu Ghalib said: and he took my forearm - and said: Are you in a land where these are many? - meaning Iraq. I said: Yes. He said: May Allah protect you from being among them. I said: O Abu Umamah, what about your saying: Dogs of the Fire - did you say it by your own opinion or something you heard? He said: Glory be to Allah, then I would be bold indeed; no, I heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - not once, nor twice, nor three times, nor four, nor five, nor six, nor seven. No one narrated this hadith from Mubarak except Ismah ibn al-Mutawakkil."
"7667","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Istakhri narrated to us, Abu Usamah Abdillah ibn Usamah al-Kalbi narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Ishaq al-Attar narrated to us, Ammar ibn Sayf narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah revealed to an angel among the angels: Overturn such-and-such a city upon its people. He said: In it is Your servant so-and-so who has not disobeyed You for the blink of an eye. He said: Overturn it upon him and upon them, for his face never changed color for Me for a single hour. No one narrated this hadith from al-A'mash except Ammar ibn Sayf; Ubayd ibn Ishaq al-Attar was alone in transmitting it."
"7668","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Istakhri narrated to us, Abu Usamah Abdillah ibn Usamah al-Kalbi narrated to us, Ali ibn Thabit al-Dahhan narrated to us, Ya'qub al-Qummi narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Abi al-Mughirah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that forty of the companions of the Negus came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and were present with him at Uhud; they had wounds but none of them was killed. When they saw the need among the believers, they said: O Messenger of Allah, we are people of means; permit us to bring our wealth to console the Muslims with it. So Allah revealed concerning them: Those to whom We gave the Book before it believe in it - the verse - Those will be given their reward twice because they were patient. So He gave them two rewards. He said: And they repel evil with good. He said: That is the spending with which they consoled the Muslims, until this verse was revealed. He said: Then the People of the Book boasted over the Muslims until this verse was revealed, saying: O Muslims, whoever among us believes in your book has two rewards, and whoever does not believe in your book has a reward like your rewards. So Allah revealed: O you who believe, fear Allah and believe in His Messenger; He will give you two shares of His mercy and give you a light by which you walk. So He increased them in light and forgiveness. And He said: So that the People of the Book may know that they have no power over anything of Allah's bounty. No one narrated this hadith from Ja'far ibn Abi al-Mughirah except Ya'qub al-Qummi; Ali ibn Thabit was alone in transmitting it."
"7669","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Istakhri narrated to us, Ismail ibn Yahya ibn Ismail al-Istakhri narrated to us, Ismah ibn al-Mutawakkil narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah al-Darir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade on the day of Hunayn selling the fifth until it is divided, and bedding women until they deliver what is in their wombs, if they are pregnant. No one narrated this hadith from al-A'mash, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Sa'id, from Ibn Abbas - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade - except Abu Mu'awiyah; Ismah was alone in transmitting it."
"7670","Muhammad ibn Musa narrated to us, Ismail ibn Yahya narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Hammad narrated to us, from Ghawrak ibn al-Hisrimi Abu Abdillah al-Ju'fi, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The charity of breaking the fast is upon every person: two mudds of flour or wheat, a sa' of barley, and of sweets - raisins or dates - a sa', a sa'."
"7671","And with the same chain, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For pasturing horses, for every horse one dinar. No one narrated these two hadiths from Ja'far ibn Muhammad except Ghawrak al-Ju'fi; al-Layth ibn Hammad al-Istakhri was alone in transmitting them."
"7672","Muhammad ibn Musa narrated to us, Ismail ibn Yahya al-Azdi al-Istakhri narrated to us, al-Kirmani ibn Amr narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Abi Ja'far al-Farra narrated to me, from Abu Ja'far, the freedman of Ali, who said: I was present with Ali at the river; when he finished killing them, he said: Seek the deformed one. They sought him but did not find him. He ordered a reed to be placed on every slain man, and they found him in a hollow in a pool of water: a black man, foul-smelling, with something like a breast with hairs on it in place of his hand. When he looked at him he said: Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth. One of his two sons - meaning al-Hasan or al-Husayn - was heard saying: Praise be to Allah who relieved the ummah of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of this band. Ali said: If only three remained of the ummah of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), one of them would be upon the view of these; they are in the loins of men and the wombs of women. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ja'far, the freedman of Ali, except Abu Ja'far al-Farra, and none from Abu Ja'far except his son Abd al-Hamid; al-Kirmani ibn Amr - the brother of Mu'awiyah ibn Amr - was alone in transmitting it."
"7673","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Istakhri narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Ismail al-Talhi al-Kufi narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym al-Nakha'i narrated to us, Abu Malik al-Nakha'i narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: I was commanded to prostrate on seven bones. No one narrated this hadith from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Tawus, except Abu Malik. And Warqa narrated it from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr."
"7674","Muhammad ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Ismail al-Talhi narrated to us, Talq ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Abu Farwah, from Abdillah ibn Ukaym, who said: The letter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached us two months before he passed away: Do not benefit from carrion by skin or sinew. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Farwah except Qays, and none from Qays except Talq ibn Ghannam; Ibrahim ibn Ismail was alone in transmitting it."
"7675","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Istakhri narrated to us, Abu Usamah Abdillah ibn Usamah al-Kalbi narrated to us, Mudar ibn Ghassan ibn Mudar narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Abi Ja'far narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and I used to bathe from one vessel, both of us dipping into it together; I would do no more than pour three handfuls over my head. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Zubayr, from Abu al-Tufayl, except al-Hasan ibn Abi Ja'far; Mudar ibn Ghassan was alone in transmitting it. And Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, Hammad ibn Salamah, and Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated it from Abu al-Zubayr, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Aishah."
"7676","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Istakhri narrated to us, Abu Usamah Abdillah ibn Usamah al-Kalbi narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Mundhir al-Kahili, from Anbasah ibn Abi Sufyan, from his sister Umm Habibah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in a day and night, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq, from al-Mundhir, except Sharik; Yahya ibn al-Mundhir was alone in transmitting it. And al-Thawri and Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated it from Abu Ishaq, from al-Musayyib ibn Rafi'."
"7677","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Istakhri narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Kathir ibn Yahya ibn Abi Kathir al-Yamami narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulayman al-Sulami narrated to us, Uyaynah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Jawshan narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Bakrah, who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when the delegation of Banu Tamim came to him, among them Qays ibn Asim, Amr ibn al-Ahtam, and al-Zibriqan ibn Badr. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Amr ibn al-Ahtam: What do you say about al-Zibriqan ibn Badr? He said: O Messenger of Allah, obeyed in his councils, severe in opposition, defending what is behind his back. Al-Zibriqan said: O Messenger of Allah, he knows more about me than he described, but he envied me. Amr said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, he is lacking in manliness, small in courtyard, base in maternal uncle, foolish in father. By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I did not lie at first, and I told the truth at last; but I was pleased so I said the best I knew, and I became angry so I said the worst I knew. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Some eloquence is magic, and some poetry is wisdom. No one narrated this hadith from Uyaynah except Sa'id ibn Sulayman; al-Hasan ibn Kathir was alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Abu Bakrah except with this chain."
"7678","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Istakhri narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Kathir narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abdillah ibn Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from his father, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When two Muslims meet and shake hands and ask after one another, Allah sends down between them one hundred mercies: ninety-nine for the more cheerful, freer, kinder of them, and the one who asks after his brother best. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir except his son Abdillah, and none narrated it from Abdillah except Yahya ibn Misma'; al-Hasan ibn Kathir was alone in transmitting it."
"7679","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Istakhri narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Kathir narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Yamami narrated to us, Nasr ibn Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Four mountains are among the mountains of Paradise, and four rivers are among the rivers of Paradise. As for the mountains: al-Tur, Lubnan, Tur Sina, and Tur Zayta. And the rivers of Paradise: the Euphrates, the Nile, Sayhan, and Jayhan. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir except his son Nasr, and none narrated it from Nasr except Yahya ibn Abi Sa'id al-Yamami; al-Hasan ibn Kathir was alone in transmitting it."
"7680","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Istakhri narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Kathir narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Nasr ibn Yahya narrated to us, my father narrated to us, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The lowest of the people of Paradise in rank is one over whom ten thousand servants stand, in the hand of each of them two dishes, one of gold and the other of silver, in each a color unlike the other; he eats from the last of it as he eats from the first of it, finding in the last of it the same fragrance and delight he finds in the first of it; then that becomes like the scent of strong musk. They do not urinate, defecate, or blow their noses - brothers upon couches facing one another."
"7681","Muhammad ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Kathir narrated to us, Salma ibn Uqbah al-Hanafi al-Yamami narrated to us, Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: Ali ibn Abi Talib said: O Messenger of Allah, who is more beloved to you: I or Fatimah? He said: Fatimah is more beloved to me than you, and you are dearer to me than her. It is as if I see you at my Pool, driving people away from it, with jugs upon it as many as the stars of the sky. I, you, al-Hasan, al-Husayn, Fatimah, Aqil, and Ja'far will be in Paradise as brothers upon couches facing one another, and you with me and your partisans will be in Paradise. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: Brothers upon couches facing one another; none of them looks at the back of his companion's neck. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir except Ikrimah ibn Ammar, and none narrated it from Ikrimah except Salma ibn Uqbah; al-Hasan ibn Kathir was alone in transmitting it."
"7682","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Istakhri narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Kathir narrated to us, Nadrah bint Jahdam ibn Abdillah ibn Abi al-Tufayl al-Qaysiyyah narrated to me, from her father, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Aishah, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, the martyr is only one killed in the path of Allah. He said: O Aishah, then the martyrs of my ummah would be few. Whoever says twenty-five times in a day: O Allah, bless death and what is after death, then dies on his bed, Allah will give him the reward of a martyr."
"7683","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Istakhri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sahl ibn Makhlad al-Istakhri narrated to us, Ismah ibn al-Mutawakkil narrated to us, from Bahr al-Saqqa, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Marry virgins, for they have more fruitful wombs, sweeter mouths, less deceit, and are more content with little. No one narrated this hadith from Bahr except Ismah ibn al-Mutawakkil."
"7684","Muhammad ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Usamah Abdillah ibn Usamah al-Kalbi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Khuwar narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Marzuq narrated to us, from Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever recites ten verses will not be recorded among the heedless; whoever stands with one hundred verses will be recorded among the devout; and whoever stands with two hundred verses will be recorded among the worshippers. No one narrated this hadith from Fudayl ibn Marzuq except Hammad ibn Hammad ibn Khuwar - the brother of Humayd ibn Hammad."
"7685","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Istakhri narrated to us, Abu Usamah Abdillah ibn Usamah narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Bazzar narrated to us, Isa ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), concerning wiping over the leather socks, he said: Three days and nights for the traveler, and for the resident one day and night."
"7686","And with the same chain, from Anas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by two graves of Banu al-Najjar whose occupants were being punished for tale-bearing and urine. He took a palm frond and split it, placing a piece on this grave and a piece on this grave, and said: It will continue to be lightened for them so long as they remain moist."
"7687","And with the same chain, from Anas who said: Ibn Masud passed by and found Abu Jahl breathing his last. He came and sat on his chest. Abu Jahl raised his head and said: Are you not the little shepherd of yesterday in Makkah? You have climbed a difficult climb. Then he cut off his head and came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: This is the head of Abu Jahl. He said: By Allah? He said: By Allah, it is indeed his head. He said: Then he ordered it to be thrown into the well. No one narrated these hadiths from Isa ibn Tahman except Ubayd ibn Abd al-Rahman; Abu Usamah al-Kalbi is alone in transmitting them."
"7688","Muhammad ibn Musa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sahl narrated to us, Ismah ibn al-Mutawakkil narrated to us, Kharijah ibn Musab narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, Abu Rifaa narrated to us, that Abu Said al-Khudri said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, I have a slave girl and I practice withdrawal from her, wanting from her what men want, but I dislike that she become pregnant, and the Jews claim that withdrawal is the lesser burying alive. He said: The Jews have lied; if Allah intends to create it, no one can turn it away. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Said except Kharijah ibn Musab; Ismah ibn al-Mutawakkil is alone in transmitting it."
"7689","Muhammad ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn al-Abbas al-Istakhri narrated to us, al-Kirmani ibn Amr narrated to us, Mindal ibn Ali narrated to us, Layth ibn Abi Sulaym narrated to us, from Ata, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Between the servant and disbelief is abandoning prayer, and between the servant and polytheism is abandoning prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Layth, from Ata, except Mindal ibn Ali; al-Kirmani ibn Amr is alone in transmitting it."
"7690","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Istakhri narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Abbas al-Istakhri narrated to us, al-Kirmani ibn Amr narrated to us, Abu Kudaynah Yahya ibn al-Muhallab narrated to us, Abu Janab narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no contagion, no bad omen, and no Hamah. A Bedouin stood and said: A mangy camel slips into my camels and makes them mangy. He said: That is the decree; then who made the first one mangy? No one narrated this hadith from Abu Janab except Abu Kudaynah; al-Kirmani is alone in transmitting it."
"7691","Muhammad ibn Musa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sahl ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Ismah ibn al-Mutawakkil narrated to us, Abu Jafar al-Razi narrated to us, from Sad ibn Said, from Umar ibn Thabit, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts Ramadan and follows it with six days of Shawwal has fasted the whole year. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Jafar al-Razi except Ismah ibn al-Mutawakkil."
"7692","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Istakhri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sahl ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Ismah ibn al-Mutawakkil narrated to us, Abu Muti narrated to us, from Muslim ibn Khalid, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade carrying the Quran to the land of the enemy, fearing the enemy would seize it. No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn Dinar except Muslim ibn Khalid; Abu Muti, who is al-Hakam ibn Abdullah al-Balkhi, is alone in transmitting it."
"7693","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Walid ibn Aban al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Jufi narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj, from Ibn Shihab, that a son of al-Numan ibn Bashir narrated to him, from his father al-Numan ibn Bashir, that he attended Zayd ibn Kharijah when he spoke after he had died and been covered. The first thing he said was: Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I testify truly; Abu Bakr, weak in the eyes of people but strong in the affair of Allah, I testify truly; Umar ibn al-Khattab, the strong, the trustworthy, I testify truly. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Bukayr, nor from Bukayr except Amr ibn al-Harith; Ibn Wahb is alone in transmitting it."
"7694","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Yusuf ibn Abdullah ibn Salam narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to the Mirbad and saw Uthman leading a camel loaded with flour, ghee and honey. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Make it kneel. So he made it kneel, and he called for a pot and put in it some of the ghee, honey and flour, then ordered a fire lit beneath it until it was done and cooked, and said: Eat. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate from it. Then he said: This is something the people of Persia call khabis. This hadith is not narrated from Abdullah ibn Salam except with this chain; al-Walid ibn Muslim is alone in transmitting it."
"7695","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Nasr ibn Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Sulami al-Himsi narrated to us, my father Muhammad ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abi Qays al-Nasri narrated to us, who said: I saw Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr standing on his pulpit in Makkah delivering a sermon, saying: The believer eats with one intestine, while the disbeliever eats with seven intestines; this is how I heard your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7696","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Rawh al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Abd Rabbihi al-Tai narrated to us, Ibn Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Masud, from his father who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: May Allah have mercy on one who hears a hadith from us and conveys it as he heard it, for many a recipient retains it better than the hearer."
"7697","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Rawh narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Abd Rabbihi narrated to us, Ibn al-Simmak ibn Harb narrated to us, from his father, from Jadah ibn Hubayrah, from his grandmother Umm Hani bint Abi Talib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me on the day of the conquest of Makkah while I was fasting. He said: Drink. I said: I am fasting. He said: A fast of makeup? I said: No. He said: Then drink. So I drank. No one narrated these two hadiths from Ibn Simak ibn Harb, whose name is Said, except Abd al-Malik ibn Abd Rabbihi al-Tai."
"7698","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Rawh narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Samad al-Ansari narrated to us, Abu Sad al-Ashhali narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Alqamah, from Mulayh ibn Abdullah al-Khatmi, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who prostrates before the imam and rises before him, his forelock is but in the hand of a devil."
"7699","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Rawh narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Samad al-Ansari narrated to us, Abu Sad al-Ashhali narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to me, from Nuaym ibn Abdullah al-Mujmir, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The excellence of congregational prayer over the prayer of the lone individual is twenty-seven degrees. No one narrated these two hadiths from Muhammad ibn Ajlan except Abu Sad Muhammad ibn Sad al-Ashhali."
"7700","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Rawh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Hatim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Ismail ibn Rafi, from a freedman of Said ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan called Duwayd, from Umm Hani bint Abi Talib, that she said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I have grown old and weak, so guide me to a deed I can do while sitting. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you magnify Allah a hundred times, it will be better than a hundred garlanded accepted sacrificial camels; if you glorify Allah a hundred times, it will be better than a hundred necks you free; if you praise Allah a hundred times, it will be better for you than a hundred saddled bridled horses carrying in the path of Allah; and if you declare His oneness a hundred times, no deed will precede it and no sin will remain with it. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Ajlan except Hatim."
"7701","Muhammad ibn Dawud ibn Jabir al-Ahmasi al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Hatim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Bashir Abu Ismail, from Sayyar, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Ibn Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Before the Hour will appear usury, adultery, and wine. No one narrated this hadith from Bashir Abu Ismail except Hatim ibn Ismail."
"7702","Muhammad ibn Dawud narrated to us, Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn Anum, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Rafi and Hibban ibn Abi Jabalah and Bakr ibn Sawadah, from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Poetry is like speech; its good is like good speech and its ugly is like ugly speech. This hadith is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain; Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad is alone in transmitting it."
"7703","Muhammad ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim al-Tarjuman narrated to us, Salih al-Murri narrated to us, from Said al-Jurayri, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most beloved of you to me are the best of you in character, the gentle and accommodating, who befriend and are befriended; and the most hateful of you to Allah are those who spread tale-bearing, who divide loved ones, who seek hardship for the innocent. No one narrated this hadith from al-Jurayri except Salih al-Murri."
"7704","Muhammad ibn Dawud narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Umar al-Aqta al-Raqqi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aisha who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The black man, when hungry steals, and when full commits adultery; yet among them are two truthful traits: generosity and courage. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Hisham ibn Urwah, except Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi."
"7705","Muhammad ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Qays ibn al-Rabi, from Ibn Jurayj, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Ata, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he forbade writing upon the grave. No one narrated this hadith from Qays except Abd al-Rahim."
"7706","Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Ismail al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, Abu Ismail al-Muaddib narrated to us, from Yaqub ibn Ata, from his father, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever equips a warrior, or gives food to break the fast of a fasting person, or equips a pilgrim, will have the like of his reward, without decreasing anything from his reward."
"7707","Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Ismail narrated to us, Mansur narrated to us, Abu Ismail narrated to us, from Yaqub, from his father who said: Umar touched the Corner and kissed it and said: I know you are a stone that neither harms nor benefits; were it not that I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kissing you, I would not kiss you. No one narrated these two hadiths from Yaqub ibn Ata except Abu Ismail; Mansur is alone in transmitting them."
"7708","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman Abu al-Saib al-Makhzumi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abi Shaybah al-Rahawi narrated to us, Miskin ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Jabir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seated me in his lap, wiped my head, and said: O Allah, teach him wisdom. No one narrated this hadith from Jabir except Shayban; Miskin ibn Bukayr is alone in transmitting it."
"7709","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Said ibn Abd al-Rahman, the brother of Abu Hurrah, narrated to us, my father Abu Hurrah narrated to me, from Qays ibn Abbad who said: I prayed with Umar ibn al-Khattab, with the elders of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with him. A man came in front of the row looking at the faces of the people, until when he was opposite me he pushed me aside with a shove and stood in my place. When Umar gave the salutation he said: Did what I did to you displease you? I said: Yes. He said: We were commanded to keep to the first row, so I looked at the faces of the people and recognized no one but you. I said: Who is this? They said: Ubayy ibn Kab. No one narrated this hadith from Said, the brother of Abu Hurrah, except Zayd ibn al-Hubab."
"7710","And with the same chain: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Humayd, the freedman of Alqamah al-Makki, narrated to me, Ata narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that a group passed by Isa son of Maryam, peace be upon him, and he said: One of these will die today, if Allah wills. They went on then returned to him in the evening with bundles of firewood. He said: Put them down. He said to the one about whom he had said he would die today: Untie your firewood. He untied it, and there was a black snake in it. He said: What did you do today? He said: I did nothing. He said: Look what you did. He said: I did nothing, except that I had a piece of bread in my hand and a poor man passed by me and asked me, so I gave him some of it. He said: By it you were protected. No one narrated this hadith from Ata except Humayd, the freedman of Alqamah; Zayd ibn al-Hubab is alone in transmitting it."
"7711","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman Abu al-Saib narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn al-Mustam al-Harrani narrated to us, Isam ibn Sayf al-Harrani narrated to us, from Abu Jafar al-Razi, from Qatadah, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that anyone pray with his hand on his flank. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Abu Jafar al-Razi, nor from Abu Jafar except Isam ibn Sayf; Abd al-Hamid ibn al-Mustam is alone in transmitting it."
"7712","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman Abu al-Saib narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, and Bakr ibn Sawadah Abu Ubaydah al-Naji narrated to me, from al-Hasan, from al-Bara ibn Azib, that he greeted the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was urinating, and he did not return the greeting until he had finished. This hadith is not narrated from al-Bara except with this chain; Ibn al-Hubab is alone in transmitting it."
"7713","And with the same chain: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Sakan ibn Qatadah Abu Qatadah al-Hanzali narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abbad al-Hanzali narrated to us, that a delegation came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he asked them, and some of them lied to him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not for a generosity in you which Allah dislikes you for, I would have made an example of you as the leader of a delegation of a people. This hadith is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain; Zayd ibn al-Hubab is alone in transmitting it."
"7714","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn al-Mustam narrated to us, Makhlad ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, Abu Bakr al-Hudhali narrated to me, from al-Hasan, from Rafi ibn Yazid al-Thaqafi, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Satan loves redness, so beware of redness and every garment of fame. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Makhlad ibn Yazid."
"7715","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Sayf al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Attab al-Dallal narrated to us, Said ibn Abd al-Rahman, the brother of Abu Hurrah, narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Ishaq, from Anas ibn Malik, that he was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he and Abu Talhah, with Safiyyah riding behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). His camel stumbled with him, so Abu Talhah leapt forward and said: Are you hurt? He said: No, take care of the woman. I threw my garment over my face and cast it over her. When we were at al-Harrah, or we overlooked Madinah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Returning, repentant, worshipping, if Allah wills, praising our Lord. No one narrated this hadith from Said, the brother of Abu Hurrah, except Abu Attab al-Dallal."
"7716","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Ali ibn Ghazwan al-Harrani narrated to us, Abd al-Azim ibn Raghban al-Himsi narrated to us, Abu Mashar narrated to us, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, Friday is binding upon him, except a slave, a woman, or a child; and whoever contents himself with amusement or trade, Allah will be free of need of him, and Allah is Rich, Praiseworthy. No one narrated this hadith from Said al-Maqburi except Abu Mashar; Abd al-Azim ibn Habib is alone in transmitting it."
"7717","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman Abu al-Saib al-Makhzumi narrated to us, Ali ibn Ghazwan al-Harrani narrated to us, Abd al-Azim ibn Habib narrated to us, Abu Mashar narrated to us, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever humbles himself for his Muslim brother, Allah raises him; and whoever exalts himself above him, Allah lowers him. No one narrated this hadith from Said al-Maqburi except Abu Mashar; Abd al-Azim is alone in transmitting it."
"7718","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman Abu al-Saib narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Kathir al-Harrani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musa ibn Ayan narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Ishaq ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aisha, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We are not inherited from; what we leave is charity; the family of Muhammad only eat from this wealth."
"7719","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musa narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Ishaq ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, that Umar said: If I do not appoint a successor, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not appoint one; and if I appoint one, Abu Bakr appointed one. No one narrated these two hadiths from Ishaq ibn Rashid except Musa ibn Ayan; Muhammad ibn Musa is alone in transmitting them."
"7720","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Sayf Abu Dawud al-Harrani narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hani narrated to us, Said ibn Zayd narrated to us, Umar ibn Musab ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Aisha, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray witr with five, not sitting between them. No one narrated this hadith from Umar ibn Musab except Said ibn Zayd; Muadh ibn Hani is alone in transmitting it."
"7721","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Kathir narrated to us, Habib ibn Farrukh al-Hadathi narrated to us, from Mubarak ibn Fadalah, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until the hypocrites of every people rule them. No one narrated this hadith from Mubarak except Habib ibn Farrukh; Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Kathir is alone in transmitting it."
"7722","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Kathir al-Harrani narrated to us, Ali ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Mani narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Amr ibn Wahb, from al-Mughirah ibn Shubah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he intended to relieve himself, would go far. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Sirin except Jarir ibn Hazim; Ali ibn Abd al-Hamid is alone in transmitting it."
"7723","Muhammad ibn Isa ibn al-Sakan al-Wasiti narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abdullah ibn Zurarah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Balisi narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever says three times before the dawn prayer on Friday: I seek forgiveness from Allah, besides whom there is no god, and I repent to Him, his sins will be forgiven even if they are more than the foam of the sea. No one narrated this hadith from Khusayf except Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Rahman."
"7724","Muhammad ibn Isa ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, Abu Mamar al-Muqad narrated to us, Abd al-Warith ibn Said narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from Mansur, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from al-Rabi ibn Umaylah al-Fazari, from Samurah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most beloved speech to Allah is four: Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest; it does not harm you with which of them you begin. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Juhadah except Abd al-Warith."
"7725","Muhammad ibn Isa ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail al-Jabbuli narrated to us, Abd al-Ala ibn Abi al-Musawir narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah who said: We were forbidden to follow a shooting star with our eyes when it falls, and we were commanded to say at that time: What Allah wills; there is no power except with Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad except Abd al-Ala ibn Abi al-Musawir; Musa ibn Ismail al-Jabbuli is alone in transmitting it."
"7726","Muhammad ibn Isa ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail al-Minqari narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, my uncle Jarir ibn Zayd narrated to me, from Salim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah narrating from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): While a man was walking between two cloaks, admiring himself, Allah caused the earth to swallow him, and he will be sinking in it until the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from Salim except Jarir ibn Zayd; Jarir ibn Hazim is alone in transmitting it."
"7727","Muhammad ibn Isa ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aishah al-Taymi narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Abu Farwah Muslim ibn Salim narrated to us, who said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla say: I heard Umar say: Ali is our best judge, and Ubayy is our best reciter. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Farwah except Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad."
"7728","Muhammad ibn Isa ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Fudayk, from al-Dahhak ibn Uthman, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade anal intercourse with women. No one narrated this hadith from al-Dahhak ibn Uthman except Ibn Abi Fudayk; Ali ibn Bahr is alone in transmitting it."
"7729","Muhammad ibn Isa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: We stayed in Madinah two years before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us, establishing prayer and maintaining the mosques. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Zubayr except Ibn Abi Layla."
"7730","Muhammad ibn Isa narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Ali, that game meat was gifted to the Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in ihram, and he returned it. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Hammam."
"7731","Muhammad ibn Isa ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail al-Jabbuli narrated to us, Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Mujahid, from Abu al-Khalil, from Abu Qatadah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Prayer is disliked at midday, except on Friday, for Hell is not stoked. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Qatadah except Abu al-Khalil."
"7732","Muhammad ibn Isa ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail al-Jabbuli narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Kharijah ibn Musab, from Uthman ibn Sad al-Katib, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is nothing against any of you, when he gives a voluntary charity, to make it on behalf of his parents, so they get its reward without decreasing anything from his reward. No one narrated this hadith from Uthman ibn Sad except Kharijah ibn Musab."
"7733","Muhammad ibn Isa ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sinan narrated to us, Sulaym ibn Hayyan narrated to us, from Said ibn Mina, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over the Negus and said takbir over him four times. No one narrated this hadith from Said ibn Mina except Sulaym ibn Hayyan."
"7734","Muhammad ibn Isa narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Yahya ibn Waththab, from Masruq, from Abdullah, raising the hadith, who said: Evil does not expiate evil, but good expiates evil. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Husayn except Qays."
"7735","Muhammad ibn Isa narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Mansur narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivered a sermon and said in his sermon: The lawful is clear, the unlawful is clear, and between them are doubtful matters; whoever grazes around the sanctuary is likely to enter it. No one narrated this hadith from Simak except Israil."
"7736","Muhammad ibn Isa ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Mansur narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abu Humayd al-Saidi, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) employed a man of the Ansar called Ibn al-Lutbiyyah over charity. When he returned, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for him to audit him, and he said: This is for you and this was gifted to me. That reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We employ among you men over what Allah has entrusted to us, then when one of them returns he says: This is for you and this was gifted to me; would he not sit in the house of his father and mother and see what is gifted to him? Whoever works for us among you must bring us its little and its much, and let each of you beware of coming on the Day of Resurrection carrying on his neck a camel with its bellow, or a cow with its moo, or a sheep that bleats. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except al-Harith ibn Mansur."
"7737","Muhammad ibn Yaqub al-Khatib al-Ahwazi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami narrated to us, Abu Imran al-Harrani Yusuf ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ata, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, who is not the Ansari, was in a caravan of Khadijah, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was with him in that caravan. He said to him: O Muhammad, I see in you traits, and I testify that you are the Prophet who will emerge from Tihamah, and I have believed in you; when I hear of your emergence I will come to you. He stayed away from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until the day of the conquest of Makkah, then he came to him. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him he said: Welcome to the first emigrant. He said: O Messenger of Allah, nothing prevented me from being among the first to come to you, while I believed in you, not denying your pledge nor breaking your covenant, and I believed in the Quran and disbelieved in the idol, except that after you we were struck by successive severe years of drought that left the marrow congealed and the mounts wandering, the milk dried up, the fat vanished, the salt-bush withered and the thorny trees and acacia dried, the tamarisk parched; the lowland dried, all dry herbage was swept away and the roots of the brush destroyed, until the hardy shrubs were cut off. I have come to you neither breaking my covenant nor denying my pledge. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take note: Allah, blessed and exalted, stretches His hand at night for the wrongdoer of the day to repent; if he repents, Allah turns to him; and He stretches His hand in the day for the wrongdoer of the night to repent; if he repents, Allah turns to him. Truth is heavy, as heavy as it will be on the Day of Resurrection, and falsehood is light, as light as it will be on the Day of Resurrection; Paradise is hedged with hardships, and Hell is hedged with desires. He said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me about the light of day and the darkness of night, about the warmth of water in winter and its coldness in summer, about the Secure Town, about the origin of clouds, about the emergence of locusts, about thunder and lightning, and about what the child gets from the man and what from the woman. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for the darkness of night and the light of day: when the sun sets it falls beneath the earth, so the night darkens thereby; when dawn brightens, seventy thousand angels hasten to it while it holds back, averse to being worshipped besides Allah, until it rises and gives light. By the length of the night its stay is long, so water warms thereby; when it is summer its stay is short, so water cools thereby. As for locusts: they are the scattering of a whale in the sea called al-Iywan, and in it they perish. As for the origin of clouds: they arise from the direction of the two horizons, the Saba and the southerly winds weave them and the northerly and westerly winds warp them. As for thunder: it is an angel with a whip in his hand who brings the distant near and puts the near far; when he raises it, it flashes, when he rebukes, it thunders, and when he strikes, it thunderbolts. As for what the child gets from the man and from the woman: the man contributes bones, veins and sinews, and the woman contributes flesh, blood and hair. As for the Secure Town: it is Makkah. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Abu Imran al-Harrani; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami is alone in transmitting it."
"7738","Muhammad ibn Yaqub al-Khatib narrated to us, Isa ibn Abi Harb al-Saffar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr al-Kirmani narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, Budayl ibn Maysarah al-Uqayli narrated to me, from al-Hasan ibn Muslim, from Safiyyah bint Shaybah, from Umm Uthman, from Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The woman whose husband has died must not wear dyed garments of usfur or mashq, nor jewelry, nor dye her hands, nor apply kohl. No one narrated this hadith from Budayl al-Uqayli except Ibrahim ibn Tahman."
"7739","Muhammad ibn Yaqub al-Khatib narrated to us, Isa ibn Abi Harb narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr al-Kirmani narrated to us, Umar ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, Zakariyya and Abdullah ibn Abi al-Safar narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe, and the emigrant is one who abandons what Allah has forbidden. No one narrated this hadith from Umar ibn Abi Zaidah except Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr."
"7740","Muhammad ibn Yaqub al-Khatib narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ishaq Abu Yusuf al-Qulusi narrated to us, al-Salt ibn Muhammad Abu Hammam al-Kharaki narrated to us, Mansur ibn Sad narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, from Aisha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah cursed a people who took the graves of their prophets as mosques. No one narrated this hadith from Uthman ibn Urwah except Mansur ibn Sad; Abu Hammam al-Kharaki is alone in transmitting it."
"7741","Muhammad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Mualla ibn Rashid al-Ammi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Thabit al-Bunani and Thumamah narrated to me, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died and none had compiled the Quran but four: Abu al-Darda, Muadh, Abu Zayd, and Zayd ibn Thabit. No one narrated this hadith from Thumamah except Abdullah ibn al-Muthanna, nor from Abdullah except Mualla ibn Rashid; Abu Yusuf is alone in transmitting it."
"7742","Muhammad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ishaq narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Anbasah al-Warraq narrated to us, Ali ibn Ghurab narrated to us, Umar ibn Abdullah ibn Yala ibn Murrah narrated to us, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever among you prays on Friday, let him pray four. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Ahwas except Umar ibn Abdullah, nor from Umar except Ali ibn Ghurab, nor from Ali except al-Hasan; Abu Yusuf is alone in transmitting it."
"7743","Muhammad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ali ibn Humayd al-Dahaki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ismail, the son-in-law of Abu al-Mualla al-Attar, narrated to us, from Abu al-Mualla, whose name is Yahya ibn Maymun, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Teach me, or guide me, to a deed that admits me to Paradise. He said: Be a caller to prayer. He said: I cannot. He said: Be an imam. He said: I cannot. He said: Then stand beside the imam. No one narrated this hadith from Said ibn Jubayr except Abu al-Mualla, nor from Abu al-Mualla except Muhammad ibn Ismail; Ali ibn Humayd is alone in transmitting it."
"7744","Muhammad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ali ibn Humayd narrated to us, Umar ibn Farqad al-Bazzar narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Mukhtar, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara ibn Azib who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says after every prayer: I seek forgiveness from Allah, besides whom there is no god, the Living, the Sustainer, and I repent to Him, will be forgiven, even if he fled from the battle line. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Abdullah ibn al-Mukhtar, nor from Abdullah ibn al-Mukhtar except Umar ibn Farqad, nor from Umar ibn Farqad except Ali ibn Humayd; Yaqub ibn Ishaq is alone in transmitting it."
"7745","And with the same chain: Umar ibn Farqad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Wasi, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr who said: My beloved Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined upon me seven things: love of the poor and closeness to them; to join kinship even if it turns away; to say: There is no power nor strength except with Allah, for it is among the treasures of Paradise; he enjoined me not to fear in Allah the blame of any blamer; he enjoined me to speak the truth even if bitter; he enjoined me to look to one below me and not to look to one above me; and he enjoined me not to take anything from people. No one narrated this hadith from Umar ibn Farqad except Ali ibn Humayd al-Dahaki; Yaqub al-Hadrami is alone in transmitting it."
"7746","Muhammad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us, Abu Umayyah ibn Yala narrated to us, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Prostration is upon seven limbs. No one narrated this hadith from Said al-Maqburi except Abu Umayyah ibn Yala; Hajjaj ibn Nusayr is alone in transmitting it."
"7747","Muhammad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya ibn Rashid narrated to us, Abd al-Nur ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Sinan al-Qaysi, from Harun ibn Sad, from Thumamah ibn Uqbah, from Zayd ibn Arqam who said: While we were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a Jewish man called Thalabah ibn al-Harith came and said: Death to you, O Muhammad. He said: And upon you. The Jew said to him: You claim that in Paradise there is food, drink and spouses. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes; do you believe in the tree of musk? He said: Yes. He said: And do you find it in your book? He said: Yes. He said: Urine and impurity become sweat flowing from beneath their forelocks to their feet as musk. No one narrated this hadith from Harun ibn Sad except Abdullah ibn Sinan; Abd al-Nur ibn Abdullah is alone in transmitting it."
"7748","Muhammad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Abu al-Ashath Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, Ubayd ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aisha, that Amrah bint al-Jawn sought refuge from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when she was brought to him, so he said: You have sought refuge with the Refuge, and he divorced her, and he ordered Usamah to provide for her with three garments. No one narrated this hadith, connected, from Hisham ibn Urwah except Ubayd ibn al-Qasim."
"7749","Muhammad ibn Yaqub al-Khatib narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ansari narrated to us, Kahmas ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah, from his father who said: I saw henna dye on the temples of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Kahmas except al-Ansari; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami is alone in transmitting it."
"7750","Muhammad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami narrated to us, Musa ibn Said ibn Salm al-Bahili narrated to us, my father Said ibn Salm narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Said ibn al-Musayyib who said: Uthman ibn Affan had a chamberlain who would go out before him to prayer. He said: One day he went out and prayed with the chamberlain before him, then he came and the chamberlain sat aside, wrapped his cloak, placed it under his head, lay down, and placed the staff before him. Ali came in a waist-wrapper and cloak with a stick in his hand. When the chamberlain saw him from afar he said: This is Ali coming. Uthman sat up and took his cloak over himself. He came and stood over his head and said: You bought the estate of so-and-so, and the endowment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has a share in its water; I know none but you would buy it. Uthman stood, and words passed between them which I will not repeat until I meet Allah. Abbas came and intervened between them; Uthman raised the staff at Ali, and Ali raised the stick at Uthman. Abbas kept calming them, saying to Ali: The Commander of the Faithful, and saying to Uthman: Your cousin. He kept on until they calmed. In the evening of the next day I saw them, each holding the hand of his companion, conversing. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Awn except Said ibn Salm, nor from Said except his son; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami is alone in transmitting it."
"7751","Muhammad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ansari narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah who said: I never saw anyone whose prayer more resembled the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than Ibn Umm Sulaym, meaning Anas ibn Malik. None of those who narrated this hadith from Shubah, from Thabit and Abu Hurayrah, included Abu Rafi except Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ansari; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami is alone in transmitting it."
"7752","Muhammad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Hafs ibn Amr al-Rabbali narrated to us, Yahya ibn Maymun al-Qurashi narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me a supplication by which I may attain good. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Say: O Allah, pardon me, for You are Pardoning, Generous. No one narrated this hadith from Ali ibn Zayd except Yahya ibn Maymun."
"7753","Muhammad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Abdah ibn Abdullah al-Saffar narrated to us, Jafar ibn Awn narrated to us, Umar ibn Rashid narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you send a messenger, send one handsome of face and handsome of name. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir except Umar ibn Rashid."
"7754","Muhammad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Abdah ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Hammam al-Dallal narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from al-Marur ibn Suwayd, from Abu Dharr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, blessed and exalted, says: Son of Adam, if you did sins filling the earth, so long as you associate nothing with Me, I will grant you forgiveness filling the earth. None perfected the chain of this hadith from Mansur except Ibrahim ibn Tahman and Kharijah ibn Musab."
"7755","Muhammad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Yahya Abu al-Khattab narrated to us, Sahl ibn Hammad Abu Attab al-Dallal narrated to us, Jarir ibn Ayyub al-Bajali narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Ishaq, from Masruq, from Aisha, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No servant wakes fasting but the gates of heaven are opened for him, his limbs glorify, and the inhabitants of the lowest heaven seek forgiveness for him until he is veiled; if he prays one or two voluntary rakahs, the heavens shine light for him, and his wives among the wide-eyed maidens say: O Allah, take him to us, for we long to see him; and if he declares oneness, glorifies, or magnifies Allah, seventy thousand angels receive it, writing it until he is veiled. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, none narrated it from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman except Jarir ibn Ayyub, and none from Jarir except Abu Attab; Ziyad ibn Yahya is alone in transmitting it."
"7756","Muhammad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Abu al-Khattab Ziyad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aisha, who said: I used to come to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in retreat in the mosque, while I was menstruating, and he would extend his head to me from the mosque, and I would comb it and oil it while I was menstruating. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Hassan except Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi."
"7757","Muhammad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Said and Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Madan ibn Abi Talhah, from Thawban who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever the soul leaves the body while he is free of three enters Paradise: pride, misappropriation of spoils, and debt. No one narrated this hadith from Rawh ibn al-Qasim except Yazid ibn Zuray; Ziyad ibn Yahya is alone in transmitting it."
"7758","Muhammad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Imran ibn Abi Anas, from Sulayman ibn Yasar and Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, that they both narrated to him, from Aisha, who said: Safiyyah bint Huyayy menstruated while she was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); she had already performed the farewell circumambulation before that. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) departed from Mina, he was told: Safiyyah has menstruated. He said: She may detain us. They said: O Messenger of Allah, she already performed the circumambulation? He said: Then let her depart. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) departed with her while she was in her bleeding. No one narrated this hadith from Sulayman ibn Yasar except Imran ibn Abi Anas, nor from Imran except Muhammad ibn Ishaq; Abd al-Ala is alone in transmitting it."
"7759","Muhammad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Ishaq ibn al-Dayf narrated to us, Mansur ibn Abi Nuwayrah narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of greed, for it is present poverty, and beware of what requires apology. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir except Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd, nor from Muhammad except Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash; Mansur ibn Abi Nuwayrah is alone in transmitting it."
"7760","Muhammad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Ishaq ibn al-Dayf narrated to us, Mansur ibn Abi Nuwayrah narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No nation differed after its prophet but the people of its falsehood prevailed over the people of its truth. No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn Dinar except Musa ibn Ubaydah, nor from Musa except Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash; Mansur ibn Abi Nuwayrah is alone in transmitting it."
"7761","Muhammad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Abu al-Ashath Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, Yusuf ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, al-Muarik ibn Abbad narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi al-Fadl, from Abu al-Jawza, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever leads a people in prayer, let him fear Allah and know that he is a guarantor, responsible as he guarantees; if he does well, he will have reward like the reward of those who prayed behind him, without decreasing anything from their rewards; and whatever shortcoming occurs is upon him. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Jawza except Yahya ibn Abi al-Fadl, none narrated it from Yahya except al-Muarik; Yusuf ibn al-Hajjaj is alone in transmitting it."
"7762","And with the same chain: al-Muarik narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi, from his grandfather, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Part of the perfection of a servant's faith is to say, if Allah wills, in every statement. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Hurayrah except with this chain; al-Muarik ibn Abbad is alone in transmitting it."
"7763","Muhammad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Hafs ibn Amr al-Rabbali narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Umar al-Waqidi narrated to us, Abd al-Hakim ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Farwah narrated to us, who said: I heard Awf ibn al-Harith ibn al-Tufayl say: I heard Aisha say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the sky produces seaborne clouds then veers, it is a copious spring. No one narrated this hadith from Awf ibn al-Harith except Abd al-Hakim; al-Waqidi is alone in transmitting it."
"7764","Muhammad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Hafs ibn Amr al-Rabbali narrated to us, al-Mundhir ibn Ziyad al-Tai narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined upon us the charity of Ramadan: a sa of barley or a sa of dates. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Dinar except al-Mundhir ibn Ziyad."
"7765","Muhammad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Hafs ibn Amr narrated to us, al-Mundhir ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when travel pressed him, would combine Maghrib and Isha. No one narrated this hadith from Thabit except al-Mundhir ibn Ziyad."
"7766","Muhammad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami narrated to us, Abu Ubaydah Mamar ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, my brother Yazid ibn al-Muthanna narrated to me, Labatah ibn al-Farazdaq narrated to me, from his father who said: Abu Hurayrah said to me: O Farazdaq, I see you are small-footed; if you can secure for them a place at the Pond, do so, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: My Pond is between Oman and Aylah; its water is whiter than milk and sweeter than honey, its vessels as numerous as the stars of the sky; whoever drinks a draught from it will never thirst again. No one narrated this hadith from Labatah ibn al-Farazdaq except Yazid ibn al-Muthanna, none narrated it from Yazid except his brother Abu Ubaydah."
"7767","Muhammad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Abu al-Ashath narrated to us, Asram ibn Hawshab narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Wasil narrated to us, from Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ali who said: We said to Abdullah ibn Jafar: Narrate to us what you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and saw of him, and do not narrate to us from anyone besides you, even if trustworthy. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: What is between the navel and the knee is nakedness. And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Charity extinguishes the anger of the Lord. And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The worst of my nation are a people born in luxury and raised in it, eating varieties of food, speaking affectedly. And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: O Banu Hashim, I have asked Allah for you to make you noble and merciful, and I asked Him to guide your straying, secure your fearful, and satiate your hungry. And I saw in the right hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a cucumber and in his left fresh dates, eating from this once and from that once. And a sheep and loaves were gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he ate and they ate, and I heard him say: Take the meat of the back, for it is among its best. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the two rakahs before dawn and the two after Maghrib: Say, O disbelievers, and Say, He is Allah, One. And the dowry of Fatimah was coats of iron. And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when al-Abbas came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I came upon a people talking, and when they saw me they fell silent, and that is only because they hate us. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Have they indeed done so? By Him in whose hand is my soul, none of them believes until he loves you. Do they hope to enter Paradise by my intercession while the sons of Abd al-Muttalib do not hope for it? This hadith is not narrated from Abdullah ibn Jafar except with this chain; Abu al-Ashath is alone in transmitting it."
"7768","Muhammad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Abu al-Ashath narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Khirash narrated to us, from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Samurah ibn Jundub who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Begging is not lawful for a rich man, except from a relative or an authority. No one narrated this hadith from Samurah except Shahr ibn Hawshab, nor from Shahr except al-Awwam; Abdullah ibn Khirash is alone in transmitting it."
"7769","Muhammad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Abu al-Ashath narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Khirash narrated to us, from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever seizes the wealth of a Muslim man by a binding oath will meet Allah while He is angry with him. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim al-Taymi except al-Awwam; Abdullah ibn Khirash is alone in transmitting it."
"7770","Muhammad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Hafs ibn Amr al-Rabbali narrated to us, Bishr ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn Hassan narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you reaches the row and it is complete, let him pull a man to him and set him beside him. This hadith is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain; Bishr ibn Ibrahim is alone in transmitting it."
"7771","Muhammad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Hafs ibn Amr al-Rabbali narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Razi narrated to us, Abu Hurrah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs ablution on Friday, that suffices and is good; and whoever bathes, bathing is better. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Hurrah except Hafs ibn Umar, the imam, the carpenter, al-Razi."
"7772","Muhammad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Qulusi narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Hilw ibn al-Sari al-Awdi narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let me not find any of you placing one leg upon the other, then singing, while neglecting to recite Surat al-Baqarah. No one narrated this hadith from Hilw ibn al-Sari except al-Harith ibn Muhammad; Yaqub ibn Ishaq is alone in transmitting it."
"7773","Muhammad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ishaq narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Anbasah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Kufi narrated to us, from Abu al-Ala al-Khaffaf, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Habbah al-Urani, from Ali who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when asked something and intending to do it, would say: Yes; and when intending not to do it, would remain silent; and he would never say No to anything. A Bedouin came to him and asked him, and he was silent; he asked again and he was silent; he asked a third time, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him as if rebuking: Ask whatever you wish, O Bedouin. We envied him and said: Now he will ask for Paradise. The Bedouin said: I ask you for a mount. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: That is yours. Then he said: Ask. He said: I ask you for provisions. He said: And that is yours. He said: We marveled at that, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How great is the difference between the asking of the Bedouin and the old woman of the Children of Israel. Then he said: When Musa was commanded to cross the sea and reached it, the faces of the mounts were turned back and they returned. Musa said: What is wrong with me, my Lord? He said to him: You are at the grave of Yusuf; carry his bones with you. The grave had become level with the ground, and Musa did not know where it was. They said: If any of you knows where it is, the old woman of the Children of Israel may know where it is. Musa, peace be upon him, sent for her and said: Do you know where the grave of Yusuf, peace be upon him, is? She said: Yes. He said: Then guide me to it. She said: No, by Allah, until you grant me what I ask you. He said: That is yours. She said: I ask you that I be with you in the station you will be in Paradise. He said: Ask for Paradise. She said: No, by Allah, but that I be with you. Musa kept bargaining with her, so Allah, blessed and exalted, revealed to him: Grant her that, for it diminishes you nothing. So he granted her, and she guided him to the grave; he took out the bones and crossed the sea. This hadith is not narrated from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, except with this chain; Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Qulusi is alone in transmitting it."
"7774","Muhammad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Hafs ibn Amr al-Rabbali narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Umar al-Waqidi narrated to us, Kathir ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abdullah ibn Suraqah al-Adawi, from Urwah, from Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever seizes the right of a man by an oath he swears upon my pulpit wrongfully, let him take his seat in Hell. No one narrated this hadith from Urwah except Umar ibn Abdullah, none narrated it from Umar except Kathir ibn Zayd; Muhammad ibn Umar al-Waqidi is alone in transmitting it."
"7775","Muhammad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Hafs ibn Amr al-Rabbali narrated to us, Bahz ibn Asad narrated to us, Yazid ibn Ibrahim al-Tustari narrated to us, al-Hasan narrated to us, who said: Samurah ibn Jundub said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never stood among us but commanded us to give charity and forbade us mutilation. No one narrated this hadith from Yazid ibn Ibrahim except Bahz ibn Asad; al-Rabbali is alone in transmitting it."
"7776","Muhammad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Hafs ibn Amr al-Rabbali narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Habib ibn Nadabah narrated to us, Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with food before him, and he said: Come near, eat, mention Allah, eat with your right hand, and eat from what is near you. No one narrated this hadith from Rawh ibn al-Qasim except al-Hasan ibn Habib."
"7777","Muhammad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Hafs ibn Amr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Hasirah narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Kathir ibn Namir who said: I entered the mosque of Kufah on a Friday evening while Ali was addressing the people. They stood from the corners of the mosque declaring arbitration, so he gestured with his hand thus, then said: A word of truth intended for falsehood; I await Allah's judgment among you: to judge among you by the Book of Allah and the practice of His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), to divide among you equally; your presence in this mosque to pray in it is not prevented so long as your hands are with our hands, and we will not fight you until you fight us. No one narrated this hadith from al-Harith ibn Hasirah except Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Kufi."
"7778","Muhammad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Isa ibn Abi Harb al-Saffar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Umar ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever embraces Islam, there is no jizyah upon him. No one narrated this hadith from Muharib ibn Dithar except Umar ibn Yazid, nor from Umar except Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr; Isa ibn Abi Harb is alone in transmitting it."
"7779","Muhammad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Isa ibn Abi Harb narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Husayn and Sulayman, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The severest of people in punishment are the image-makers. No one narrated this hadith from Shubah, from Husayn, except Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr."
"7780","Muhammad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Hafs ibn Amr al-Rabbali narrated to us, Yahya ibn Maymun narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abdullah al-Ansari who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was standing praying, and a sheep went to pass before him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shooed it until he pressed it against the wall, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nothing cuts off prayer; repel as much as you can. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir except Jarir ibn Hazim; Yahya ibn Maymun is alone in transmitting it."
"7781","Muhammad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Qulusi narrated to us, Ali ibn Isa al-Hudhali narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abdullah al-Qurashi narrated to us, Jawnah, the freedwoman of Abu al-Tufayl, narrated to us, who said: I heard Abu al-Tufayl narrating from Abu al-Darda who said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, the affairs of Mina are wondrous; it is narrow, yet when people settle in it, it widens. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of Mina is like the womb; it is narrow, but when it carries, Allah widens it. This hadith is not narrated from Abu al-Darda except with this chain; Yaqub ibn Ishaq is alone in transmitting it."
"7782","Muhammad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Isa ibn Abi Harb al-Saffar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Abu Uthman, from Usamah ibn Zayd who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not return after me as disbelievers, striking the necks of one another. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr; Isa ibn Abi Harb is alone in transmitting it."
"7783","Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Sam al-Qadi narrated to us, Abu Mamar al-Qatii narrated to us, Abu Ismail al-Muaddib and Isa ibn Yunus, both, narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have a Pond, and I will precede you to it. No one narrated this hadith from al-Shabi except Mujalid, nor from Mujalid except Abu Ismail and Isa ibn Yunus; Abu Mamar is alone in transmitting it."
"7784","Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Sam narrated to us, al-Zubayr ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, a man of Banu Qushayr called Bahz ibn Hakim narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For every five pasturing camels there is charity. No one narrated this hadith from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, except Abd al-Majid; al-Zubayr is alone in transmitting it. Abd al-Razzaq narrated it from Mamar, from Bahz."
"7785","Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Sam narrated to us, Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Zayd ibn Umar ibn Asim narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: No one ever raises the voice in talbiyah but is given glad tidings, and no one ever magnifies Allah but is given glad tidings. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, of Paradise? He said: Yes. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Umar ibn Asim except Mutamir."
"7786","Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Sam narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, al-Muttalib ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from Abd Khayr, from Ali, concerning His saying: You are only a warner, and for every people a guide, who said: The Messenger of Allah is the warner, and the guide is a man of Banu Hashim. No one narrated this hadith from al-Suddi except al-Muttalib ibn Ziyad; Uthman is alone in transmitting it."
"7787","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to us, Thabit Abu Hamzah narrated to us, Kathir al-Nawwa narrated to us, from Rifaa al-Fityani who said: I entered upon al-Mukhtar, and when I wanted to leave he said: O Abu Umar, will you not help us against this chair, for Jibril just rose from it? I said: Yes, I will help you by burning it and scattering it in the sea. Rifaa said: I reached for the hilt of my sword and said to myself: Shall I not kill this liar, until I remembered the word of my brother Amr ibn al-Hamiq that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever a man trusts with his life and he kills him, I am free of the killer, even if the killed is a disbeliever. No one narrated this hadith from Kathir al-Nawwa except Thabit Abu Hamzah; Zahmawayh is alone in transmitting it."
"7788","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Isa al-Tai narrated to us, Rahmah ibn Musab al-Bahili narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Said al-Katib, from Anas ibn Malik who said: We used to sit with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as if birds were upon our heads; none of us spoke except Abu Bakr and Umar. No one narrated this hadith from Uthman ibn Said except Rahmah ibn Musab; al-Qasim ibn Isa is alone in transmitting it."
"7789","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Khallad al-Bahili narrated to us, Azhar ibn Sad narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: We were commanded to undo our provision bags after three, meaning the sacrifices. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Awn except Azhar; Abu Bakr ibn Khallad is alone in transmitting it."
"7790","Mahmud narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Isa al-Tai narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Thabit narrated to us, Nafi narrated to us, who said: I set out with Ibn Umar on an errand to Ibn Abbas, and Ibn Umar fulfilled his errand with Ibn Abbas. His narration that day was that he said: A man passed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a lane, having just come from urine and stool, and greeted him, but he did not return the greeting. When the man was about to disappear into the lane, he struck his hand upon the wall and wiped his face, then struck another blow with his hand upon the wall and wiped his forearms, then returned the greeting to the man. He said: Nothing prevented me from returning your greeting except that I was not in a state of purity. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), mentioning tayammum, except Nafi."
"7791","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us: Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to us, Salih ibn Umar narrated to us, from Mutarrif ibn Tarif, from Atiyyah, from Abu Said al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the sons of al-Hakam reach thirty, they will make the religion of Allah a deceit, the servants of Allah chattels, and the wealth of Allah something passed around. No one narrated this hadith from Mutarrif except Salih ibn Umar; Zahmawayh is alone in transmitting it."
"7792","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us: Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to us, Salih ibn Umar narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Hashimi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The oath in trade is a seller but an eraser of profit. No one narrated this hadith from Dawud ibn Abi Hind except Salih ibn Umar; Zahmawayh is alone in transmitting it."
"7793","Mahmud ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: An Ansari man came hurrying on his camel; when the Maghrib prayer was established he came to the mosque and found Muadh ibn Jabal leading them, and he opened with Surat al-Baqarah or Al Imran. When the man saw that, he withdrew, prayed aside, then joined his camel. The people of Madinah said: So-and-so has become a hypocrite. When the man heard that, he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Muadh and said: Are you a trial? Why did you not recite By the sun and its brightness, and Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High? No one narrated this hadith from al-Shaybani except Khalid."
"7794","Mahmud ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from Awn ibn Abdullah, from his brother Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, who said: Abu Hurayrah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: In Friday there is an hour in which no servant asks Allah for anything at all but Allah grants it to him. No one narrated this hadith from al-Shaybani except Khalid."
"7795","Mahmud ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to us, Sinan ibn Harun narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Shaybani who said: I said to Ibn Umar: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, some people command us to ascend the pulpits and speak; when we descend, by Allah, for one of us to fall from the sky is dearer to him than to persist in any of it. He said: This in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was hypocrisy. No one narrated this hadith from Mujalid except Sinan ibn Harun; Zahmawayh is alone in transmitting it."
"7796","Mahmud ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Zakariyya narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Amir ibn Shaqiq, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Abdullah who said: I watched the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he did not stop the talbiyah until he stoned the Aqabah pillar. No one narrated this hadith from Amir ibn Shaqiq except Sharik; Zahmawayh is alone in transmitting it."
"7797","Mahmud ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Zakariyya narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Talhah Abu Muhammad, the freedman of Bahilah, Qatadah narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Amr ibn Kharijah al-Ashari who said: I attended with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) his pilgrimage, while I was between the front of the Messenger of Allah's she-camel (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she chewing her cud with her saliva flowing between my shoulders. I heard him say: Allah has given every rightful one his right; no bequest for an heir; the child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone. No one narrated this hadith from Talhah ibn Abd al-Rahman except Hushaym."
"7798","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Abu Musab Ahmad ibn Abi Bakr al-Zuhri narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Imran narrated to us, from the nephew of Ibn Shihab, from his uncle, from Salim, from his father who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more than forty mornings during the expedition of Tabuk reciting in the two rakahs before dawn: Say, O disbelievers, and Say, He is Allah, One. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except his nephew, nor from the nephew of al-Zuhri except Abd al-Aziz ibn Imran; Abu Musab is alone in transmitting it."
"7799","Mahmud ibn Muhammad narrated to us, al-Salt ibn Masud al-Jahdari narrated to us, Abu Sayfi narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Hammam narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: It is of the practice that when a man invites his brother, he should stand with him until he leaves. No one narrated this hadith from Ikrimah except Ubayd ibn Hammam, nor from Ubayd except Abu Sayfi; al-Salt is alone in transmitting it."
"7800","Mahmud ibn Muhammad narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Said ibn al-Musayyib ibn Sharik narrated to us, Shuja ibn al-Walid narrated to us, who said: I heard Abd al-Malik ibn Abjar who said: I heard Zirr ibn Hubaysh who said: Ubayy ibn Kab used to swear by Allah that the Night of Decree is the night of the twenty-seventh, without exception. He said: We said to him: From where did you know that? He said: By the sign the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed us of; we counted and memorized that it is the night of the twenty-seventh. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Abjar except Shuja ibn Walid; al-Qasim ibn Said is alone in transmitting it."
